E["item:ados-fragment"] = {t="item",n="Ados Fragment",z="wetlands",s="At Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands, Ados Fragment lies among three lost pieces of the Goaz Stone. Together, the four shards make an ancient relic carved with Titan inscriptions.",h="At Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands, Ados Fragment lies among three lost pieces of the Goaz Stone.",sec={{t="A Piece of the Goaz Stone",b="The Ados Fragment is one of four pieces Prospector Whelgar needs to restore the Goaz Stone at Whelgar's Excavation. Before raptors overran the dig site, Whelgar began translating the main tablet and found its inscriptions broke off at crucial moments. The four pieces, named Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru, were lost across the ruins in ancient containers and dirt mounds, among prowling beasts.",sp=0},{t="The Titan Script",b="Prospector Whelgar can read the full Titan script carved into the Goaz Stone once he joins Ados Fragment with the other three pieces. The completed text speaks of a grand divine plan and a doomed prophecy, then declares, “Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.” It reveals that the Titans imprisoned primordial entities beneath Azeroth in ages past.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Ados Fragment?",a="Ados Fragment is one broken piece of the ancient Goaz Stone, found at Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands. Its carved script comes from the world-shaping Titans.",al={"ados fragment","what is ados","goaz stone fragment ados"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the fragment found?",a="The fragment lies across Whelgar's Excavation, east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. It is usually inside ancient relics or loose soil patches, with territorial raptors nearby.",al={"where is ados fragment","ados location","how to find ados"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the fragment say?",a="Ados Fragment's inscription is incomplete on its own. Prospector Whelgar needs the Modr, Golm, and Neru fragments to continue translating the tablet.",al={"ados fragment text","what is written on ados","goaz stone translation"},sp=1},{q="Who wants this fragment?",a="Prospector Whelgar seeks Ados Fragment to finish translating the Goaz Stone. He is an Explorer's League dwarf overseeing the ruined excavation site.",al={"who needs ados fragment","ados fragment turn in","whelgar ados"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Ados Fragment come from, and who made it?",a="The Ados Fragment is a broken piece of the Goaz Stone, an ancient relic uncovered at the dig site in the Wetlands. It was inscribed by the Titans, bearing their mysterious script, before it shattered into four separate pieces amidst the ruins.",al={"ados fragment origin","who made ados fragment","where is ados fragment from"},it="origin",add="f3ac27ac"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Explorer's League seeks Titan relics like Ados Fragment to uncover the origins of your people and their ancient makers."},kw={"ados fragment","excavation","goaz stone","old gods","relic","titans","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:299","npc:prospector-whelgar","item:modr-fragment","item:golm-fragment","item:neru-fragment","topic:titan","topic:old-god","zone:wetlands"},src={"Ados Fragment","Uncovering the Past"}}
E["item:bundle-of-crocolisk-skins"] = {t="item",n="Bundle of Crocolisk Skins",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, hunters prepare crocolisk skins for Menethil Harbor. The hides are valuable trade goods for local leatherworkers.",h="In the Wetlands, hunters prepare crocolisk skins for Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="Wetlands Commerce and Domestic Strife",b="Crocolisk hides are an essential trade good for coastal Menethil Harbor. Hunters gather and cure the tough, water-resistant skins in the Wetlands before sending them west to artisans such as James Halloran. Einar has gathered this bundle, but asks a traveler to carry it into town. He wants to avoid returning home to face the temper of his frustrated wife, Sida.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Bundle of Crocolisk Skins used for?",a="The bundle holds raw and cured marsh hides for James Halloran, a tanner in Menethil Harbor. He turns the skins into sturdy boots, belts, and leather armor suited to the Wetlands’ damp, flooded ground.",al={"crocolisk skins use","what are these skins for","bundle of skins purpose"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who gathered these crocolisk skins?",a="Hunter Einar gathered and bundled the skins in the marshes. He usually brings his trade goods into town himself, but asks passing travelers to carry this bundle so he can avoid an argument with his wife, Sida.",al={"who made the bundle","who gathered the skins","einar crocolisk"},it="origin"},{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a working leatherworker and tanner based in the port town of Menethil Harbor. He buys raw and cured hides from marsh hunters and makes boots, cured leather, and practical gear for sailors, soldiers, and townspeople.",al={"james halloran role","who is halloran","tanner menethil"}},{q="What is the Bundle of Crocolisk Skins?",a="It is a wrapped parcel of raw hides harvested from the dangerous crocolisks that lurk across the Wetlands. Einar Stonegrip gathered and tied them together to sell to the local craftsmen in Menethil Harbor, though personal troubles keep him from delivering the goods on his own.",al={"what is bundle of crocolisk skins","bundle of crocolisk skins"},it="identity",add="639d94c2"},{q="Why does James Halloran want the Bundle of Crocolisk Skins?",a="James Halloran works as a tanner in Menethil Harbor, relying on reliable shipments of fresh hides to craft quality leather boots and cured armors for residents and travelers. Raw crocolisk hides provide the tough, resilient material he needs to ply his trade and stock his shelves.",al={"why does james halloran need skins","why want bundle of crocolisk skins","james halloran crocolisk skins"},it="why_wanted",add="8cc4b9e1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see how hunters beyond Menethil Harbor supply materials that help equip its garrison and citizens for the harsh swamp."},kw={"crocolisk","einar","james halloran","leather","menethil harbor","sida","skins","wetlands"},rel={"quest:469","npc:james-halloran","npc:sida","subzone:menethil-harbor","item:crocolisk-skin-classic","zone:wetlands"},src={"Bundle of Crocolisk Skins","Daily Delivery"}}
E["item:crude-flint"] = {t="item",n="Crude Flint",z="wetlands",s="Across the Wetlands, Mosshide gnolls carry Crude Flint to kindle fires with freshly hewn marsh timber. Their fires anger Rethiel the Greenwarden, protector of the marsh.",h="Across the Wetlands, Mosshide gnolls carry Crude Flint to kindle fires with freshly hewn marsh timber.",sec={{t="Kindling in the Mire",b="In the Wetlands, Mosshide gnolls use Crude Flint to strike sparks for warmth and to cook meat in the damp bogs. They cut down living timber for their hearths and bonfires. Rethiel the Greenwarden sees each spark as an assault on the marsh's natural balance.",sp=1,bt={"q463.2"}},{t="The Greenwarden's Retribution",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden seeks to stop the Mosshide gnolls from cutting down the marsh's trees. He asks passing adventurers to take the firestones from the pack. Rethiel plans to smash each flint to dust and cast the fragments into the sea, so the gnolls can no longer burn the Wetlands' living wood.",sp=1,bt={"q463.2"}}},faq={{q="What is Crude Flint used for?",a="Mosshide gnolls use Crude Flint to strike sparks for warmth and cooking. Rethiel the Greenwarden asks travelers to gather the flints to stop the gnolls from setting living trees aflame.",al={"crude flint use","what does crude flint do","crude flint purpose"},sp=1,it="purpose",gp=true,bt={"q463.2"}},{q="Which creatures carry Crude Flint?",a="Most adult and specialized Mosshide gnolls carry Crude Flint, including Mosshide Brutes, Trappers, Fenrunners, Mistweavers, Mystics, Alphas, and Gnawbone. Smaller Mosshide gnolls and mongrels do not carry it.",al={"who drops crude flint","where to get crude flint","which gnolls have flint"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Rethiel want the flints destroyed?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is horrified that the gnolls cut down living wetland trees and burn the wood for warmth. He plans to destroy their flints and cast the shards into the sea, leaving them without a way to spark fires.",al={"why destroy crude flint","rethiel flint reason","fire taboo reason"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",bt={"q463.2"}},{q="Are these flints valuable for crafting?",a="No. Crude Flint is a rough stone suited only to sparking a crude flame; it lacks the purity and shape smiths and engineers need.",al={"can i use crude flint in blacksmithing","is crude flint crafting material"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Crude Flint?",a="Crude Flint is a rough, primitive fire-starting stone carried by the Mosshide gnolls of the Wetlands. With these simple tools, the gnolls strike sparks to kindle their campfires, burning the living boughs of the marshland to keep themselves warm.",al={"what is crude flint","crude flint lore","what are these flints"},it="identity",add="b9abde94"},{q="Where does Crude Flint come from, and who made it?",a="These stones are knapped and carried by the Mosshide gnolls inhabiting the bogs of the Wetlands. Almost every mature Mosshide raider, trapper, and mystic keeps one on hand as an essential survival tool for striking flame in the damp marsh.",al={"who made crude flint","where do gnolls get crude flint","crude flint origin"},it="origin",add="e1f52dc4"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that cutting down living plants for gnoll comfort offends the tenets of nature. Taking and shattering the firestones is a natural duty for a guardian of the wild."},kw={"crude flint","fire taboo","gnoll","greenwarden","mosshide","rethiel","striking stone","wetlands"},rel={"quest:277","npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","topic:gnoll","zone:wetlands"},src={"Crude Flint","Fire Taboo"}}
E["item:deepfury-s-orders"] = {t="item",n="Deepfury's Orders",z="wetlands",s="Beneath the Thandol Span, Deepfury's Orders lie with the fallen Ol' Rustlocke. The crumpled parchment carries grim instructions from the Dark Iron dwarves who ambushed the scouting defender.",h="Beneath the Thandol Span, Deepfury's Orders lie with the fallen Ol' Rustlocke.",sec={{t="A Grasp Beneath the Span",b="Ol' Rustlocke, a dwarven bridge defender, was scouting the foundations of the Thandol Span when Dark Iron dwarves cornered and slew him. Beside his clenched fist lay crumpled orders drafted by their leader, Deepfury. The parchment is direct proof of a coordinated plot against the bridge linking the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Threat",b="When the orders reach Rhag Garmason, they confirm the bridge garrison's worst suspicions. The Dark Iron dwarves have planned operations directly beneath the Thandol Span's stonework. Rhag calls for urgent reinforcements from Ironforge and Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are Deepfury's Orders?",a="Deepfury's Orders are written military orders belonging to the Dark Iron commander Deepfury. They were found beside Ol' Rustlocke's corpse beneath the Thandol Span.",al={"deepfurys orders","what are these orders","deepfury parchment"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the orders found?",a="The crumpled parchment was found beside Ol' Rustlocke's clenched fist in the cavernous support structures beneath the Thandol Span in the northern Wetlands.",al={"where are the orders","rustlocke location","find deepfury orders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Ol' Rustlocke?",a="Ol' Rustlocke was a dwarven scout stationed at the Thandol Span. He went to investigate strange activity around the bridge supports and was ambushed by Dark Iron dwarves.",al={"who is rustlocke","ol rustlocke lore"}},{q="Who receives Deepfury's Orders?",a="Deepfury's Orders are brought to Rhag Garmason, the dwarven commander holding out at Dun Modr near the Thandol Span. He reads them to assess the Dark Iron threat.",al={"who do i bring orders to","rhag garmason"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where did Deepfury's Orders come from?",a="These written orders originate from the Dark Iron clan, named after Deepfury, an operative or leader orchestrating hostilities around the Thandol Span. They were carried by the Dark Iron dwarves who ambushed and murdered the mountaineer Ol' Rustlocke, left behind in the dirt beside his fallen body.",al={"who wrote deepfury orders","deepfury orders source","who made deepfury orders"},it="origin",add="21094d89"},{q="Why does Rhag Garmason want Deepfury's Orders?",a="Rhag Garmason needs tangible proof of what befell his missing scout, Ol' Rustlocke. The parchment provides grim confirmation of the mountaineer's death and exposes the hostile schemes the Dark Iron dwarves are putting into motion near the bridge.",al={"why bring deepfury orders to rhag","why are deepfury orders wanted","rhag garmason orders"},it="why_wanted",add="ac08f373"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the discovery of Dark Iron scheming beneath the Thandol Span cuts deep for Ironforge. The span is one of your kingdom's greatest engineering achievements and a vital northern trade link.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the intercepted orders expose a sabotage attempt against the primary overland artery linking Dun Morogh, the Wetlands, and the northern Alliance outposts."},kw={"dark iron","deepfury","orders","rhag garmason","rustlocke","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:631","subzone:thandol-span","quest:634","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},src={"Deepfury's Orders","The Thandol Span (2)"}}
E["item:disarming-colloid"] = {t="item",n="Disarming Colloid",z="wetlands",s="At the Stonewrought Dam, Disarming Colloid could keep Seaforium from exploding when wet. Ashlan Stonesmirk provides it in the Wetlands for a mixture that can neutralize the powder.",h="At the Stonewrought Dam, Disarming Colloid could keep Seaforium from exploding when wet.",sec={{t="A Chemical Neutralizer",b="Ashlan Stonesmirk recognized the powder left by Dark Iron sappers at the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan as Seaforium. Its scent and fine silver crystals gave it away. The powder is harmless while dry, but moisture makes it immensely destructive, a grave danger at the waterlogged dam. Stonesmirk provided Disarming Colloid to stop the reaction before detonation. Mixed with lurker venom, crushed Mo'grosh crystal, and a crocolisk tear, the colloid neutralizes Seaforium's explosive properties.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Disarming Colloid used for?",a="Disarming Colloid is the base chemical agent for defusing Seaforium. Mixed with lurker venom, crushed Mo'grosh crystal, and a crocolisk tear, it neutralizes the powder's volatile reaction when wet.",al={"colloid purpose","what does disarming colloid do","seaforium disarmer"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created or provided this colloid?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk provides the colloid. He is an explosives expert assigned to the regiment guarding Dun Modr in the Wetlands, and recognizes the Dark Iron dwarves' plan to destroy the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"who gives the colloid","ashlan colloid"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Seaforium so dangerous in the Wetlands?",a="Seaforium is harmless while dry, but moisture makes it violently explosive. The Wetlands are saturated with water, and the powder is aimed at the Stonewrought Dam, so damp Seaforium threatens massive devastation.",al={"why is seaforium dangerous","wet seaforium"},it="danger"},{q="Who must this colloid be delivered to?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk says the colloid and news of the Seaforium plot must go straight to Chief Engineer Hinderweir at the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"who do i take colloid to","colloid turn in"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Disarming Colloid?",a="Disarming Colloid is a specialized neutralizing mixture prepared by Ashlan Stonesmirk. When combined with three other potent reagents—lurker venom, crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, and a crocolisk tear—it safely defuses the volatile chemical reaction of Seaforium blast powder before the explosive compound can be triggered by moisture.",al={"what is disarming colloid","disarming colloid identity","colloid lore"},it="identity",add="6b4ad5ab"},{q="Why is Disarming Colloid needed?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir urgently needs the colloid to avert catastrophe at the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan. Dark Iron saboteurs have planted volatile Seaforium at the dam, and without this chemical agent to defuse the reaction, contact with water could blow the dam apart.",al={"why need disarming colloid","why is colloid wanted","who wants disarming colloid"},it="why_wanted",add="1c3f9fc5"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know Seaforium can bring immense destruction. It takes a precise chemical counteragent like this colloid to stop it.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Seaforium aimed at the Stonewrought Dam threatens dwarven engineering and the security of Loch Modan above."},kw={"ashlan stonesmirk","dark iron","disarming colloid","explosives","hinderweir","seaforium","stonewrought dam","wetlands"},rel={"quest:161","npc:ashlan-stonesmirk","item:lurker-venom","item:mo-grosh-crystal","item:crocolisk-tear-classic","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},src={"Disarming Colloid","A Dark Threat Looms (4)"}}
E["item:dragonmaw-war-banner"] = {t="item",n="Dragonmaw War Banner",z="wetlands",s="Dragonmaw War Banners rise over orc encampments in the Wetlands. Their clan markings give the dwarven defenders of Menethil Harbor proof of the growing threat.",h="Dragonmaw War Banners rise over orc encampments in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Emblems of an Enduring Threat",b="After the Second War, the Dragonmaw clan was shattered when they lost control of their enslaved red dragons. The enraged drakes turned on their captors and drove the survivors from Grim Batol into the eastern hills. Now the remaining orcs gather strength under Chieftain Nek'rosh and raise their banners over camps northeast of Menethil Harbor. Those rough standards mark their defiance and threaten the settlements in the marsh.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Conquest",b="Captain Stoutfist at Menethil Harbor sends Alliance adventurers into the marsh camps to bring back Dragonmaw banners. Raiders, centurions, and bone-warders carry these trophies, which confirm to the dwarven garrison that the camps are being broken before the clan can launch coordinated raids.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist want these banners?",a="Captain Stoutfist wants the banners as proof that adventurers have struck the Dragonmaw camp northeast of Menethil Harbor and thinned its ranks.",al={"why collect banners","war banners purpose","why stoutfist wants banners"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who carries the Dragonmaw War Banners?",a="Dragonmaw raiders, swamprunners, centurions, battlemasters, shadowwarders, bonewarders, and Chieftain Nek'rosh carry the banners in their Wetlands camps.",al={"who drops dragonmaw banner","where to get war banners","which orcs have banners"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands?",a="Near the end of the Second War, the Dragonmaw lost control of their captive red dragons. The freed dragons hunted their former masters, forcing the surviving orcs to flee Grim Batol and scatter into the eastern hills, the wetlands, and the surrounding mountains.",al={"why are dragonmaw here","wetlands dragonmaw history","dragonmaw lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Who leads the Dragonmaw clan now?",a="Chieftain Nek'rosh leads the clan. He is the son of its former chieftain, Nekros, and has sworn vengeance against the red dragons who turned on and killed his father.",al={"dragonmaw leader","who is nek'rosh","chieftain nek'rosh"},it="leader"},{q="What is a Dragonmaw War Banner?",a="These battle standards serve as the rallying symbols of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. Marked with the sigils of an orcish clan infamous for once enslaving the red dragonflight, the banners represent their military pride and enduring defiance. To Alliance defenders in Menethil Harbor, capturing them proves that an encampment has been broken and its warriors routed.",al={"what is dragonmaw war banner","dragonmaw banner","dragonmaw war banners"},it="identity",add="abf078db"},{q="Where do Dragonmaw War Banners come from, and who made them?",a="They are crafted and borne by the surviving orcs of the Dragonmaw clan. After losing their stronghold of Grim Batol and fleeing the wrath of liberated red dragons, the Dragonmaw regrouped in the mountains and marshes northeast of Menethil Harbor. There, their raiders, centurions, and shamans fashion these standards to mark their newly claimed territory and rally their growing warbands under Chieftain Nek'rosh.",al={"who made dragonmaw banners","origin dragonmaw war banner","where do the war banners come from"},it="origin",add="2c481a00"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Khaz Modan, you help clear Dragonmaw banners from the marsh and keep the trade corridors to Menethil Harbor safe from orc raiders.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you weaken an old enemy before the Dragonmaw can rebuild the terrible strength they wielded during the Second War."},kw={"dragonmaw","grim batol","menethil","nek'rosh","stoutfist","war banner","wetlands"},rel={"quest:464","npc:captain-stoutfist","zone:wetlands","subzone:grim-batol","topic:second-war"},src={"Dragonmaw War Banner","War Banners"}}
E["item:dwarven-tinder"] = {t="item",n="Dwarven Tinder",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Dwarven Tinder gives Alliance saboteurs a way to burn Dragonmaw siege engines before they reach Menethil Harbor.",h="In the Wetlands, Dwarven Tinder gives Alliance saboteurs a way to burn Dragonmaw siege engines before they...",sec={{t="Sabotaging the Dragonmaw",b="When Alliance scouts found Chieftain Nek'rosh's heavy catapults inside the Dragonmaw encampment, Menethil Harbor faced a crisis. Fighting in Dun Algaz had cut off the harbor from southern reinforcements, and its defenders could not withstand a long siege. They chose to sabotage the catapults before they could be used. Volunteers carrying Dwarven Tinder into orcish territory could light it with a struck spark. Its flames burned through the reinforced wooden engines in minutes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Dwarven Tinder used for?",a="Alliance saboteurs use Dwarven Tinder to burn the Dragonmaw catapults in the Wetlands before they can attack Menethil Harbor.",al={"dwarven tinder purpose","why use dwarven tinder","what does dwarven tinder do"},it="purpose"},{q="Why burn the catapults instead of capturing them?",a="The defenders cannot capture heavy siege engines deep in Dragonmaw territory. With the garrison outnumbered and cut off from Ironforge reinforcements by the blockade at Dun Algaz, destroying the catapults is their only viable defense.",al={"why destroy the catapults","why not take the siege engines"},it="conflict"},{q="Who prepared this tinder?",a="The dwarven garrison at Menethil Harbor supplies the tinder, prepared to catch fire quickly and reliably during sabotage runs.",al={"who made the tinder","where does dwarven tinder come from"},it="origin"},{q="What is Dwarven Tinder?",a="Dwarven Tinder is a highly flammable, specially prepared kindling provided by the defenders of Menethil Harbor. Crafted by dwarf militiamen to catch fire quickly from even a stray spark, it ensures that hefty wooden war machines can be ignited swiftly and thoroughly in the damp Wetlands before enemy forces can react.",al={"what is dwarven tinder","dwarven tinder item","about dwarven tinder"},it="identity",add="5fa2c489"},{q="Why is Dwarven Tinder needed right now?",a="The Dragonmaw orcs under Nek'rosh have constructed massive siege catapults to batter down Menethil Harbor. With reinforcements from Ironforge cut off by fierce fighting in Dun Algaz, Menethil cannot endure a prolonged assault. You must use this tinder to infiltrate the Dragonmaw encampment and burn their war engines to ash before they can march.",al={"why dwarven tinder","why need dwarven tinder","why do we need tinder"},it="why_wanted",add="f9865b90"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know dependable firestarters matter in the Wetlands, where rain and bogs keep the land perpetually soggy.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know burning enemy war engines before they reach Menethil Harbor helps keep your primary marsh port standing while the Dun Algaz passes are contested."},kw={"catapults","dragonmaw","dwarven tinder","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","sabotage","wetlands"},rel={"quest:465","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:wetlands"},src={"Dwarven Tinder","Nek'rosh's Gambit"}}
E["item:ear-of-balgaras"] = {t="item",n="Ear of Balgaras",z="wetlands",s="At Dun Modr, Balgaras the Foul's ear marks the warlock's end. Recovered from the Dark Iron commander's corpse, it gives Ironforge's mountaineers proof of his death.",h="At Dun Modr, Balgaras the Foul's ear marks the warlock's end.",sec={{t="A Grim Trophy",b="Balgaras the Foul commanded the Dark Iron assault on Dun Modr. The invaders sabotaged the Thandol Span and destroyed the local dwarven garrison, leaving the outpost in ruins. A scheming warlock, Balgaras directed his troops from the shadows and shunned personal combat. Longbraid the Grim, the mountain king's officer stationed outside the ruins, wants proof that the ringleader has fallen. Balgaras's severed ear confirms the warlock's reign at the northern border is over.",sp=0},{t="Justice for the Fallen",b="Dun Modr's fall cost Longbraid his brother and dozens of stout soldiers in the collapse of the West Bridge. The ear cannot mend the span or revive the fallen. With Balgaras unable to direct them, the surviving Dark Iron forces scattered through the northern Wetlands become easier for Ironforge's scouts to contain before another commander arrives from the south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul was a Dark Iron dwarf warlock who commanded the warband that struck Dun Modr and destroyed the West Bridge of the Thandol Span. Notorious for cowardice, he sent waves of soldiers to die while hiding from Alliance patrols.",al={"who is balgaras","balgaras lore","balgaras the foul"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Longbraid the Grim want his ear specifically?",a="Longbraid the Grim wants proof that the elusive warlock has been slain. A severed ear is a classic frontier trophy that verifies the contract without making the bearer haul a corpse back to the dwarven camp.",al={"why an ear","why cut off the ear","longbraid proof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens to the Dark Irons once Balgaras is dead?",a="Without their calculating leader, the surviving Dark Iron forces in Dun Modr lose cohesion. Though they still haunt the ruins, Longbraid believes the Alliance can manage them before Ironforge's enemies send a replacement commander.",al={"what happens after balgaras dies","dark irons in dun modr"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does the Ear of Balgaras come from?",a="This severed ear is taken directly from Balgaras the Foul, a cowardly Dark Iron warlock operating in the northern reaches of the Wetlands. Balgaras commands the hostile dwarves who assaulted Dun Modr and destroyed the western span of the Thandol Span, yet he prefers to hide away while sending his minions to fight.",al={"ear of balgaras origin","where to get balgaras ear","who has balgaras ear"},it="origin",add="a51409b4"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Ironforge dwarves, claiming the ear settles a bloody score for the kinsmen slaughtered during the Thandol Span sabotage.",["class:Warlock"]="Balgaras wielded shadow and fel arts from hiding. His defeat puts down an errant practitioner who brought ruin to the northern road."},kw={"balgaras the foul","dark iron","dun modr","ear of balgaras","longbraid the grim","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:304","npc:longbraid-the-grim","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","zone:wetlands","topic:warlock","quest:631"},src={"Ear of Balgaras","A Grim Task"}}
E["item:giant-crocolisk-skin"] = {t="item",n="Giant Crocolisk Skin",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, giant crocolisks yield thick hides that Menethil Harbor tradesmen need for leatherworking. Taking one is perilous work, and more than one hunter has been maimed.",h="In the Wetlands, giant crocolisks yield thick hides that Menethil Harbor tradesmen need for leatherworking.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Trade",b="The Wetlands' bogs and waterways shelter enormous crocolisks with hides dense enough to resist the marsh's damp rot. In Menethil Harbor, artisans such as James Halloran rely on steady shipments of skins to make rugged leather goods. Reaching a full-grown giant crocolisk means braving deep water and facing a fierce swamp predator, so every hide comes hard-won.",sp=0},{t="The Apprentice's Folly",b="Halloran's young apprentice once gathered the thick skins. Without the skill to defeat full-grown marsh beasts, the boy was ambushed along the northern coast. Giant crocolisks mauled him, and he now lies in a local midwife's care. She says he might pull through. After the attack, Halloran hired seasoned adventurers to hunt the predators and secure the skins he needs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are Giant Crocolisk Skins used for?",a="James Halloran, a tradesman in Menethil Harbor, uses Giant Crocolisk Skins to make sturdy leather goods that can endure the marshlands' damp climate.",al={"crocolisk skin use","why collect giant crocolisk skins","halloran skin purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are the crocolisks found that provide these skins?",a="Giant Wetlands Crocolisks roam the coast and inland marsh waters north of Menethil Harbor, in the shallows beyond local murloc settlements.",al={"giant crocolisk location","where to find giant crocolisks","croc coast wetlands"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happened to Halloran's apprentice?",a="Halloran sent his apprentice alone to gather skins in the marsh. Giant crocolisks mauled the boy, and he now lies in a Menethil midwife's care. She says he might pull through.",al={"apprentice injured","halloran apprentice","who lost a leg"}},{q="How do these skins compare to young crocolisk skins?",a="Young crocolisks yield thinner, more pliable skins. Full-grown giant crocolisks yield thicker, tougher hides, but killing one takes seasoned combat skill.",al={"young vs giant crocolisk skin","crocolisk leather difference"}},{q="What is a Giant Crocolisk Skin?",a="It is the thick, durable hide taken from the giant crocolisks roaming the marshes of the Wetlands. Prized by leatherworkers and craftsmen for its toughness and size, harvesting such a pelt is no easy task, as these predators are among the most vicious beasts prowling the waterways.",al={"what is giant crocolisk skin","giant croc skin","crocolisk skin info"},it="identity",add="406c8fec"},{q="Where does Giant Crocolisk Skin come from, and who made it?",a="The skin is harvested naturally from giant Wetlands crocolisks living in the marshes north along the coast beyond the murloc hovels. Rather than being manufactured by an artisan, it must be flayed directly from the carcasses of these massive swamp beasts.",al={"who made giant crocolisk skin","where do giant crocolisk skins come from","giant crocolisk skin source"},it="origin",add="bd43ba97"},{q="Why does James Halloran want Giant Crocolisk Skins?",a="James Halloran, a craftsman in Menethil Harbor, requires the hides for his trade. He originally dispatched his young apprentice to gather them, but after the boy was mauled by the ravenous beasts and left in a midwife's care, Halloran turned to seasoned adventurers to secure the materials and avenge his protege.",al={"why does halloran want skins","who wants giant crocolisk skins","why need giant crocolisk skins"},it="why_wanted",add="c37602c5"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, stalking giant crocolisks along the coastline tests your skill at tracking aquatic beasts and keeping clear of the marsh waters."},kw={"apprentice's duties","crocolisk","giant crocolisk skin","james halloran","menethil harbor","wetlands"},rel={"quest:471","npc:james-halloran","quest:484","item:young-crocolisk-skin","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc","item:crocolisk-skin-classic"},src={"Giant Crocolisk Skin","Apprentice's Duties"}}
E["item:golm-fragment"] = {t="item",n="Golm Fragment",z="wetlands",s="At the southern Wetlands dig, Golm Fragment lies among the four missing pieces of the Goaz Stone. Dwarven archaeologists need it to piece together the ancient Titan inscriptions.",h="At the southern Wetlands dig, Golm Fragment lies among the four missing pieces of the Goaz Stone.",sec={{t="A Piece of the Goaz Stone",b="Golm Fragment lies among the remains of Whelgar's excavation in the southern Wetlands. Prospector Whelgar found the monumental Goaz Stone shortly before raptors drove the Explorers' League back. Its inscription had been severed in four places. When the dig was overrun, the fragment remained amid dirt and overturned crates, hidden inside an ancient relic box until explorers could retrieve it.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Titans",b="Golm Fragment completes a cryptic Titan text when joined with the Ados, Modr, and Neru fragments. Reassembling the Goaz Stone lets Whelgar decipher lines about a divine plan, a doomed prophecy, and ancient entities chained beneath the earth. The inscription reveals lore older and more dangerous than dwarven heritage alone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Golm Fragment used for?",a="Prospector Whelgar needs Golm Fragment with three other pieces to restore the Goaz Stone at the Wetlands excavation site during Uncovering the Past.",al={"golm fragment purpose","why need golm fragment","golm fragment quest"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Where can the Golm Fragment be found?",a="Golm Fragment can be found in ancient relics and loose soil across the raptor-infested dig site in the southern Wetlands hills.",al={"golm fragment location","find golm fragment","where is golm fragment"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the Goaz Stone say once assembled?",a="Whelgar's first translation speaks of a divine plan and a doomed prophecy. He needs all four fragments to keep deciphering the incomplete Titan script.",al={"goaz stone translation","what does the tablet say","whelgar translation"},sp=1},{q="What other fragments are needed to finish the stone?",a="You need the Ados, Modr, and Neru fragments along with Golm to assemble the tablet.",al={"other tablet fragments","goaz stone pieces","four fragments"},gp=true},{q="What is the Golm Fragment?",a="The Golm Fragment is one of four missing pieces broken off from the Goaz Stone, an ancient relic uncovered at the excavation site in the Wetlands. It bears archaic inscriptions that fit into the larger tablet's cryptic narrative.",al={"what is golm fragment","golm fragment lore","what is the golm piece"},it="identity",add="523a83d7"},{q="Where does the Golm Fragment come from, and who made it?",a="The fragment originated as part of the Goaz Stone, carved long ago in Titan script. It was unearthed during the dwarven archaeological dig at the Wetlands excavation site, before hostile raptors overran the area and scattered its broken pieces.",al={"who made the golm fragment","origin of golm fragment","where did golm fragment come from"},it="origin",add="890266ad"},{q="Why does Prospector Whelgar want the Golm Fragment?",a="Prospector Whelgar needs the Golm Fragment along with its sister pieces to assemble the complete Goaz Stone. Without it, the translated text abruptly cuts off, leaving crucial details about a divine plan and doomed prophecy missing.",al={"why does whelgar need golm fragment","who wants the golm fragment","why search for the golm fragment"},it="why_wanted",add="6695e471"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can help piece together the Goaz Stone and uncover your Titan ancestry and the hidden history beneath Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help the Explorers' League secure priceless ancient knowledge before raptors overrun the dig site."},kw={"excavation site","goaz stone","golm fragment","uncovering the past","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:299","npc:prospector-whelgar","item:ados-fragment","item:modr-fragment","item:neru-fragment","zone:wetlands","topic:titan","topic:old-god"},src={"Golm Fragment","Uncovering the Past"}}
E["item:intrepid-strongbox-key"] = {t="item",n="Intrepid Strongbox Key",z="wetlands",s="On the wreck of the Intrepid, Captain Halyndor still guards the key to his strongbox. The rusted iron key once kept a mysterious item locked away aboard the doomed Alliance vessel off the Wetlands.",h="On the wreck of the Intrepid, Captain Halyndor still guards the key to his strongbox.",sec={{t="A Captain's Secret",b="The Intrepid was wrecked with the Third Fleet off the Wetlands, and its crew became restless, cursed spirits. Captain Halyndor watched over a mysterious item inside the ship’s heavy strongbox. Now his ghost prowls the waterlogged deck, still clutching the rusted key that opens it.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Bond",b="Captain Halyndor’s key opens the Intrepid’s strongbox, where a cursed relic anchors the crew to their torment. The relic can be taken to Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarven priest in Menethil Harbor, for cleansing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who carries the Intrepid Strongbox Key?",a="Captain Halyndor carries the key as he paces the upper deck of the northern shipwreck off the Wetlands’ northwest coast.",al={"who has the key","intrepid key drop","halyndor key"},it="people"},{q="What does the Intrepid Strongbox Key open?",a="The key opens the Intrepid’s Locked Strongbox, submerged in the fractured hull beneath the captain’s deck.",al={"what does it unlock","intrepid strongbox location","where is the chest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why was the strongbox kept locked?",a="Captain Halyndor locked a cursed object inside the chest to keep it hidden and secure. After the fleet sank, its lingering evil bound the crew to undeath.",al={"what was in the chest","why was it locked"},it="motive"},{q="Who can cleanse the cursed item inside the chest?",a="Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarven priest in Menethil Harbor, can cleanse the cursed artifact once the chest is unlocked.",al={"who cleanses it","glorin steelbrow chest"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Intrepid Strongbox Key?",a="It is a rusted ship key kept by Captain Halyndor aboard the wrecked vessel Intrepid. Even after death, the cursed captain guards the key zealously, for it is the only means of unlocking the ship's reinforced strongbox hidden within the shattered hull.",al={"intrepid strongbox key","what is the key","intrepid key"},it="identity",add="b4277111"},{q="Why is the Intrepid Strongbox Key needed?",a="The key is required to open the Intrepid's strongbox and recover the dark relic locked inside. First Mate Fitzsimmons believes this stowed artifact brought about the horrific curse that binds Halyndor and his crew to the wreck, and opening the chest is the first step toward lifting it.",al={"why do i need the key","why get the key","intrepid key purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="90ec2e74"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can bring the cursed artifact to Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor for cleansing, freeing the crew’s souls from their torment.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the key belonged to a commander of the Third Fleet, lost off the coast of Menethil Harbor. Its loss remains an open wound for the harbor’s survivors."},kw={"captain halyndor","cursed crew","glorin steelbrow","intrepid","shipwreck","strongbox","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:290","quest:288","npc:glorin-steelbrow","zone:wetlands","topic:priest"},src={"Intrepid Strongbox Key","Lifting the Curse (Classic)"}}
E["item:mackreel-s-moonshine"] = {t="item",n="MacKreel's Moonshine",z="wetlands",s="On the broken Thandol Span, Foggy MacKreel brews moonshine strong enough to fell a sentry. Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore takes a batch to settle Foggy's debt.",h="On the broken Thandol Span, Foggy MacKreel brews moonshine strong enough to fell a sentry.",sec={{t="A Potent Brew",b="Foggy MacKreel brews his moonshine while stationed as a guard on the Thandol Span. The liquor has a fierce reputation, and even hardened dwarven sentries can be laid low after a night of drinking it. They wake with headaches like siege engines rolling overhead. Travelers value its warmth against the damp chill of Lordaeron and Khaz Modan.",sp=0},{t="Payment to Southshore",b="Foggy MacKreel owed an unsettled debt to Brewmeister Bilger, Southshore's tavern keeper and master brewer. He sent a batch of moonshine instead of coin to clear his tab. Bilger accepts the liquor in place of gold and adds MacKreel's potent brew to his stock for the chilly coastal days of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who makes MacKreel's Moonshine?",a="Foggy MacKreel, a dwarf sentry stationed on the broken Thandol Span between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands, distills the moonshine.",al={"creator of mackreels moonshine","who brewed it","foggy mackreel liquor"},it="origin"},{q="Why is this moonshine being sent to Southshore?",a="Foggy MacKreel owed a debt to Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore. He agreed to settle it by sending Bilger a fresh batch of moonshine instead of coin.",al={"why southshore","moonshine delivery","brewmeister bilger debt"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How strong is MacKreel's Moonshine?",a="MacKreel's Moonshine is exceptionally strong. Foggy admitted that he passed out while on duty after drinking it, then woke with a headache like siege engines rumbling over his skull.",al={"how potent is it","moonshine strength","effects of mackreels moonshine"},it="power"},{q="Why does the delivery need to be rushed?",a="Foggy drank heavily and slept through his watch. When he woke, only minutes remained before his debt deadline with Brewmeister Bilger.",al={"why timed","is the quest timed","why hurry"},it="motive"},{q="What is MacKreel's Moonshine?",a="MacKreel's Moonshine is a potent, handcrafted liquor brewed by Foggy MacKreel in the Wetlands. Notorious for packing a tremendous punch, it is potent enough to leave even a sturdy dwarf nurse a hangover that feels like a brigade of siege engines rolling over his head. Beyond its formidable kick, it serves as valuable barter, sought after even as far north as Hillsbrad Foothills to warm folk on brisk days.",al={"what is mackreel's moonshine","mackreels moonshine","foggy mackreel drink"},it="identity",add="abca7076"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know a good stiff drink when you smell one. Foggy's moonshine packs enough punch to knock a mountaineer flat.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know potent regional spirits like Foggy's rough moonshine are staple trade goods across frontier taverns."},kw={"brewmeister bilger","dwarf brew","foggy mackreel","mackreel's moonshine","moonshine","southshore","wetlands"},rel={"quest:647","npc:foggy-mackreel","npc:brewmeister-bilger","subzone:southshore","zone:wetlands"},src={"MacKreel's Moonshine","MacKreel's Moonshine (quest)"}}
E["item:menethil-statuette"] = {t="item",n="Menethil Statuette",z="wetlands",s="Off the Wetlands coast, the Menethil Statuette lies lost from a shipwreck. The rare silver likeness honors Lordaeron's fallen king.",h="Off the Wetlands coast, the Menethil Statuette lies lost from a shipwreck.",sec={{t="A Rare Relic of Lordaeron",b="King Terenas Menethil II appears in his youth, a long-haired paladin lifting a hammer toward the heavens. He was humble and disliked personal monuments, so few statues or likenesses were made in his honor. The Scourge's fall of Lordaeron destroyed almost all of them. This surviving effigy is extraordinarily valuable to the Alliance.",sp=0},{t="Loss in the Bogs",b="The Blind Princess carried the statuette toward the Alliance harbor of Menethil. Bluegill murlocs attacked the merchant vessel off the marshy coast, scattering its cargo. The statuette became trapped in a half-buried barrel on shore. With Dragonmaw orcs and other local threats nearby, defenders hurried to send the recovered icon south to Stormwind City. There, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon entrusted it to the Cathedral of Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is shown on the statuette?",a="The statuette depicts King Terenas Menethil II, former ruler of Lordaeron and architect of the original Alliance. He appears as a young paladin, raising a warhammer.",al={"who is on the statue","what does the statuette depict","who is the menethil statuette"},it="identity"},{q="How was the statuette lost?",a="The merchant vessel Blind Princess carried it across the Great Sea. Bluegill murlocs attacked the ship in the Wetlands, and its cargo washed ashore and was buried in the mud.",al={"how did it get lost","who lost the statuette","shipwreck wetlands statue"},it="history"},{q="Why are depictions of King Terenas so rare?",a="King Terenas disliked self-aggrandizing memorials, so few statues of him were made. The Scourge's devastation of Lordaeron destroyed almost all the portraits and figures that remained in the north.",al={"why are there few statues of terenas","terenas memorials"},it="fame"},{q="Where does the statuette end up?",a="After its recovery in the Wetlands, the statuette is brought to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep. He recognizes the Light within the relic and entrusts it to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker at the Cathedral of Light.",al={"where do i take the statuette","who keeps the statuette","statuette cathedral"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Menethil Statuette?",a="The Menethil Statuette is a silvery figurine depicting King Terenas Menethil II in his youth as a long-haired paladin with his hammer raised. Beyond being an exquisite likeness of the fallen monarch of Lordaeron, the relic seems to have the Light itself coalescing within it, making it both a precious historical monument and a blessed sacred object.",al={"what is menethil statuette","menethil statue","what is the statuette"},it="identity",add="00c7d589"},{q="Why is the Menethil Statuette so sought after?",a="King Terenas despised personal monuments and memorials, leaving extraordinarily few likenesses of him behind, almost all of which were destroyed when Lordaeron fell to the Scourge. Its rarity, sacred Light, and deep sentimental tie to the founder of the Alliance make it an irreplaceable heirloom, one that enemies like the local Dragonmaw orcs would gladly desecrate or plunder if left unguarded.",al={"why do people want menethil statuette","why is the statuette valuable","who wants the statuette"},it="why_wanted",add="0d8a0354"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see King Terenas as a young warrior of the Light, raising his hammer. His portrait speaks to holy knights who mourn the fallen kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Terenas as the unifying leader who founded the Grand Alliance. Any memorial of him that survives is an inspiring treasure in a fractured world."},kw={"blind princess","bluegill","bolvar fordragon","cathedral of light","grayson shadowbreaker","menethil statuette","terenas menethil","wetlands"},rel={"topic:terenas-menethil-ii","topic:lordaeron","subzone:cathedral-of-light","npc:bolvar-fordragon","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","zone:wetlands","topic:paladin","subzone:stormwind-keep"},src={"Menethil Statuette","A Friend of the Family","A Friend of the Family (2)"}}
E["item:merrin-s-letter"] = {t="item",n="Merrin's Letter",z="wetlands",s="At the Whelgar's Excavation site, Merrin Rockweaver sends an urgent message from the Wetlands. Raptors have overrun the dig, but Merrin assures her loved ones that she survived.",h="At the Whelgar's Excavation site, Merrin Rockweaver sends an urgent message from the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Dispatch from the Ruins",b="Merrin Rockweaver writes from the ruined dig at Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands. The dwarven expedition had been uncovering enormous prehistoric fossils and relics when they disturbed a nest of Mottled Raptors. The beasts swarmed the trenches, killed several workers, and cut off the surviving researchers. Amid the chaos, Merrin sends word to her husband Tarrel at Menethil Harbor. She, Prospector Whelgar, and Ormer Ironbraid survived behind a barricaded shelter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote Merrin's Letter?",a="Merrin Rockweaver wrote the letter while taking part in the archaeological expedition at the dig site east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"author of merrins letter","who is merrin"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the letter addressed to?",a="Merrin addressed the letter to Tarrel Rockweaver, who waits anxiously for news on the bridge at Menethil Harbor.",al={"recipient of merrins letter","who gets merrins letter"}},{q="What happened to the excavation team?",a="Mottled Raptors overran the archaeological team while it uncovered massive fossilized bones. Many dwarven workers were killed, and only a handful survived behind barricades in a makeshift camp.",al={"what happened to the dig","why did the expedition fail"},it="conflict"},{q="Who helped Merrin survive the attack?",a="Ormer Ironbraid helped Merrin survive the attack. He defended Merrin and the head prospector, giving them time to retreat to shelter while the raptors overwhelmed the rest of the dig.",al={"who saved merrin","ormer ironbraid"},it="allies"},{q="What is Merrin's Letter?",a="Merrin's Letter is an urgent message written by Merrin Rockweaver, a survivor of the catastrophic raptor assault on the Wetlands excavation site. Addressed to her beloved Tarrel Rockweaver, the note recounts the disaster that befell their digging team and confirms that she, Prospector Whelgar, and Ormer Ironbraid narrowly escaped with their lives.",al={"merrins letter","what is merrins letter","merrin note"},it="identity",add="bce088a8"},{q="Why does Tarrel want Merrin's Letter?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver sent you into the dangerous bogs specifically seeking news of his loved one and the fate of the missing dig crew. Merrin's Letter provides him with vital confirmation that she is still alive, while detailing the tragic loss of the excavation site and their desperate refuge from the surrounding raptors.",al={"why deliver merrins letter","why does tarrel want the letter","merrins letter purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="ded8799c"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For a dwarf, Merrin's letter shows the personal cost the Explorers' League pays to uncover ancient history in the dangerous wilds of Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="For an Alliance traveler, delivering the note brings vital intelligence and bittersweet comfort to the sentries watching the Wetlands highway."},kw={"explorers' league","merrin rockweaver","merrin's letter","mottled raptors","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands","whelgar's excavation"},rel={"quest:305","npc:tarrel-rockweaver","zone:wetlands"},src={"Merrin's Letter","In Search of The Excavation Team (2)"}}
E["item:modr-fragment"] = {t="item",n="Modr Fragment",z="wetlands",s="At Whelgar Excavation Site, Modr Fragment lies among the relics and loose earth of a raptor-overrun dig. The ancient Titan script on it is one of four missing pieces of the Goaz Stone.",h="At Whelgar Excavation Site, Modr Fragment lies among the relics and loose earth of a raptor-overrun dig.",sec={{t="A Piece of the Goaz Stone",b="Prospector Whelgar uncovered the Goaz Stone, a massive tablet marked with ancient Titan writing, at his Wetlands dig. Vicious raptors drove the Explorers' League from the site before they could finish their work. The translated inscription broke off at four gaps, hiding warnings of a divine plan and a doomed prophecy. Modr Fragment is one of the missing pieces, left among the relics and overturned soil when the diggers fled for their lives.",sp=0},{t="Secrets Beneath the Earth",b="Prospector Whelgar can restore the full inscription by joining Modr Fragment with the Ados, Golm, and Neru fragments. Its translated words tell of the dawn of the world and speak of 'Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.' The dig in the marshlands has uncovered traces of a struggle from the world's beginning, bound beneath the soil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Modr Fragment?",a="Modr Fragment is a shard of inscribed stone broken from the Goaz Stone, an ancient Titan relic Prospector Whelgar found at the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands.",al={"modr fragment","what is modr","modr relic"},it="identity"},{q="Who is looking for this fragment?",a="Prospector Whelgar, an archeologist of the Explorers' League, seeks the fragment to complete the tablet's missing text. He is stationed at the edge of the raptor-infested dig site.",al={"who wants modr fragment","whelgar fragment quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when all four fragments are gathered?",a="Joining Modr Fragment with the Ados, Golm, and Neru fragments lets Prospector Whelgar restore the Goaz Stone. Its full Titan script speaks of 'Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.'",al={"goaz stone completed","uncovering the past ending","what does the goaz stone say"},sp=1},{q="Where is the fragment found?",a="You can find Modr Fragment scattered across the Whelgar Excavation Site east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. It lies in ancient relic pots or patches of loose dirt guarded by aggressive raptors.",al={"modr fragment location","where to find modr"},gp=true},{q="Where does the Modr Fragment come from, and who made it?",a="The Modr Fragment is a piece of the Goaz Stone, an ancient relic uncovered at the excavation site east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Inscribed with Titan script, the stone is an artifact of the Titans, who shaped the world in primordial times and left behind mysterious records of their divine plan and doom prophecies.",al={"modr fragment origin","who made the modr fragment","where did modr fragment come from"},it="origin",add="c1df2f2b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Explorers' League seeks lost pieces like Modr Fragment to decipher Titan heritage and uncover the deep history of your kind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help Prospector Whelgar brave the overrun excavation and preserve invaluable historical research for Ironforge."},kw={"ados","excavation","goaz stone","golm","modr fragment","neru","old gods","titan","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:299","npc:prospector-whelgar","item:ados-fragment","item:golm-fragment","item:neru-fragment","zone:wetlands","topic:titan","topic:old-god"},src={"Modr Fragment","Uncovering the Past"}}
E["item:nek-rosh-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Nek'rosh's Head",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Nek'rosh's Head proves the Dragonmaw chieftain has fallen. Captain Stoutfist receives it as proof that the threat to Menethil Harbor has been broken.",h="In the Wetlands, Nek'rosh's Head proves the Dragonmaw chieftain has fallen.",sec={{t="A Decisive Strike",b="The Dragonmaw clan gathers forces and siege weapons across the marshlands, threatening the Alliance port of Menethil Harbor. After the clan's catapults are burned, the port's defense depends on killing Chieftain Nek'rosh. His severed head gives Captain Stoutfist and the Ironforge authorities proof that the warlord's hold over the Wetlands is broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Nek'rosh?",a="Nek'rosh was the chieftain of the Dragonmaw clan remnants in the Wetlands. He directed attacks and war efforts against nearby Alliance territories.",al={"who is nek'rosh","chieftain nek'rosh","who was nekrosh"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Nek'rosh's Head?",a="Captain Stoutfist wants Nek'rosh's Head as proof that the chieftain has fallen. He commands Menethil Harbor's defense and gives a reward on Ironforge's behalf.",al={"who takes the head","nekrosh head turn in","where do i bring nek'rosh's head"}},{q="Why was Nek'rosh targeted for death?",a="Nek'rosh directed the Dragonmaw forces threatening Menethil Harbor. The Alliance sought to cripple the clan's presence in the region by destroying its siege weapons and killing its chieftain.",al={"why kill nekrosh","why defeat nek'rosh"},it="target"},{q="What is Nek'rosh's Head?",a="It is the severed head of Chieftain Nek'rosh, the warlord commanding the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. It serves as gruesome, undeniable proof that the Ironforge Mountaineers' greatest local enemy has finally been slain.",al={"what is nekrosh head","nekrosh head item","nekrosh severed head"},it="item",add="e464fcda"},{q="Where does Nek'rosh's Head come from, and who made it?",a="It is taken directly from Chieftain Nek'rosh after you defeat him at the Dragonmaw encampment in the Wetlands. It was not crafted or manufactured, but rather severed from the fallen orc chieftain as a trophy and confirmation of his demise.",al={"where does nekrosh head come from","how to get nekrosh head","origin of nekrosh head"},it="origin",add="160e4c8d"},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist want Nek'rosh's Head?",a="Captain Stoutfist requires indisputable proof that the leader of the Dragonmaw clan has fallen. With Nek'rosh dead and their war catapults destroyed, Stoutfist knows the Dragonmaw will struggle to recover, ensuring Menethil Harbor and the Wetlands are finally safe from organized assault.",al={"why does stoutfist want nekrosh head","why do they want nekrosh head","purpose of nekrosh head"},it="why_wanted",add="ce210494"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, presenting Nek'rosh's Head to Captain Stoutfist helps secure Menethil Harbor from imminent assault and earns favor with the Kingdom of Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Dragonmaw have plagued Khaz Modan since the Second War. Carrying the chieftain's severed head brings long-awaited justice to the marshlands' defenders."},kw={"captain stoutfist","chieftain","dragonmaw","menethil","nek'rosh","nekrosh","wetlands"},rel={"quest:474","npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},src={"Nek'rosh's Head","Defeat Nek'rosh"}}
E["item:neru-fragment"] = {t="item",n="Neru Fragment",z="wetlands",s="Unearthed from disturbed earth, the Neru Fragment carries part of the Goaz Stone's ancient Titan script. The relic was discovered at Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands, and its words tell of Azeroth's primeval history.",h="Unearthed from disturbed earth, the Neru Fragment carries part of the Goaz Stone's ancient Titan script.",sec={{t="Piece of the Goaz Stone",b="Prospector Whelgar led the dwarven expedition that discovered the Goaz Stone. The relic broke into four pieces: Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru. Raptors overran the dig, halting the work, and the Neru Fragment remained beneath loose soil among the aggressive beasts. Once recovered, it can join the other pieces and restore the tablet. Its surviving words speak of a divine plan and a doomed prophecy, giving dwarven scholars a record to decipher.",sp=0},{t="Reading the Restored Tablet",b="With all four fragments gathered, Prospector Whelgar restores the Goaz Stone and continues translating its Titan script. The newly legible words tell of Old Gods chained beneath the land.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Neru Fragment?",a="The Neru Fragment is an ancient stone piece broken from the Goaz Stone, a larger relic. The dwarven expedition uncovered it in the Wetlands before raptors overran the dig.",al={"neru fragment lore","what is neru fragment","neru tablet piece"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the fragment found?",a="The Neru Fragment lies scattered in Whelgar's Excavation, east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. It is typically buried under loose soil or hidden among abandoned artifacts.",al={"where to find neru fragment","neru fragment location","how to get neru fragment"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when all four fragments are gathered?",a="After all four fragments are gathered, Prospector Whelgar pieces the Goaz Stone back together and continues translating its Titan script, pursuing the mystery hinted at by the surviving text.",al={"goaz stone complete","what does the goaz stone say","uncovering the past ending"},sp=1},{q="Where does the Neru Fragment come from, and who made it?",a="The fragment comes from the ancient Goaz Stone uncovered at Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands. Its inscription uses Titan script, but the recovered quest text does not identify its maker.",al={"neru fragment origin","who made neru fragment","where did the neru fragment come from"},it="origin",add="1f660d59"},{q="Why does Prospector Whelgar want the Neru Fragment?",a="Prospector Whelgar unearthed the Goaz Stone right before the dig site was overrun by raptors, but found the inscription broke off in four distinct places. He urgently needs the Neru Fragment alongside the other three pieces to assemble the tablet and continue deciphering the references to a divine plan and a doomed prophecy.",al={"why find neru fragment","why does whelgar need neru fragment","neru fragment purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="b6f45f31"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the Explorer's League, recovering tablet pieces like the Neru Fragment is vital to unearthing Titan secrets and piecing together the origins of dwarven kind."},kw={"excavation","goaz stone","loose soil","neru fragment","prospector whelgar","uncovering the past","wetlands"},rel={"quest:299","npc:prospector-whelgar","item:ados-fragment","item:golm-fragment","item:modr-fragment","zone:wetlands","topic:titan","topic:old-god"},src={"Neru Fragment","Uncovering the Past"}}
E["item:sarltooth-s-talon"] = {t="item",n="Sarltooth's Talon",z="wetlands",s="Above Whelgar's Excavation Site, Sarltooth's Talon marks the end of the raptor's attack. Ormer Ironbraid wants the claw as proof that the beast has been slain.",h="Above Whelgar's Excavation Site, Sarltooth's Talon marks the end of the raptor's attack.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Vengeance",b="Ormer Ironbraid watched from the ridge as raptors overran Whelgar's Excavation Site and butchered the dwarven expedition. He could not stop the slaughter. One massive raptor, Sarltooth, seemed to Ormer the likely pack leader. Seeking vengeance for his fallen kin, Ormer demanded the beast's death and one of its talons as proof. The claw marks the end of Sarltooth's reign over the ancient dwarven ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Sarltooth's Talon come from?",a="Sarltooth's Talon comes from Sarltooth, a large alpha raptor prowling the western ridges above Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands.",al={"who drops sarltooths talon","sarltooth location","how to get talon"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Sarltooth's Talon?",a="Ormer Ironbraid wants the talon. The dwarf is stationed on the overlook above Whelgar's Excavation Site and asks for proof that the beast that slaughtered his crew has been slain.",al={"who takes the talon","where to turn in talon","ormer ironbraid quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Ormer Ironbraid need proof of Sarltooth's death?",a="Ormer believes Sarltooth led the raptor pack that drove off and killed the dwarven excavators. He sees the talon as justice and closure for his fallen colleagues.",al={"why kill sarltooth","what did sarltooth do"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to the dwarves at the excavation site?",a="The dwarven dig sought ancient artifacts for the Explorers' League. Wild raptors ambushed the workers, slaughtering most and driving the survivors to the nearby ridge.",al={"whelgars excavation site lore","why are raptors at the dig"},it="history"},{q="What is Sarltooth's Talon?",a="It is a severed claw taken from Sarltooth, the ferocious raptor suspected of leading the savage pack that overran Whelgar's Excavation Site. Ormer Ironbraid demands the claw as undeniable evidence that the beast has been slain and the fallen dwarven excavators have been avenged.",al={"what is sarltooth talon","sarltooth talon lore"},it="identity",add="28fc0e8a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, recovering this talon brings vengeance for the dwarven archaeologists who died serving the Explorers' League at King Magni Bronzebeard's behest.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking a cunning pack leader like Sarltooth and taking a claw as a trophy tests marksmanship and beast mastery."},kw={"excavation","ormer ironbraid","raptor","sarltooth","talon","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:294","npc:ormer-ironbraid","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","zone:wetlands","quest:299"},src={"Sarltooth's Talon","Ormer's Revenge (3)"}}
E["item:sida-s-bag"] = {t="item",n="Sida's Bag",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Sida's Bag lies swallowed in an ooze near Ironbeard's Tomb. Sida, a resident of Menethil Harbor, fled after throwing her satchel at one of the slimes during her weekly visit; the bag and its contents must be recovered from the acidic creatures.",h="In the Wetlands, Sida's Bag lies swallowed in an ooze near Ironbeard's Tomb.",sec={{t="A Panicked Defense",b="Sida visits Ironbeard's Tomb near Dun Modr each week. Dreadful, dripping oozes ambushed her there, and panic drove her to fling her satchel at one of them. The ooze absorbed the bag into its body. The distraction gave Sida time to escape alive and return to Menethil Harbor, while her possessions remained trapped inside an unknown slime.",sp=0},{t="Recovered from the Slime",b="The oozes around Ironbeard's Tomb range from crimson to monstrous, and look much alike. Sida's Bag can be found by cutting down the marsh slimes until the swallowed satchel emerges intact. Acidic muck has soaked the durable sack, but its contents remain preserved. Sida reclaims her belongings, then discards the ruined, slime-coated exterior and offers the washed-out container to whoever braved the marsh on her behalf.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Sida's bag inside an ooze?",a="Sida panicked when dripping slimes attacked her during a visit to Ironbeard's Tomb. She hurled her satchel at one to escape, and the ooze swallowed it whole.",al={"how did ooze get bag","why is bag in slime","how did sida lose bag"},it="why_here"},{q="Which oozes carry Sida's Bag?",a="Sida cannot tell the slimes apart, so any predatory ooze around Ironbeard's Tomb in the northeastern Wetlands might have swallowed the bag. Crimson Oozes, Black Oozes, and Monstrous Oozes all prowl there.",al={"where to find sida's bag","what drops sida's bag","which slime has bag"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Sida visit Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Sida makes a weekly trip from Menethil Harbor to visit the ancient dwarven crypt near Dun Modr. She keeps the personal reasons for these visits to herself.",al={"sida ironbeard connection","why ironbeard's tomb"},it="motive"},{q="What was inside Sida's bag?",a="Sida empties her recovered items onto the ground and gathers them without showing what they are. She says only that they were far too important to leave dissolving inside an ooze.",al={"what does sida take out of the bag","bag contents"},it="item"},{q="What is Sida's Bag?",a="Sida's Bag is a personal satchel belonging to Sida, a resident staying in Menethil Harbor. While making her routine visit to Ironbeard's Tomb in the Wetlands, she was ambushed by slimes and flung her pack at one in a frantic bid to escape. The creature swallowed it whole, leaving the bag trapped inside the creature's gelatinous body.",al={"what is sidas bag","sida bag","who is sida bag"},it="identity",add="113113dd"},{q="Why does Sida want her bag back?",a="Sida desperately needs the contents locked inside her lost satchel, rather than the bag itself. Once you pry it from the remains of the oozes at Ironbeard's Tomb and return it to her in Menethil Harbor, she immediately dumps the slimy contents onto the ground, scoops them up, and hands you the empty, ooze-stained pouch.",al={"why does sida want her bag","why sidas bag","why does anyone want sidas bag"},it="why_wanted",add="afbd2451"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor's beleaguered refugees and townsfolk rely on passing travelers to face the predatory horrors creeping in from the flooded Wetlands."},kw={"dun modr","ironbeard's tomb","menethil harbor","ooze","sida","sida's bag","wetlands"},rel={"quest:470","npc:sida","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Sida's Bag","Digging Through the Ooze"}}
E["item:snellig-s-snuffbox"] = {t="item",n="Snellig's Snuffbox",z="wetlands",s="At the Lost Fleet, Snellig's Snuffbox remains with its undead owner among the wrecks. First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor wants it as proof his cursed crewmate has been put to rest.",h="At the Lost Fleet, Snellig's Snuffbox remains with its undead owner among the wrecks.",sec={{t="A Keepsake of the Third Fleet",b="First Mate Snellig still clutches his snuffbox in a wreck off the northern Wetlands. When the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras ran aground there, its sailors and officers drowned beneath a mysterious power tied to a hidden treasure aboard the ships. Bound by that power, the drowned crew rose again as tortured spirits and skeletal undead. Snellig haunts the rotting hold of the wreck closest to the coastline. His snuffbox is a small, ordinary reminder of his mortal life at sea. First Mate Fitzsimmons, the disaster's sole living survivor, wants this possession returned as proof that at least one lost shipmate has found release from torment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Snellig's Snuffbox?",a="First Mate Snellig once owned the small, personal container called Snellig's Snuffbox. His undead remnant carries it aboard a shipwreck off the northern Wetlands coast.",al={"what is this item","snelligs snuffbox","snuff box"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Snellig's Snuffbox?",a="You can take the snuffbox from First Mate Snellig, who haunts the hold of the shipwreck closest to shore at the Lost Fleet in the northwestern Wetlands.",al={"where does snellig drop snuffbox","find snellig","first mate snellig location"},gp=true},{q="Who wants this snuffbox?",a="First Mate Fitzsimmons wants you to bring him the snuffbox at Menethil Harbor. The Third Fleet's sole living survivor asks for it as proof that Snellig has been put to rest.",al={"who takes the snuffbox","who do i turn this into","fitzsimmons quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is First Mate Snellig cursed?",a="Fitzsimmons says a dark, terrible treasure hidden aboard one of the Third Fleet's vessels doomed the crews when the ships wrecked. Their souls remain trapped in the rotting timbers, denied rest.",al={"why is snellig undead","lost fleet curse","curse of third fleet"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, recovering the possessions of fallen Kul Tiran sailors and laying their cursed spirits to rest is a grim duty to an old naval ally."},kw={"cursed crew","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","lost fleet","snellig","snuffbox","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:289","quest:288","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","subzone:lost-fleet","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:kul-tiras","zone:wetlands"},src={"Snellig's Snuffbox","The Cursed Crew (Classic)"}}
E["item:young-crocolisk-skin"] = {t="item",n="Young Crocolisk Skin",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, young crocolisks provide hides for trade from Menethil Harbor. Their softer skins are cured by local tanner James Halloran and shipped to distant ports.",h="In the Wetlands, young crocolisks provide hides for trade from Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="Tanning and Trade in the Marshes",b="Menethil Harbor sends marsh goods to distant ports from the western coast of Khaz Modan. The town’s resident tanner, James Halloran, cures hides among its most lucrative exports. Full-grown crocolisks have thick, tough scales, while their young provide softer leather that is easier to work. The delicate skins are in high demand, so Halloran depends on local hunters and passing travelers to search the boggy marshes just outside town and keep his curing racks stocked.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does James Halloran want skins from young crocolisks specifically?",a="Young crocolisks have softer hides that are easier to work and cure than the thick, tough scales of mature crocolisks. Their leather is in high demand across sea trade routes.",al={"why young crocolisk skin","halloran skins","why soft skins"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can young crocolisks be found?",a="Young Wetlands Crocolisks live in the waterways, bogs, and marshes just outside Menethil Harbor in the western Wetlands.",al={"young crocolisk location","where to find young crocs","wetlands crocolisks"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who else hunts these crocolisks for the harbor?",a="Einar, a local hunter, regularly brings crocolisk hides to James Halloran’s leatherworking business, though one tracker cannot always meet demand.",al={"who hunts crocs","einar hunter","menethil tanner hunters"},it="people"},{q="Where are these cured skins shipped?",a="James Halloran’s finished goods leave Menethil Harbor aboard merchant vessels bound for major ports and markets across the Eastern Kingdoms and beyond.",al={"crocolisk leather trade","menethil skin exports","where do skins go"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Young Crocolisk Skin?",a="It is the raw, supple hide harvested from juvenile crocolisks prowling the Wetlands marshes. Because the young beasts have not yet developed the thick, rigid scales of full-grown adults, their hides are far more pliable and prized by local leatherworkers.",al={"what is young crocolisk skin","young croc skin item","crocolisk skin meaning"},it="identity",add="2363e64c"},{q="Where does Young Crocolisk Skin come from?",a="These skins come directly from the young crocolisks dwelling in the sodden marshes surrounding Menethil Harbor. They are not crafted goods, but natural pelts skinned from hunted beasts before being cured and tanned into fine leather.",al={"young crocolisk skin source","where to get young crocolisk skin","who made young crocolisk skin"},it="origin",add="a9554702"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can stalk the muddy edges of the Wetlands for crocolisk hides to supply Menethil Harbor’s leather trade."},kw={"crocolisk","james halloran","leather","menethil harbor","skin","tanning","wetlands"},rel={"quest:484","npc:james-halloran","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:471","item:crocolisk-skin-classic","topic:hunter"},src={"Young Crocolisk Skin","Young Crocolisk Skins"}}
E["npc:ashlan-stonesmirk"] = {t="npc",n="Ashlan Stonesmirk",z="wetlands",s="At Dun Modr, Ashlan Stonesmirk watches the border with the regiment guarding the Thandol Span. The dwarven explosives expert keeps alert for dangers threatening Ironforge.",h="At Dun Modr, Ashlan Stonesmirk watches the border with the regiment guarding the Thandol Span.",sec={{t="An Expert on the Border",b="At Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands, Ashlan Stonesmirk serves the regiment guarding the Thandol Span. His knowledge of explosives makes him a useful contact when suspicious materials threaten dwarven defenses.",sp=0},{t="A Dark Threat Looms",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir finds suspicious powder near the Stonewrought Dam and sends it to Ashlan for examination. Ashlan identifies the powder as Seaforium and explains how to neutralize it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Ashlan Stonesmirk?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is stationed at Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands, near the Thandol Span.",al={"ashlan location","where is ashlan stonesmirk","ashlan stonesmirk loc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Ashlan Stonesmirk's role?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is a dwarven explosives expert with the regiment guarding Dun Modr and the Thandol Span. Hinderweir turns to him to identify suspicious powder found near the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"who is ashlan stonesmirk","ashlan purpose","what does ashlan do"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests does Ashlan offer?",a="Ashlan helps adventurers examine suspicious powder sent by Chief Engineer Hinderweir during 'A Dark Threat Looms'.",al={"ashlan quests","quests from ashlan stonesmirk"},gp=true},{q="Who is Ashlan Stonesmirk?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is a dwarven explosives expert stationed with the regiment at Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands.",al={"who is ashlan","ashlan stonesmirk lore","who is ashlan stonesmirk"},it="identity",add="0cdc60de"},{q="Whose side is Ashlan Stonesmirk on?",a="He serves Ironforge and the Alliance, helping defend the northern Wetlands and identify threats to dwarven works.",al={"ashlan stonesmirk faction","is ashlan alliance","who does ashlan stonesmirk serve"},it="side",add="c5f8e74c"},{q="Why is Ashlan Stonesmirk here?",a="Ashlan is stationed at Dun Modr, where his knowledge of explosives helps the dwarven regiment and travelers investigating danger to the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"why is ashlan in loch modan","ashlan stonesmirk camp purpose","why is ashlan near mogrosh"},it="why_here",add="82d01692"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Ashlan represents the skilled specialists who support Ironforge's soldiers along Khaz Modan's borders.",["faction:Alliance"]="Ashlan's work helps secure the strategic corridor connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands and northern Alliance territories."},kw={"a dark threat looms","ashlan","dun modr","ironforge","loch modan","stonesmirk"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","zone:lochmodan","quest:161","topic:dwarf"},src={"Ashlan Stonesmirk"}}
E["npc:captain-stoutfist"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Stoutfist",z="wetlands",s="At Menethil Harbor, Captain Stoutfist directs the defense against Dragonmaw attacks. The dwarf officer coordinates the garrison’s defenses and counterstrikes to keep the Alliance port from falling.",h="At Menethil Harbor, Captain Stoutfist directs the defense against Dragonmaw attacks.",sec={{t="Defender of Menethil",b="Menethil Harbor is the principal deepwater port linking Ironforge and Stormwind to the Wetlands and the sea beyond. Captain Stoutfist commands the town’s defense, guarding its docks, people, and garrison from the dangers around them. The marshlands are hazardous, but the greatest threat is an organized advance by renegade orcs.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Threat",b="The Dragonmaw clan has held strongholds in the Wetlands since the Second War and now presses toward the roads and mountain passes. By infiltrating Dun Algaz, the orcs threaten the overland route linking Loch Modan and Ironforge with Menethil Harbor. Stoutfist has too few troops, so he depends on Alliance volunteers sent by Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw to hold them back.",sp=0},{t="Striking at Nek'rosh",b="Captain Stoutfist leads a campaign against the orc camps rather than waiting for a siege. He directs allied forces to capture war banners near Whelgar's Excavation Site, sabotage Dragonmaw catapults preparing to attack, and kill Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, the clan’s ruthless local chieftain. Stoutfist seeks to break the orc offensive before Menethil Harbor is overwhelmed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist?",a="Captain Stoutfist commands the dwarf forces defending Menethil Harbor. He organizes the garrison’s defenses, weighs threats across the region, and recruits volunteers to drive back enemies threatening the port.",al={"captain stoutfist","stoutfist menethil","menethil captain"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Captain Stoutfist located?",a="Captain Stoutfist is stationed inside Menethil Harbor, the main Alliance hub on the Wetlands’ western coast.",al={"stoutfist location","where is captain stoutfist","find stoutfist"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist need outside help?",a="The local garrison is stretched thin across the Wetlands. Dragonmaw orcs have seized the mountain passes at Dun Algaz and are pressing toward town, leaving Stoutfist short of troops to strike back and guard the harbor at once.",al={"why stoutfist need help","menethil defense problems"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Nek'rosh Skullcrusher?",a="Nek'rosh Skullcrusher leads the Dragonmaw orcs operating in the Wetlands. Captain Stoutfist orders his death to disrupt the orcs’ coordination and protect Menethil Harbor from a full assault.",al={"who is nekrosh","nekrosh skullcrusher","dragonmaw boss wetlands"}},{q="How does Dun Algaz connect to Captain Stoutfist's mission?",a="Dun Algaz is the vital mountain pass linking Loch Modan and Ironforge to the Wetlands. When Dragonmaw orcs pushed into the pass, Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw warned that Menethil was in danger and sent adventurers to help Captain Stoutfist reinforce the harbor.",al={"dun algaz stoutfist","algaz gauntlet connection"}},{q="What threat do the Dragonmaw catapults pose?",a="Dragonmaw catapults could batter Menethil Harbor’s fortifications in a direct siege. Stoutfist directs champions to sabotage them before they reach firing range.",al={"nekroshs gambit catapults","dragonmaw catapults"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Captain Stoutfist on?",a="Captain Stoutfist serves the Alliance and the dwarven kingdom of Ironforge. Stationed at Menethil Harbor, he commands the town's garrison to safeguard this vital port town and protect travellers moving between the Wetlands and the mountains of Khaz Modan.",al={"captain stoutfist faction","is stoutfist alliance","who does stoutfist serve"},it="side",add="40162abd"},{q="What does Captain Stoutfist want?",a="Captain Stoutfist wants to eliminate the encroaching Dragonmaw orc threat once and for all. He seeks to seize their war banners from the Dragonmaw encampment, burn the catapults Nek'rosh built to lay siege to Menethil Harbor, and see their chieftain, Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, slain to keep Menethil Harbor secure.",al={"captain stoutfist goals","what does stoutfist need","stoutfist objective"},it="wants",add="31290b24"},{q="Why is Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor?",a="Captain Stoutfist is stationed in Menethil Harbor as the commander tasked with defending the port. With the strategic mountain passes at Dun Algaz choked by hostile Dragonmaw orcs, he remains here to rally soldiers and mercenaries to safeguard the harbor from destruction.",al={"why is stoutfist in wetlands","captain stoutfist role menethil","why is stoutfist here"},it="why_here",add="6891235c"},{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist tied to?",a="Captain Stoutfist coordinates with fellow Alliance defenders across Khaz Modan, receiving reinforcements routed by Valstag Ironjaw. He commands the garrison at Menethil Keep and relies on traveling Alliance champions to take the fight directly to the Dragonmaw clan.",al={"captain stoutfist allies","who does captain stoutfist work with","captain stoutfist connections"},it="ties",add="2b51270f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Captain Stoutfist defends one of the Alliance’s most important maritime hubs, keeping naval routes open between Khaz Modan, Stormwind, and distant outposts.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Ironforge’s military resolve in Stoutfist, entrusted with guarding vital lowland infrastructure far below the mountain peaks.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you’ll find Stoutfist a blunt tactician who favors bold strikes over cautious fortification, sending warriors to destroy enemy artillery and leadership."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","dun algaz","dwarf","ironforge","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:474","quest:465","quest:464","quest:473","npc:valstag-ironjaw","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:wetlands"},src={"Captain Stoutfist"}}
E["npc:einar-stonegrip"] = {t="npc",n="Einar Stonegrip",z="wetlands",s="Along the Wetlands crossroads, Einar Stonegrip keeps to the road and sends his goods to town with travelers. He avoids Menethil Harbor, where his estranged wife lives.",h="Along the Wetlands crossroads, Einar Stonegrip keeps to the road and sends his goods to town with travelers.",sec={{t="A Trapper at the Crossroads",b="Einar Stonegrip hunts crocolisks where the roads meet in the Wetlands. The crossroads link Dun Algaz, Dun Modr, and Menethil Harbor. He sells their sturdy hides to leatherworkers and merchants along the coast. Though rugged enough to wrestle reptiles from the mire, Einar is embroiled in a bitter falling-out with his wife, Sida. He stays on the road and asks travelers to carry his bundles of skins to his trading partner, James Halloran, rather than enter Menethil Harbor himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Einar Stonegrip?",a="Einar Stonegrip hunts crocolisks at the Wetlands crossroads and sells their hides in Menethil Harbor.",al={"who is einar","einar stonegrip lore","wetlands dwarf crossroads"},it="identity"},{q="Why won't Einar deliver his own goods to Menethil Harbor?",a="Einar avoids Menethil Harbor because he is on terribly bad terms with his wife, Sida, who lives there. He stays in the swamplands and pays passing couriers to carry his goods.",al={"why doesn't einar go to town","einar stonegrip wife","why hire adventurers"},it="why_here"},{q="Who does Einar work with in Menethil Harbor?",a="Einar gathers crocolisk skins for James Halloran, a merchant in Menethil Harbor who sells leather goods.",al={"einar business partner","who buys einar skins","james halloran connection"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Einar Stonegrip on?",a="Einar is loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. Stationed out along the crossroads of the Wetlands, he works alongside his fellow mountaineers and provides trade goods for the harbor settlement of Menethil.",al={"einar stonegrip faction","who does einar stonegrip serve","einar alliance or horde"},it="side",add="2e6b6b46"},{q="What does Einar Stonegrip want?",a="Einar wants to keep up his business supplying crocolisk skins to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor without having to go there himself. He is eager to find passing travelers willing to deliver the bundles on his behalf so he can delay having to face his wife, Sida.",al={"what does einar want","einar stonegrip goal","einar stonegrip quest motive"},it="wants",add="61290d18"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize Einar's rugged self-reliance. His troubles with his wife keep him in the soggy marshes instead of a warm tavern.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you may pass Einar's roadside post on the way between Ironforge and Menethil Harbor. He offers courier work along the Alliance supply routes."},kw={"crocolisk","einar stonegrip","james halloran","menethil harbor","sida","skins","trapper","wetlands"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","npc:sida","quest:469","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:dwarf","subzone:dun-algaz","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Einar Stonegrip"}}
E["npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons"] = {t="npc",n="First Mate Fitzsimmons",z="wetlands",s="Outside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern, First Mate Fitzsimmons drinks through the days. Once first mate of the Wave Mistress in Kul Tiras's Third Fleet, he is its sole known living survivor after the fleet's destruction in the Second War. Now he seeks travelers willing to face the restless spirits of his drowned comrades.",h="Outside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern, First Mate Fitzsimmons drinks through the days.",sec={{t="A Broken Sailor",b="Outside the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, First Mate Fitzsimmons drinks alone. His unwashed stench keeps many patrons away, and most see only a broken old sailor drowning his memories. Those who sit and listen hear how a proud fleet fell to fire and claw.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the Third Fleet",b="During the Second War, Fitzsimmons served aboard the Wave Mistress as first mate. The ship sailed with Kul Tiras's Third Fleet to fight the Horde. Off the Wetlands coast, Dragonmaw orcs ambushed the fleet with enslaved red dragons and burned its ships. The vessels broke apart and sank. Fitzsimmons alone managed to reach shore alive.",sp=0},{t="The Lingering Curse",b="First Mate Fitzsimmons survived the dragonfire, but his former crewmates did not find rest. Their ships, remembered as the Lost Fleet, now hold cursed undead sailors trapped in watery graves. Haunted by guilt and terror, Fitzsimmons asks travelers to put the sailors down and recover ancient relics that might lift the evil binding their souls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?",a="First Mate Fitzsimmons is an old Kul Tiran sailor who once served as first mate of the Wave Mistress. He survived the destruction of Kul Tiras's Third Fleet in the Second War and now drinks outside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern.",al={"fitzsimmons lore","who is fitzsimmons","first mate fitzsimmons"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to his ship?",a="During the Second War, enslaved red dragons flown by Dragonmaw orcs ambushed the Wave Mistress and the rest of the Third Fleet. The vessels burned and broke apart on the reef off the Wetlands coast.",al={"what happened to wave mistress","third fleet destruction","why did his ship sink"},it="history"},{q="Where is the Lost Fleet located?",a="The Lost Fleet's shattered hulls lie submerged along the rocky Wetlands coast north of Menethil Harbor. Murlocs and the restless spirits of drowned sailors guard them.",al={"lost fleet location","where are the sunken ships","fitzsimmons ship location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does he want adventurers to fight his old crew?",a="The drowned sailors of the Third Fleet rose as cursed, tormented undead. Fitzsimmons seeks travelers to put them to rest and recover the artifacts that keep their souls shackled.",al={"cursed crew quest lore","why kill his crew"},it="wants"},{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="The Eye of Paleth is an ancient, potent artifact carried aboard the Third Fleet. Its dark power is tied to the curse afflicting the sunken sailors, and recovering it is crucial to granting the drowned fleet peace.",al={"eye of paleth","paleth relic"},it="item"},{q="Why does Fitzsimmons smell so bad?",a="Fitzsimmons lost everything when his fleet went down and now lives in drunken neglect outside the Deepwater Tavern. He wears sea-soaked rags and rarely washes.",al={"why does fitzsimmons smell","fitzsimmons stench"}},{q="Whose side is First Mate Fitzsimmons on?",a="Fitzsimmons aligns with the Alliance through his past loyalties to Kul Tiras and the Third Fleet. Today, however, he serves no nation or lord. He is simply a broken sailor drinking his days away outside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern, relying on passing Alliance adventurers to clean up the cursed remnants of his past.",al={"fitzsimmons faction","who does fitzsimmons serve","is fitzsimmons alliance"},it="side",add="c1574e2a"},{q="Why is First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor?",a="Fitzsimmons ended up in Menethil Harbor because he is the sole survivor of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet, which was destroyed by orc dragon riders along the Wetlands coast during the Second War. Haunted by the gruesome fate of his comrades, he has retreated to the steps outside the Deepwater Tavern to drown his trauma in liquor.",al={"why is fitzsimmons here","fitzsimmons menethil harbor why","why is fitzsimmons outside tavern"},it="why_here",add="468babc7"},{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons tied to?",a="Fitzsimmons was the first mate aboard the Wave Mistress, a Kul Tiras vessel that served in the Third Fleet. He remains closely tied to his old captain and shipmates, who now haunt the shipwrecks off the coast as cursed undead, bound by dark relics like the Eye of Paleth.",al={"fitzsimmons connections","fitzsimmons ship","fitzsimmons crew"},it="ties",add="786aa53e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Fitzsimmons recalls a tragic chapter in Alliance naval history and the losses suffered against the Horde's enslaved dragon armada.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share a kinship with Fitzsimmons, a veteran of Kul Tiras. His people made great sacrifices to defend Lordaeron during the Second War."},kw={"deepwater tavern","eye of paleth","first mate fitzsimmons","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","lost fleet","menethil harbor","third fleet","wave mistress"},rel={"quest:288","quest:289","quest:290","quest:292","subzone:deepwater-tavern","subzone:lost-fleet","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:kul-tiras"},src={"First Mate Fitzsimmons"}}
E["npc:foggy-mackreel"] = {t="npc",n="Foggy MacKreel",z="wetlands",s="On the broken Thandol Span, Foggy MacKreel worries about a moonshine delivery bound for Southshore. Stranded on ruined lower masonry above a dizzying drop, the dwarf keeps his mind on the task.",h="On the broken Thandol Span, Foggy MacKreel worries about a moonshine delivery bound for Southshore.",sec={{t="Stranded on the Span",b="Foggy MacKreel waits on broken pylons beneath the Thandol Span, calm despite his dangerous perch. Dark Iron sabotage and war damage shattered the bridge between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. MacKreel gives little thought to rescue; he wants his potent moonshine delivered to the patrons of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He hires passing travelers nimble enough to reach his ledge and finish the delivery for him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foggy MacKreel?",a="Foggy MacKreel is a dwarf courier stranded on ruined stone pillars beneath the broken Thandol Span. The drop does not trouble him; he is focused on getting his moonshine delivered.",al={"foggy mackreel","who is foggy","mackreel npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Foggy MacKreel?",a="Foggy MacKreel waits on a stone platform midway down the broken central span of the Thandol Span. Reach him by carefully jumping down from the bridge structure on the Arathi Highlands side.",al={"where is foggy mackreel","foggy mackreel location","how to find mackreel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Foggy MacKreel down there?",a="Foggy MacKreel became stuck in the Thandol Span wreckage during his travels. His main concern is finding someone to carry his moonshine the rest of the way to Southshore.",al={"why is foggy stranded","how did mackreel get there","why is he on the bridge"},it="why_here"},{q="What quest does Foggy MacKreel offer?",a="Foggy MacKreel offers MacKreel's Moonshine, asking travelers to take a jug of his potent brew to the tavern in Southshore across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"foggy quest","mackreel moonshine quest","what quest does foggy give"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Foggy MacKreel on?",a="Foggy MacKreel is an Alliance-aligned dwarf. Even stranded precariously along the damaged ruins of the Thandol Span, his loyalties and dealings lie squarely with his kin and fellow Alliance settlements, most notably aiming to get his potent brew north into the hands of the folk holding Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"foggy mackreel faction","is foggy mackreel alliance","foggy mackreel side"},it="side",add="28a25d1f"},{q="What does Foggy MacKreel want?",a="Foggy MacKreel wants his special batch of moonshine safely carried to Southshore. Despite being trapped on a shattered pillar beneath the bridge, he shows surprisingly little care for his own perilous situation, remaining entirely preoccupied with ensuring his brew reaches its destination in Hillsbrad rather than plotting an immediate rescue.",al={"foggy mackreel motive","what does foggy want","foggy mackreel goal"},it="wants",add="c1253653"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize MacKreel's stubborn grit and peculiar priorities: he values delivering strong liquor on time above being marooned over a fatal chasm.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance courier traveling between Ironforge and Southshore, you may cross paths with Foggy and carry his stranded cargo to help a fellow subject of the Alliance."},kw={"arathi","foggy","mackreel","moonshine","southshore","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:647","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:southshore","zone:arathi","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Foggy MacKreel"}}
E["npc:harlo-barnaby"] = {t="npc",n="Harlo Barnaby",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Harbor, Harlo Barnaby bears the wounds of Dun Modr's fall. The dwarven refugee escaped the Dark Iron assault and warns travelers of the tragedy in the northern marshes.",h="In Menethil Harbor, Harlo Barnaby bears the wounds of Dun Modr's fall.",sec={{t="Escape from Dun Modr",b="Harlo Barnaby fled Dun Modr when Dark Iron dwarves struck the northern stronghold without warning. In the chaos, a stray axe hit him square in the back. The blow knocked him unconscious, yet he survived the trek across the marshland. Harlo awoke bandaged in Menethil Harbor, alive but marked by his wounds and memories of the massacre. He cannot return to Dun Modr, so he urges Alliance adventurers to investigate the smoking ruins of his former home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Harlo Barnaby?",a="Harlo Barnaby survived the Dark Iron assault on Dun Modr and now lives in Menethil Harbor. He is an Ironforge dwarf.",al={"harlo barnaby","who is harlo","menethil harbor dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="How did Harlo Barnaby end up in Menethil Harbor?",a="Harlo Barnaby fled Dun Modr and was struck in the back by a thrown axe. He lost consciousness during his retreat and woke in Menethil Harbor, where local healers cared for him.",al={"how did harlo get here","harlo barnaby back injury"},it="why_here"},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dark Iron dwarves pushing south from the Thandol Span overran and devastated Dun Modr. The attack wiped out the local dwarven defenders and drove survivors into the wetlands.",al={"dun modr fall","what happened at dun modr"}},{q="Whose side is Harlo Barnaby on?",a="Harlo Barnaby is loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. As a survivor of the catastrophic assault on the northern outpost of Dun Modr, he stands with his fellow Bronzebeard dwarves and seeks brave Alliance adventurers to help deal with the Dark Iron invaders who overrun the northern pass.",al={"harlo barnaby faction","who does harlo barnaby serve","is harlo barnaby alliance"},it="side",add="2ef93137"},{q="What does Harlo Barnaby want?",a="Still nursing his wounds, Harlo wants you to carry news and assistance regarding the fall of Dun Modr. He narrowly escaped with his life when the Dark Iron dwarves breached the northern redoubt, and he seeks capable fighters to bring retribution to the traitors and reclaim what was lost.",al={"harlo barnaby motive","what does harlo want you to do","harlo barnaby quest goal"},it="wants",add="4a6adfe0"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see in Harlo a living reminder of the bloody clan war against the treacherous Dark Irons, who seek to sever Khaz Modan from the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Dun Modr's fall threatens the critical land bridge between the marshlands and Arathi. Harlo's warnings matter to Alliance forces."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","harlo barnaby","menethil harbor","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:dun-modr","quest:472","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Harlo Barnaby"}}
E["npc:james-halloran"] = {t="npc",n="James Halloran",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Harbor, James Halloran makes a living tanning crocolisk hides. Passing travelers and nearby trade channels help him gather raw skins and carry finished leather to buyers across the eastern continents.",h="In Menethil Harbor, James Halloran makes a living tanning crocolisk hides.",sec={{t="A Tanner in the Marshes",b="James Halloran lives and works in Menethil Harbor, earning his living from the marsh just outside town. The dangerous bogs provide crocolisk skins, which he turns into fine leather through rare craftsmanship. Nearby trade channels carry his finished goods to buyers across Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Hides, Apprentices, and Daily Trade",b="Halloran tends his curing vats and trade arrangements near the marsh, where danger is constant. He hires hardy travelers to skin young marsh beasts and handle routine deliveries between his work site and nearby settlements. Their help keeps his leather craft supplied while he manages the tanning and trade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a human tanner in Menethil Harbor who hunts and skins the region’s crocolisks, then cures their tough hides into leather for buyers across the world.",al={"james halloran","halloran","who is halloran","wetlands tanner"},it="identity"},{q="Where does James Halloran sell his leather?",a="Halloran ships his fine leather throughout Azeroth. He relies on the maritime trade passing through Menethil Harbor to carry his wares across the seas.",al={"halloran leather trade","where do crocolisk skins go","halloran business"}},{q="Why does Halloran need adventurers to collect young crocolisk skins?",a="Tanning and curing keep Halloran busy at his workshop, so he hires traveling adventurers to cull local marsh crocolisks and strip their hides. Their work gives him a steady supply of raw material without leaving his workshop.",al={"why kill young crocolisks","young crocolisk skins quest","crocolisk hides halloran"},it="wants"},{q="What is Halloran's connection to Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor is Halloran’s trade and supply hub. He relies on the harbor and its shipping lanes to send cured hides to distant markets and keep his tanning business viable.",al={"halloran menethil","halloran port connection","does halloran live in menethil"},it="ties"},{q="Where can James Halloran be found?",a="James Halloran lives and works in Menethil Harbor, on the western coast of the Wetlands, with crocolisk marshes just outside town.",al={"halloran location","where is james halloran","find halloran"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Halloran have an apprentice?",a="Yes. Halloran sent his apprentice, whom he thinks of like a son, into the marshes to skin giant crocolisks. The young man was mauled and lost a leg. While he recovers, Halloran relies on hardy travelers to gather the skins his trade needs.",al={"halloran apprentice","apprentice duties halloran","who works for halloran"}},{q="Whose side is James Halloran on?",a="James Halloran is aligned with the Alliance. A human craftsman working out of the Wetlands, he maintains ties with the port town of Menethil Harbor to supply his goods across Alliance lands.",al={"is halloran alliance","james halloran faction","who does halloran serve"},it="side",add="21c95e2f"},{q="Why is James Halloran here in the Wetlands?",a="Halloran makes his living as a tanner and trapper. The bogs and waterways of the Wetlands are teeming with crocolisks, providing him with a steady supply of hides that he cures and exports far and wide.",al={"why is halloran in wetlands","james halloran purpose","why is halloran here"},it="why_here",add="b76d5522"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Halloran’s trade sustains the Alliance’s commercial presence in the rugged Wetlands, supplying valuable crafted leather to towns across the kingdom.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may find common ground with Halloran. His livelihood depends on stalking and harvesting the Wetlands’ aggressive reptilian predators."},kw={"crocolisk","halloran","james halloran","leatherworking","menethil harbor","tanner","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:484","quest:469","quest:471"},src={"James Halloran"}}
E["npc:longbraid-the-grim"] = {t="npc",n="Longbraid the Grim",z="wetlands",s="Outside fallen Dun Modr, Longbraid the Grim keeps watch over the northern Wetlands. He mourns his brother and the loss of the Thandol Span, while leading the surviving dwarves against the Dark Iron clan.",h="Outside fallen Dun Modr, Longbraid the Grim keeps watch over the northern Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Bitter Watch",b="Longbraid the Grim rallies the dwarven garrison near the bridge to the Arathi Highlands. The Dark Iron clan seized Dun Modr in a sudden assault that devastated the defenders. Longbraid's brother died during the siege of the Thandol Span. Grief and hatred keep Longbraid at the northern boundary, where he directs travelers and surviving mountaineers in strikes against the Dark Iron advance.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Longbraid also directs dwarven operations across the Wetlands. He sent soldiers to escort Prospector Whelgar into the marshlands and works to reclaim Dun Modr's lost fortifications. He vows retribution against the Dark Iron saboteurs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Longbraid the Grim?",a="Longbraid the Grim commands the dwarves stationed outside Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands. He leads the local Alliance resistance against the Dark Iron dwarfs who overran the area.",al={"who is longbraid","longbraid identity","dun modr dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Longbraid called 'the Grim'?",a="Longbraid earned his grim demeanor when his brother died in the Dark Iron attack on the Thandol Span. Since then, he has pursued vengeance for his fallen kin.",al={"why is he grim","longbraid brother","longbraid backstory"},it="fame"},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="The Dark Iron clan overran and occupied Dun Modr after ambushing its dwarven garrison. They tried to sever the Thandol Span and cut off the main route between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands.",al={"fall of dun modr","what happened to the bridge","thandol span attack"}},{q="What is Longbraid's connection to Prospector Whelgar?",a="Longbraid sent soldiers from his forces to accompany and protect Prospector Whelgar as the dwarven excavation team explored deeper into the hazardous Wetlands.",al={"whelgar longbraid","merrin letter"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Longbraid the Grim on?",a="Longbraid the Grim serves Ironforge and the Alliance. Stationed in the northern Wetlands, he commands dwarven forces attempting to hold the line against the Dark Iron clan that has seized Dun Modr and damaged the Thandol Span.",al={"longbraid faction","who does longbraid serve","longbraid alliance"},it="side",add="d54d2b61"},{q="What does Longbraid the Grim want?",a="Longbraid seeks vengeance against the Dark Iron dwarves who overran Dun Modr and killed his brother during the assault on the Thandol Span. He wants their forces broken and the northern border secured for Ironforge.",al={"longbraid the grim goal","what does longbraid want","longbraid motives"},it="wants",add="40b05609"},{q="Why is Longbraid the Grim here?",a="Longbraid is encamped just outside Dun Modr in the far north of the Wetlands to monitor the ruins and coordinate the defense. Following the brutal Dark Iron invasion that shattered the town and the span, he remains on the frontline to direct counterattacks against the encroaching enemy.",al={"why is longbraid in wetlands","why is longbraid outside dun modr","longbraid location reason"},it="why_here",add="0c91256b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Ironforge dwarves, Longbraid embodies the fierce blood feud with their Dark Iron cousins, who struck at their northern gateway.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Longbraid guards Khaz Modan's northern gate and fights to reopen the land route across the Thandol Span into Arathi."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","longbraid","thandol span","the grim","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","topic:dark-iron-clan","quest:472","quest:304","quest:378","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands"},src={"Longbraid the Grim"}}
E["npc:merrin-rockweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Merrin Rockweaver",z="wetlands",s="On a ridge above Whelgar's Excavation Site, Merrin Rockweaver waits with the survivors. A raptor infestation drove them from the dig, where she represented the Explorers' League.",h="On a ridge above Whelgar's Excavation Site, Merrin Rockweaver waits with the survivors.",sec={{t="Displaced by the Dig",b="Merrin Rockweaver came to the Wetlands for the Ironforge Explorers' League, seeking ancient Titan secrets beneath the muck. The expedition fell apart when the large bones the crew unearthed drew raptors to the dig. The beasts swarmed the trenches, and Merrin and the surviving crew fled, leaving their equipment, notes, and progress behind. Now Merrin is trapped with a few survivors on a bluff overlooking the overrun ruins.",sp=0},{t="Salvaging the Operation",b="The survivors on the bluff still hope to save what they can of the expedition. Ormer Ironbraid plans vengeance against the beasts, while Prospector Whelgar seeks tablet fragments in the raptor-infested trenches. Merrin worries about her husband Tarrel, who has heard nothing from her in weeks. A scout Longbraid sent to find the team can carry word of their plight back to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is a dwarf archaeologist with the Explorers' League of Ironforge. She worked at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands before raptors overran the operation.",al={"merrin rockweaver lore","who is merrin","wetlands dwarf merrin"},it="identity"},{q="Why is she trapped above the dig site?",a="Raptors drawn by the large bones the team uncovered overwhelmed the dig, and many lives were lost. Ormer Ironbraid defended Merrin and Prospector Whelgar as they fled to a nearby bluff, where they remain trapped.",al={"why is merrin at the retreat","whelgars retreat merrin","what happened to her camp"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Merrin need help with?",a="Merrin needs someone to carry a letter about the disaster to her husband Tarrel. He has worried since her letters stopped arriving.",al={"merrin quests","merrin rockweaver tasks","tooling around lore"},it="wants"},{q="What was the expedition trying to find?",a="The Wetlands expedition sought ancient artifacts tied to dwarven ancestry and the mysterious Titan relics hidden throughout Khaz Modan.",al={"what are they digging for","excavation site purpose"}},{q="Whose side is Merrin Rockweaver on?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is firmly aligned with the Ironforge dwarves and the Alliance. As an active surveyor and member of the Explorers' League, her loyalties lie with the scholars and excavators dispatched from Ironforge to uncover their people's ancient origins across Khaz Modan.",al={"merrin rockweaver faction","merrin rockweaver allegiance","who does merrin serve"},it="side",add="86a5e24a"},{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver tied to?",a="Merrin accompanies Prospector Whelgar's expedition at the excavation site in the Wetlands. Ormer Ironbraid helps defend their camp from the raptors surrounding it.",al={"merrin rockweaver connections","merrin rockweaver associates","who is merrin working with"},it="ties",add="f33c6ea8"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can help Merrin protect Titan relics and historical records the Explorers' League risked their lives to uncover.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can help Merrin safeguard Ironforge's research presence in the Wetlands and strengthen the Alliance's tenuous foothold in the wild marshland."},kw={"explorers' league","merrin rockweaver","raptors","tooling around","wetlands","whelgar's excavation site","whelgar's retreat"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","topic:explorers-league","quest:305","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Merrin Rockweaver"}}
E["npc:ormer-ironbraid"] = {t="npc",n="Ormer Ironbraid",z="wetlands",s="At Whelgar's Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid faces a raptor threat that has driven the dwarven workers away. He remains at the dig, seeking allies to reclaim it.",h="At Whelgar's Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid faces a raptor threat that has driven the dwarven workers away.",sec={{t="A Dig Derailed",b="Ormer Ironbraid came to the Wetlands with the dwarven effort to uncover Titan relics and ancient history at Whelgar's Excavation Site. The work stirred packs of fierce Wetlands raptors, or at least drew them to the dig. Now beasts prowl among the ruins where Ormer's team hoped to study ancient earthenware and tablets. The raptors have disrupted their work, and Ormer's anger toward them runs deep.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Feud with Claws",b="Ormer will not abandon the dig, though he cannot drive the raptors out alone. He asks passing travelers to kill the beasts, beginning with smaller ones and taking on larger, fiercer raptors in turn. Reclaiming the excavation means recovering the artifacts, but the fight has become personal: Ormer wants vengeance for the work the raptors disrupted and the dwarven pride wounded by their presence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer Ironbraid oversees dwarven research at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands. The dig studies ancient ruins buried in the marsh.",al={"who is ormer","ormer ironbraid","ormer wetlands"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer stands on the overlook above Whelgar's Excavation Site in the southern Wetlands cliffs, just east of the main road toward Loch Modan.",al={"ormer location","where is ormer","find ormer ironbraid"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Ormer hate raptors so much?",a="Raptor packs overran the excavation, drove out the dwarven workers, and halted the archaeological work. Ormer took the disruption as a personal insult and wants payback.",al={"why raptors","ormer raptors","ormers revenge lore"},it="motive"},{q="What is Whelgar's Excavation Site?",a="Whelgar's Excavation Site is an archaeological dig founded by Ironforge dwarves to uncover ancient Titan and earthen ruins beneath the Wetlands. Aggressive wildlife has made the site a dangerous battleground.",al={"whelgars excavation site","what is this dig site","wetlands dig site"},it="place"},{q="What quests does Ormer offer?",a="Ormer offers a three-part chain called 'Ormer's Revenge,' asking travelers to kill ever-larger raptors at the excavation.",al={"ormer quests","strike the earth","ormers revenge quest"},gp=true},{q="Is Ormer affiliated with the Explorers' League?",a="Yes. Ormer works on behalf of Ironforge's archaeological efforts to uncover the dwarves' Titan heritage, like many dwarves excavating ancient ruins across Khaz Modan.",al={"ormer explorers league","is ormer an archaeologist"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Ormer Ironbraid on?",a="Ormer is a loyal dwarf of Ironforge aligned with the Alliance and the dwarven expeditionary efforts across Khaz Modan. While his immediate focus is surviving out in the wilds of the Wetlands and securing the dig site, he stands firmly alongside his kin and the Alliance.",al={"ormer faction","is ormer alliance","ormer ironbraid allegiance"},it="side",add="97454981"},{q="What does Ormer Ironbraid want?",a="Ormer wants nothing more than to see the vicious raptors infesting Whelgar's Excavation Site wiped out. The beasts overran the expedition's diggings and drove the excavators away, and he seeks vengeance and retribution against the creatures so the site can be reclaimed.",al={"ormer goals","what does ormer want","ormer revenge why"},it="wants",add="f4da8dc2"},{q="Why is Ormer Ironbraid here in the Wetlands?",a="Ormer came to the Wetlands as part of the dwarven archaeological expedition stationed at Whelgar's Excavation Site. Instead of calmly unearthing ancient treasures, however, he found himself trapped in a bitter fight for survival after native raptors swarmed the dig.",al={"why is ormer at the excavation site","ormer ironbraid wetlands purpose","why is ormer here"},it="why_here",add="60616fd2"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Ormer's refusal to yield the ancient grounds to a pack of overgrown lizards speaks to dwarven tenacity.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Ormer secures the southern Wetlands road and supports Ironforge's archaeological work.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can bring your tracking and beast-slaying skills to Ormer's fight against some of Khaz Modan's fiercest raptors."},kw={"dwarf","excavation","explorers league","ironbraid","ormer","raptors","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","quest:294","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Ormer Ironbraid"}}
E["npc:prospector-whelgar"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Whelgar",z="wetlands",s="At Whelgar's Excavation Site, Prospector Whelgar's search for titan relics has stalled. Vicious raptors overran the dig, and he seeks hardy adventurers to recover ancient artifacts.",h="At Whelgar's Excavation Site, Prospector Whelgar's search for titan relics has stalled.",sec={{t="A Dig Under Siege",b="Prospector Whelgar leads a dwarven dig in the Wetlands. His camp, Whelgar's Excavation Site, lies east of Menethil Harbor, where he searches for the history of the dwarven race. Ancient stone relics once filled the valley, but territorial raptors drove his team into hiding. Whelgar refuses to leave his duty unfinished. He still hopes to recover valuable relics, including the Goaz Stone, before predators or rival scoundrels ruin the site.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Whelgar?",a="Prospector Whelgar leads an Ironforge dwarf expedition in the Wetlands. East of Menethil Harbor, he oversees a dig where he studies relics from the dawn of dwarven history.",al={"whelgar","who is whelgar","prospector whelgar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Prospector Whelgar?",a="You can find Prospector Whelgar sheltering on a ridge above Whelgar's Excavation Site, east of Menethil Harbor and southwest of Dun Modr in the Wetlands.",al={"whelgar location","where is whelgar","whelgar wetlands map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Whelgar having trouble at the dig site?",a="Fierce native raptors have overrun the dig, killing or scattering Whelgar's crew and forcing him into a defensive pocket. He cannot continue unearthing relics without protection.",al={"raptors excavation","what happened to whelgar dig","whelgars excavation raptors"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Goaz Stone?",a="The Goaz Stone is an ancient artifact uncovered among the ruins at Whelgar's excavation site. Whelgar is working to translate its inscriptions to learn more about the forgotten origins and ancient history of the dwarven people.",al={"goaz stone","what is the goaz stone","uncovering the past relic"},it="item"},{q="Whose side is Prospector Whelgar on?",a="Prospector Whelgar is firmly loyal to Ironforge and the Alliance. Like his fellow dwarven prospectors, his expeditions are carried out in service of dwarven heritage and the Explorers' League, unearthing ancient history on behalf of his people.",al={"whelgar faction","is whelgar alliance","who does whelgar serve"},it="side",add="430ccc65"},{q="What does Prospector Whelgar want?",a="Whelgar wants to safely conduct his excavations and uncover relics of the past, most notably understanding ancient artifacts like the Goaz Stone. However, local threats like the raptors overrunning his dig site continually thwart his archaeological work.",al={"what does whelgar need","whelgar goal","whelgar objective"},it="wants",add="3be180e4"},{q="Why is Prospector Whelgar here in the Wetlands?",a="He traveled to the Wetlands to lead excavations into the region's ancient ruins. He established an excavation site here to unearth artifacts of dwarven antiquity, though vicious wildlife and native perils have severely disrupted his expedition.",al={"why is whelgar in wetlands","whelgar excavation purpose"},it="why_here",add="3a0c9faf"},{q="Who is Prospector Whelgar tied to?",a="Whelgar is tied to the dwarven archaeological initiatives out of Ironforge, working alongside fellow dwarven prospectors and researchers who investigate Titan and ancient titan-forged ruins throughout Khaz Modan and beyond.",al={"whelgar organization","whelgar affiliation","who does whelgar report to"},it="ties",add="bbf3af84"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Whelgar's mission serves the Explorers' League and King Magni Bronzebeard's search into the titan roots of the dwarven race.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find rich mineral veins in the craggy ridges around Whelgar's dig site. Raptors also roam the area and plague his team."},kw={"dwarf","excavation site","explorers league","goaz stone","prospector whelgar","uncovering the past","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","quest:299","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf","quest:463"},src={"Prospector Whelgar"}}
E["npc:red-jack-flint"] = {t="npc",n="Red Jack Flint",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Keep, Red Jack Flint connects sailors with travelers bound across the sea. He is a seasoned human mariner and crew member of the Maiden's Virtue, helping travelers find passage and contacts toward Kalimdor.",h="In Menethil Keep, Red Jack Flint connects sailors with travelers bound across the sea.",sec={{t="A Sailor in Menethil Keep",b="Red Jack Flint is a seasoned sailor in Menethil Keep. A crewman of the Maiden's Virtue, he knows the sea routes from Khaz Modan to distant shores. He also directs capable travelers to allies across the Great Sea, including Fiora Longears in Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Red Jack Flint?",a="Red Jack Flint is a human sailor aboard the Maiden's Virtue. From Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor, he helps travelers connect with contacts across the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",al={"who is flint","red jack flint lore","what does flint do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Red Jack Flint be found?",a="Red Jack Flint can be found inside Menethil Keep, the stone fortress defending Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"red jack flint location","where is flint","find red jack flint"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What ship does Red Jack Flint sail on?",a="Red Jack Flint serves aboard the Maiden's Virtue, a merchant vessel sailing from Menethil Harbor.",al={"flints ship","what ship is red jack on","maidens virtue"}},{q="Who does Red Jack Flint send travelers to see?",a="Red Jack Flint directs travelers to Fiora Longears, his partner across the sea in the port of Theramore.",al={"flint quest","fiora longears connection","where does flint send you"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Red Jack Flint on?",a="Red Jack Flint stands with the Alliance. Stationed among the guards and mariners of Menethil Harbor, he offers guidance and contacts to Alliance travelers moving between the Eastern Kingdoms and the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"red jack flint faction","is red jack flint alliance","red jack flint allegiance"},it="side",add="1faeb3cc"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler sailing from Khaz Modan, you can rely on sailors like Red Jack Flint to connect you with outposts along Kalimdor's northern coast."},kw={"fiora longears","maidens virtue","menethil harbor","menethil keep","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:1132","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Red Jack Flint"}}
E["npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden"] = {t="npc",n="Rethiel the Greenwarden",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Rethiel the Greenwarden calls travelers to the Green Belt. He seeks help against threats that disturb the marsh's uneasy balance.",h="In the Wetlands, Rethiel the Greenwarden calls travelers to the Green Belt.",sec={{t="Tending the Wounds",b="Rethiel asks sympathetic travelers to ease the Wetlands' suffering. He urges them to hunt the destructive Mosshide gnolls that ravage wildlife and take the crude flints they use to burn the marsh's living trees. He also calls for the diseased fen creepers festering in the marsh waters to be thinned. Rethiel hopes these efforts will bring peace back to the wounded soil.",sp=0},{t="Guardian of the Marsh",b="Rethiel watches over the marsh from the damp thickets of the Green Belt. His towering form is made of moss, peat, and primal plant life. Unlike the bog beasts that wander the marsh as aggressive predators, Rethiel is conscious and speaks with sorrow. He feels the Wetlands as a living ecosystem, suffering under foreign predation and corruption.",sp=1,bt={"q463.2"}}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is a sentient bog beast in the Green Belt of the Wetlands. Unlike the mindless creatures of his kind, he speaks with mortals and protects the marsh.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel lore","bog beast npc wetlands"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q463.2"}},{q="Where can I find Rethiel?",a="Rethiel can be found in the Green Belt within the Wetlands, northeast of Dun Algaz.",al={"rethiel location","where is rethiel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Rethiel want travelers to help him?",a="Rethiel senses the marsh suffering under invasive threats. He asks travelers to confront destructive Mosshide gnoll bands, take the crude flints they use to set marsh trees ablaze, and thin diseased fen creepers, bringing relief to the land.",al={"why rethiel gives quests","rethiel goal","what does rethiel want"},it="wants"},{q="Are all bog beasts sentient like Rethiel?",a="Most bog beasts across Azeroth act on hostile instinct and lack higher intellect. Rethiel is exceptional: his deep natural attunement gives him sapience and speech.",al={"can bog beasts talk","intelligent bog beasts","why can rethiel speak"},sp=1,bt={"q463.2"}},{q="What threats does Rethiel focus on?",a="Rethiel focuses on curbing aggressive Mosshide gnolls, taking away their crude flints used to burn living wood, and purging diseased fen creepers festering in the marsh.",al={"rethiel quests","rethiel enemies","threats to wetlands rethiel"},it="threat"},{q="Is Rethiel aligned with the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Rethiel is friendly to the Alliance and hostile to the Horde. He cares for the land and calls on Alliance travelers willing to mend the marsh.",al={"is rethiel alliance","rethiel faction","can horde talk to rethiel"},it="side"},{q="Why is Rethiel the Greenwarden here in the Wetlands?",a="Rethiel resides at the Green Belt because the surrounding marshes are in agony. As a creature deeply entwined with the natural world, he feels the distress of the land firsthand, lamenting that it cries out for mercy. He remains here to watch over the tainted marshes, seeking the aid of passing wanderers to push back corrupting forces, quell burning threats, and soothe the suffering earth.",al={"why is rethiel here","why is rethiel in wetlands","rethiel greenwardens grove why"},it="why_here",add="1fcd3a41"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may recognize Rethiel as an unusual expression of Azeroth's wild balance. He speaks directly for a wounded ecosystem, much like the ancient protectors of Kalimdor.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may sense Rethiel's attunement to the marsh's elemental and physical disharmony. He echoes the distress of the land itself as it groans under contamination and fire."},kw={"bog beast","greenwarden","mosshide","nature","rethiel","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","quest:463","quest:275","quest:276","quest:277"},src={"Rethiel the Greenwarden"}}
E["npc:sida"] = {t="npc",n="Sida",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Harbor, Sida lives apart from her estranged husband, Einar Stonegrip. She spends her days in the Wetlands port and sometimes ventures into the marshes, where she recently lost her bag near Ironbeard's Tomb.",h="In Menethil Harbor, Sida lives apart from her estranged husband, Einar Stonegrip.",sec={{t="A Harbor Resident",b="Sida lives in Menethil Harbor, the Alliance port in the Wetlands, apart from Einar Stonegrip. Their marriage is strained, and Einar refuses to travel to Menethil while Sida remains there. She still sometimes ventures beyond the coastal settlement into the Wetlands. On a recent trip toward Ironbeard's Tomb, she lost her personal bag.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sida?",a="Sida is a dwarven woman living in Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. She gives tasks to adventurers passing through the port.",al={"who is sida","sida npc","sida wetlands"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Sida's bag?",a="Sida lost her bag while visiting Ironbeard's Tomb, an ancient burial site in the Wetlands. Foul oozes have overrun the area and swallowed her belongings.",al={"where is sida's bag","lost bag","ironbeard tomb bag"},it="wants"},{q="Why won't Einar Stonegrip visit Menethil Harbor?",a="Einar Stonegrip is Sida's estranged husband. Bad blood between them keeps him away from Menethil Harbor while Sida lives there.",al={"einar and sida","sida husband","einar stonegrip drama"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Sida be found?",a="You can find Sida along the docks and roads of Menethil Harbor, on the Wetlands' western coast.",al={"sida location","where is sida"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Sida on?",a="Sida is an Ironforge dwarf loyal to the Alliance. Like many of her kin residing in the port town of Menethil Harbor, she looks to travelers and fellow Alliance champions to lend a hand when trouble arises in the dangerous surrounding marshes.",al={"sida faction","is sida alliance","who does sida answer to"},it="side",add="46b5f80b"},{q="Why is Sida in Menethil Harbor?",a="Sida resides in Menethil Harbor, though she recently made a venture east into the marshlands to visit Ironbeard's Tomb. Following that disastrous excursion—where local oozes swallowed her belongings—she has remained in town, hoping an adventurer will head out into the bog to retrieve her lost bag.",al={"why is sida here","sida wetlands why","why is sida in menethil"},it="why_here",add="62842a43"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see everyday town life in Menethil Harbor alongside domestic disputes and the dangers of the wilderness beyond its gates.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler arriving at Menethil Harbor's docks, you can take local errands from Sida that lead inland toward Ironbeard's Tomb."},kw={"einar stonegrip","ironbeard's tomb","menethil harbor","ooze","sida","wetlands"},rel={"npc:einar-stonegrip","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","quest:470","quest:469","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Sida"}}
E["npc:tarrel-rockweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Tarrel Rockweaver",z="wetlands",s="At Menethil Harbor’s bridge, Tarrel Rockweaver anxiously waits for news of his wife, Merrin. The dwarf fears for her safety after she joined an inland archaeological expedition.",h="At Menethil Harbor’s bridge, Tarrel Rockweaver anxiously waits for news of his wife, Merrin.",sec={{t="A Watch on the Bridge",b="Tarrel Rockweaver watches the bridge at Menethil Harbor, where trade and military shipments pass. His wife, Merrin Rockweaver, joined Prospector Whelgar’s prestigious archaeological expedition deeper in the Wetlands. Violent raptors overran the excavation site and cut off regular communication. Stranded in town, Tarrel begs travelers to scout east toward Whelgar’s Excavation Site and learn whether Merrin survived.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel is an Ironforge dwarf waiting desperately near the entrance bridge of Menethil Harbor. He hopes for word of his wife, Merrin, who left on an inland dig.",al={"tarrel rockweaver","who is this dwarf","menethil bridge dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Tarrel asking travelers for help?",a="Tarrel lost contact with Merrin after danger struck her archaeological team at the dig site. Unable to leave his post, he asks travelers to head east toward Whelgar’s Excavation Site and find her.",al={"tarrel quest","in search of the excavation team","tarrel rockweaver mission"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is Tarrel’s wife and an archaeologist with Prospector Whelgar’s excavation team. She survived an attack on their camp and took shelter with the other survivors in a cave overlooking the dig site.",al={"merrin rockweaver","tarrel wife","who is merrin"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Where did Tarrel's wife go?",a="Merrin traveled east into the Wetlands to study ancient titan and dwarven relics. After the main dig site was attacked, she and the surviving excavators took shelter in a cave overlooking the ruined dig.",al={"where is merrin","excavation team location","whelgar's retreat"},sp=1},{q="Whose side is Tarrel Rockweaver on?",a="Tarrel is a loyal dwarven citizen of Ironforge and stands firmly with the Alliance. Positioned just outside Menethil Harbor, he relies on passing Alliance travelers to look out for his kin across the perils of the marsh.",al={"tarrel rockweaver faction","is tarrel rockweaver alliance"},it="side",add="017f26af"},{q="Why is Tarrel Rockweaver here in Menethil Harbor?",a="Tarrel waits on the bridge leading into Menethil Harbor to flag down passing adventurers. With wild raptors, dark iron dwarves, and hostile troggs cutting through the marshlands, he stays near the harbor hoping to enlist brave travelers to check on his missing wife.",al={"why is tarrel rockweaver here","tarrel rockweaver location why","why is tarrel on the bridge"},it="why_here",add="89989482"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Tarrel’s worry shows the perilous cost of the Explorer’s League’s relentless drive to uncover dwarven origins across the wild frontiers of Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers arriving at Menethil’s port, Tarrel offers a close look at the hardships facing Alliance citizens stationed along the untamed marshes."},kw={"dwarf","excavation team","menethil harbor","merrin rockweaver","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands"},rel={"npc:merrin-rockweaver","quest:305","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Tarrel Rockweaver"}}
E["npc:veronica-nials"] = {t="npc",n="Veronica Nials",z="wetlands",s="At Refuge Pointe, Captain Veronica Nials directs Stromgarde's defense as her kingdom crumbles. She faces Syndicate treachery and Boulderfist ogres in the Arathi Highlands.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Captain Veronica Nials directs Stromgarde's defense as her kingdom crumbles.",sec={{t="Defender of a Broken Realm",b="After the Third War, Stromgarde shattered, and its people faced invading Boulderfist ogres and the Syndicate's treachery. At Refuge Pointe, Captain Veronica Nials commands the surviving Stromgarde defenders. She directs Alliance champions against Syndicate leaders, including Lord Falconcrest and the warlock Marez Cowl. She also seeks the badges of fallen soldiers so their grieving families can learn what became of them.",sp=0},{t="A Plea Denied",b="When Rhag Garmason and the dwarven defenders of Dun Modr asked Stromgarde for help, Captain Nials had to refuse. Dark Iron saboteurs had devastated the Thandol Span, but her troops could not spare a single blade beyond the Arathi Highlands. Honor and duty bound them to defend their homeland while Stromgarde remained occupied.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Veronica Nials?",a="Veronica Nials is a human captain in the Stromgarde army, stationed at Refuge Pointe. She directs resistance against Syndicate infiltrators and ogres in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who is veronica nials","captain nials","refuge pointe captain"},it="identity"},{q="Why won't Captain Nials help Dun Modr and the Thandol Span?",a="Captain Nials cannot spare soldiers for Dun Modr and the Thandol Span. With Stromgarde near destruction, duty keeps her forces focused on reclaiming their fallen kingdom.",al={"thandol span plea","why no help for dwarfs","plea to the alliance quest"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Nials do with Stromgarde badges?",a="The Syndicate offers bounties for badges taken from slain Stromgarde soldiers. Nials asks Alliance adventurers to recover the stolen badges so she can confirm the deaths and notify the fallen defenders' families.",al={"stromgarde badges","why collect badges","badges quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Veronica Nials on?",a="Captain Nials stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stromgarde and the Alliance. As an officer in the Stromic military, her foremost devotion is to her people and their ancestral homeland, holding Refuge Pointe against the myriad enemies pressing into the Arathi Highlands.",al={"veronica nials faction","who does veronica nials serve","nials loyalty"},it="side",add="c41e517e"},{q="What does Captain Nials want?",a="Captain Nials aims to reclaim the fallen kingdom of Stromgarde from the hostile forces occupying it. She directs military efforts against the Boulderfist ogres and the Syndicate rogues who have seized the capital, while recovering the badges of fallen Stromgarde militiamen to notify their grieving families.",al={"veronica nials goal","what does captain nials want","nials objective"},it="wants",add="558769df"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stromgarde's northern kingdoms fractured and isolated, struggling to survive with little aid to offer neighboring allies.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Stromgarde's martial pride in Nials, who refuses to abandon Arathor's ancestral realm despite devastating odds."},kw={"arathi highlands","falconcrest","marez cowl","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","thandol span","veronica nials"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-modr","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance"},src={"Veronica Nials"}}
E["quest:274"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="wetlands",s="At the Stonewrought Dam, suspicious powder puts Loch Modan and Ironforge in danger. Ashlan Stonesmirk in Dun Modr identifies it as unstable Seaforium, which can explode catastrophically when it touches water.",h="At the Stonewrought Dam, suspicious powder puts Loch Modan and Ironforge in danger.",sec={{t="A Volatile Discovery",b="Ashlan Stonesmirk recognizes the silver crystals and distinct odor in samples from the Stonewrought Dam as Seaforium. It stays inert while dry, but moisture makes it react violently. An unchecked explosion could blow Ironforge out of the mountain, Ashlan warns.",sp=0},{t="Racing the Clock",b="Ashlan Stonesmirk prepares a disarming colloid to counter the explosive. Neutralizing it requires the colloid, lurker venom, crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, and a crocolisk tear. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII must be warned at once, before moisture triggers disaster.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of explosive was found at the dam?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk identifies the powder from the dam as Seaforium, marked by silver crystals and a pungent chemical smell.",al={"what powder is this","what is the powder","seaforium powder"},it="item"},{q="Why is Seaforium so dangerous here?",a="Seaforium is relatively harmless while dry, but explodes catastrophically when exposed to water. That makes the Stonewrought Dam, which holds back Loch Modan's waters, an extraordinarily hazardous place for it.",al={"why is seaforium dangerous","what makes seaforium explode"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Ashlan Stonesmirk?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is an Alliance dwarven specialist living in the Wetlands. Ashlan has the engineering and chemical expertise to analyze mysterious powders and craft neutralizers.",al={"who is ashlan","ashlan stonesmirk identity"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII oversees engineering and defense concerns in the region from the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan, safeguarding dwarven infrastructure.",al={"who is hinderweir","chief engineer hinderweir"},it="identity"},{q="How can the Seaforium be neutralized?",a="Ashlan's disarming colloid must be combined with lurker venom, crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, and a crocolisk tear to defuse the chemical reaction.",al={"how to defuse seaforium","seaforium defusal recipe","disarming colloid recipe"},it="item"},{q="What is the danger to Ironforge?",a="Ashlan warns that an uncontrolled detonation could cause seismic failure in the surrounding mountain systems, blowing Ironforge out of the mountain.",al={"is ironforge in danger","how is ironforge threatened"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Ashlan Stonesmirk want this done?",a="Ashlan realized that the mysterious substance isn't ordinary blast powder, but unstable Seaforium. Once Seaforium comes into contact with water, its explosive power could bring down entire mountains. Ashlan needs Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII warned immediately so the dwarven engineers can prepare a neutralizing solution before the volatile compound detonates.",al={"why does ashlan send you","ashlan motive","why warn hinderweir"},it="motive",add="7e9e3f07"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize Seaforium as an extremely potent volatile compound. It demands delicate handling and precise chemical countermeasures to prevent massive shockwaves.",["race:Dwarf"]="For the dwarves of Khaz Modan, volatile Seaforium in the hands of explosive saboteurs near the gateway to Dun Morogh and Ironforge is an existential threat.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance defenders must act quickly to help Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII and secure the lowlands before enemy saboteurs shatter strategic infrastructure."},kw={"ashlan stonesmirk","blast powder","chief engineer hinderweir vii","dark threat looms","disarming colloid","ironforge","seaforium","wetlands"},rel={"npc:ashlan-stonesmirk","npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Ashlan Stonesmirk",["end"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=274},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (4)"}}
E["quest:275"] = {t="quest",n="Blisters on The Land",z="wetlands",s="In the eastern Wetlands, Rethiel senses sickness spreading through the marsh. The bog beast warden asks travelers to destroy Fen Creepers, hoping to ease the land's rising fever.",h="In the eastern Wetlands, Rethiel senses sickness spreading through the marsh.",sec={{t="A Festering Marshes",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden watches the Wetlands from a grove among the marshes. The mire has always been harsh, but now an unnatural sickness spreads through it. Rethiel senses a fever in the earth, warping wild nature into mindless, shambling horrors.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Fen",b="Fen Creepers are decaying masses of swamp vegetation that wander the waterways. Rethiel calls them diseased blisters swelling on the land. Their tormented presence agitates the marsh, so Rethiel asks passing allies to destroy them and let their tangled remains settle into the mud.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is a bog beast who lives at Greenwarden's Grove in the eastern Wetlands. Rethiel tends the marsh's natural balance and works to soothe its afflictions and curb corrupted elemental growth.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel greenwarden lore","who gives blisters on the land"},it="identity"},{q="What are Fen Creepers?",a="Fen Creepers are hostile plant and bog elementals that roam the Wetlands waterways. They are hulking, shambling masses of animated vines, mud, and decaying marsh plants.",al={"fen creepers","what is a fen creeper","creepers wetlands"},it="target"},{q="Why does Rethiel want the Fen Creepers destroyed?",a="Rethiel sees the Fen Creepers as fevered signs of the marsh's growing sickness. Rethiel believes destroying them lets their forms dissolve into the earth and soothes the agitated land.",al={"why kill fen creepers","why blisters on the land"},it="motive"},{q="What causes the festering in the Wetlands?",a="Rethiel does not know what is causing the festering in the Wetlands. Rethiel senses the land's distress and calms elemental unrest wherever it rises.",al={"why are wetlands diseased","cause of wetland sickness"},it="threat"},{q="Where are Fen Creepers found in the Wetlands?",a="Fen Creepers roam the Wetlands' damp waterways, muddy banks, and central channels, especially near the deeper bogs west of Greenwarden's Grove.",al={"fen creeper locations","where to find fen creepers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest connect to other tasks for Rethiel?",a="Yes. Rethiel's concern about the Mosshide gnolls burning Wetlands trees led to Fire Taboo. Rethiel continues working to protect the marsh's balance.",al={"greenwarden questline","rethiel quests"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Rethiel's work reflects a druid's duty to heal the natural world and calm agitated elemental blights so the earth can return to balance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you may find a solitary bog beast warden allied with Stormwind in the Eastern Kingdoms. Even the land's own spirits seek help to heal wounded land.",["class:Shaman"]="Fen Creepers twist earth and water, so destroying them helps pacify discordant elemental spirits."},kw={"blisters on the land","fen creepers","greenwarden","marshes","rethiel","wetland bogs","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:277","quest:463","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=275},src={"Blisters on The Land"}}
E["quest:276"] = {t="quest",n="Tramping Paws",z="wetlands",s="At Greenwarden's Grove in the Wetlands, Rethiel watches the Mosshide numbers rise near the Gate of Algaz. Their fires and trampling threaten the bog, and Rethiel asks travelers to thin their ranks.",h="At Greenwarden's Grove in the Wetlands, Rethiel watches the Mosshide numbers rise near the Gate of Algaz.",sec={{t="A Swelling Fen Menace",b="Mosshide gnolls lived in the Wetlands for many years without overwhelming the natural order. Now their numbers have surged south toward the pass of Dun Algaz. Their heavy boots and paws crush rare fen plants, while their logging strips groves for campsite fires. If the packs keep growing, the fragile marsh will suffer.",sp=0},{t="The Greenwarden's Judgment",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden watches the marsh for signs of imbalance. The gnolls' existence is not the trouble; their numbers have grown beyond what the Wetlands can support. Thinning the Mosshide gnolls and mongrels helps preserve the fen, and may earn the approval of its ancient guardian.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is a bog beast who lives in the Wetlands along the road between Ironforge's borders and Arathi. Dedicated to preserving the marsh, Rethiel watches the land's health and asks travelers to keep destructive populations in check.",al={"rethiel lore","who gives tramping paws","greenwarden wetlands"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Mosshide gnolls a problem now?",a="The Mosshide gnolls once lived alongside the marsh without lasting harm, but their recent population boom has brought heavy logging for firewood and widespread trampling of fragile marsh plants.",al={"why kill gnolls wetlands","mosshide gnoll threat"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the gnolls causing this damage?",a="Mosshide gnolls and mongrels gather in large numbers in the southern Wetlands, especially near the dwarven pass of Dun Algaz.",al={"where are mosshide gnolls","tramping paws location"},it="place"},{q="What comes after culling the gnolls?",a="After the packs are thinned, Rethiel investigates the cause of their unusual activity and fuel use, then sends travelers to Fire Taboo.",al={"next quest after tramping paws","tramping paws follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rethiel mention having its faith tested?",a="Rethiel says its faith in your people has been taxed in the past, and it remains wary of mortals and their rapid expansion. Helping protect the wild fen shows that mortals can care for nature rather than exploit it.",al={"rethiel dialogue","faith taxed in the past"}},{q="Who are the Mosshide gnolls you are sent to hunt?",a="The Mosshide are a clan of gnolls native to the Wetlands. Though they lived here peacefully alongside nature for generations, their burgeoning population now strips the marshland bare. Their heavy paws trample the fen's delicate flora, while their axes fell excessive timber for cooking and campfires, driving the local ecosystem entirely out of balance.",al={"mosshide gnolls","who are mosshide","mosshide mongrels"},it="target",add="24db34f0"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share the Cenarion duty to keep nature in balance. Thinning an unnatural population surge can help keep the marsh from collapsing.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share old bonds with nature's wild spirits. Helping Rethiel heal the marsh is a familiar and honored duty.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the gnolls swarm just outside the Gate of Algaz. Thinning their ranks protects the fen and secures the vital road between Ironforge and Menethil Harbor."},kw={"algaz","gnolls","greenwarden","mongrels","mosshide","rethiel","tramping paws","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:463","quest:277","zone:wetlands","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=276},src={"Tramping Paws"}}
E["quest:277"] = {t="quest",n="Fire Taboo",z="wetlands",s="Along the marsh roads of the Wetlands, Fire Taboo puts Rethiel's concern for the forest into action. The bog beast asks travelers to take the crude flints Mosshide gnolls use to burn living trees, hoping to spare the ancient boughs.",h="Along the marsh roads of the Wetlands, Fire Taboo puts Rethiel's concern for the forest into action.",sec={{t="A Greenwarden's Anguish",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden feels the Wetlands' trees as kin. Rot and renewal belong to the swamp, but the Mosshide gnolls cut living timber and cast it into their hearthfires. The groans of those boughs weigh on Rethiel, who can no longer watch the trees suffer in silence.",sp=0},{t="Extinguishing the Mosshides",b="The Mosshide pack cuts green trees for warmth and territory instead of gathering deadwood. Rethiel seeks to curb their spread without a long war, so the bog beast asks you to take the crude flints carried by stronger gnolls. Without those tools, the pack cannot burn the timber it fells. Rethiel smashes each stone and casts its dust into the sea, where it can never spark the forest again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is a bog beast who lives in the Wetlands. Bound to the life of its trees and plants, Rethiel seeks to protect the wounded swamp from the Mosshide gnolls.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel greenwarden lore","who gives fire taboo"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Rethiel want crude flints instead of killing the gnoll leaders?",a="Rethiel sees burning living wood as an unpardonable violation. Taking the flints keeps the gnolls from lighting fires against the wetland trees and ends the destruction of living wood.",al={"why flints","why take flints","crude flint purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens to the flints once they are turned in?",a="Rethiel smashes the flints and casts their remains into the sea, so they can never spark against living timber again.",al={"what does she do with flints","flint destruction"}},{q="Which gnolls carry the flints?",a="The stronger Mosshide gnolls carry the crude flints. Smaller Mosshides and weaker mongrels are not trusted with fire-making tools and carry none.",al={"who drops flints","which gnolls have crude flint"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why are the Mosshides cutting down trees?",a="The Mosshide gnolls cut living trees to fuel their campfires and keep warm in the damp swamp, rather than use dry, fallen timber.",al={"why gnolls cut trees","mosshide woodcutting"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next after gathering the flints?",a="After you take the flints and deprive the gnolls of fire, Rethiel sends you to deal with another blight afflicting the marshes in the follow-up, Blisters on The Land.",al={"what quest is after fire taboo","next quest after flints"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rethiel the Greenwarden want this done?",a="As a protector tied to the land and nature, Rethiel acutely feels the suffering of the Wetlands. The Mosshide gnolls are chopping down living trees and burning them for warmth, inflicting agony upon the wilderness. By stripping the gnolls of their flints, Rethiel hopes to stop the destruction of the forest and ensure the gnolls can no longer burn living wood.",al={"rethiel motive","why take flints","why does rethiel hate fire"},it="motive",add="e3ab03fe"},{q="What is the Crude Flint for?",a="The Mosshide gnolls carry crude flints as primitive tools to strike spark and kindle fire. Without them, they cannot burn the living wood they fell across the Wetlands. Rethiel demands you collect these flints so it can shatter them and cast the remains into the sea, stripping away their ability to light blazes.",al={"crude flint use","what are crude flints","why do gnolls have flint"},it="item",add="b6cb9238"},{q="Who are the Mosshides you are sent against?",a="You are pitted against the Mosshide gnolls, a vicious clan of hyena-men infesting the Wetlands. They have spread throughout the marshes, building camps and aggressively cutting down ancient trees to build fires and claim territory, bringing ruin and misery to the natural balance Rethiel protects.",al={"mosshides wetlands","who are the gnolls","mosshide gnolls"},it="target",add="25034295"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share Rethiel's reverence for the wild and understand the pain living trees suffer in gnoll firepits.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may recognize a fellow protector of living trees in Rethiel, a bog beast who feels the Wetlands' suffering.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know the Mosshide gnolls threaten those crossing the Wetlands. Helping the local spirits protects the trade routes between Dun Morogh and Arathi."},kw={"crude flint","fire taboo","gnolls","greenwarden","living wood","mosshide","rethiel","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:276","quest:275","topic:gnoll","zone:wetlands","quest:463"},m={start="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=277,ri={"Crude Flint"}},src={"Fire Taboo"}}
E["quest:288"] = {t="quest",n="The Third Fleet",z="wetlands",s="Outside the Deepwater Tavern, First Mate Fitzsimmons drinks to drown his memories. He alone survived Kul Tiras's Third Fleet, burned off the Wetlands by red dragons enslaved by orcs during the Second War.",h="Outside the Deepwater Tavern, First Mate Fitzsimmons drinks to drown his memories.",sec={{t="A Sailor's Grief",b="First Mate Fitzsimmons spends his days outside the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, nursing a hangover and memories he cannot shake. He once served as an officer aboard the Wave Mistress, a ship-of-the-line that sailed under Kul Tiras's maritime banner. Now he trades those grim memories for dwarven mead. Anyone who buys him another drink can hear his account of one of the Second War's worst naval slaughters.",sp=0},{t="Fire Over the Waves",b="During the Second War, the Third Fleet sailed along the shores of Khaz Modan when fire came from the sky. The Dragonmaw clan had subdued the red dragonflight at Grim Batol and unleashed dragonfire on the unsuspecting warships. Fitzsimmons remembers helpless wooden hulls burning beneath towering flames, their crews dragged into the deep. He alone survived and washed ashore. His fallen brothers lie in the watery graveyard now known as the Doomed Fleet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?",a="First Mate Fitzsimmons is an old sailor drinking away his trauma outside the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Once first mate of the Kul Tiras warship Wave Mistress, he is the sole known survivor of the Third Fleet's destruction.",al={"fitzsimmons","who is the drunk sailor","fitzsimmons tavern"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the Third Fleet?",a="During the Second War, the Dragonmaw clan ambushed and burned Kul Tiras's Third Fleet off the Wetlands coast. Orcs riding dragons rained fire from above, sending ships and sailors to the seabed.",al={"third fleet fate","how did the fleet sink","kul tiras ships sunk"},it="history"},{q="Why were dragons attacking human ships?",a="During the Second War, the Dragonmaw clan enslaved the red dragon Alexstrasza with the Demon Soul at nearby Grim Batol. Bound by dark sorcery, the red dragons were forced to serve the Horde as mounts and siege weapons.",al={"dragonmaw dragons","red dragons wetlans","why orcs on dragons"},it="origin"},{q="Where did the ships actually sink?",a="The charred wrecks lie beneath the sea off the Wetlands' western coast, north of Menethil Harbor. The area is remembered as the Doomed Fleet.",al={"where is the doomed fleet","shipwreck location wetlands","third fleet wreckage"},it="place"},{q="What drink does Fitzsimmons want?",a="Fitzsimmons wants a flagon of dwarven mead to loosen his tongue and ease his splitting hangover. The innkeeper inside the Deepwater Tavern sells it.",al={"fitzsimmons mead","what does fitzsimmons want","flagon of mead"},it="item"},{q="What nation did the Third Fleet serve?",a="The Third Fleet served Kul Tiras, an island kingdom whose formidable navy was the backbone of the Alliance's naval forces during the Second War.",al={"is the third fleet stormwind","kul tiras fleet","who owned the wave mistress"},it="ties"},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons want a drink?",a="Fitzsimmons is the lone survivor of a terrible massacre, haunted by the burning of his fleet and nursing a vicious hangover. His head is pounding so severely that he cannot bear to recount the tragedy of the Third Fleet without strong drink to dull the pain and loosen his tongue. A flagon of mead is all that will get him talking.",al={"fitzsimmons motive","why does fitzsimmons want mead","why help fitzsimmons"},it="motive",add="03818f34"},{q="Why does Fitzsimmons need you to fetch the mead?",a="Fitzsimmons is a broken, destitute survivor wallowing in self-pity and agony right outside the tavern. Plagued by a throbbing hangover and having likely spent his last copper, he has neither the means nor the vigor to walk up to the bar himself, leaving him to beg passing adventurers for charity.",al={"why can't fitzsimmons buy his own drink","why ask me for mead","fitzsimmons why me"},it="why_me",add="53fbd504"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can remember the Third Fleet's destruction as a bitter mark of the naval battles Kul Tiras and the Alliance fought against the Dragonmaw.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you hear in Fitzsimmons's account of the Wave Mistress the scars left by the Horde's dragon-riders across Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Grim Batol cast a shadow over Khaz Modan, while dragons bred in its depths wreaked havoc on dwarf lands and human allies alike."},kw={"deepwater tavern","doomed fleet","dragonmaw","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","menethil harbor","red dragons","third fleet","wave mistress","wetlands"},rel={"npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","subzone:deepwater-tavern","quest:270","topic:kul-tiras","zone:wetlands"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=288,ri={"Flagon of Dwarven Mead"}},src={"The Third Fleet (Classic)"}}
E["quest:289"] = {t="quest",n="The Cursed Crew",z="wetlands",s="Off the Wetlands coast, The Cursed Crew still haunts its sunken ships. First Mate Fitzsimmons, the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras's sole living survivor, asks for mercy for his lost brethren. A dark relic aboard one of the wrecks binds the drowned sailors and marines to the ships as restless undead.",h="Off the Wetlands coast, The Cursed Crew still haunts its sunken ships.",sec={{t="A Restless Fleet",b="The Third Fleet of Kul Tiras wrecked along the jagged shores north of Menethil Harbor. First Mate Fitzsimmons alone made it ashore alive. His fellow sailors did not find peace beneath the waves. A mysterious treasure hidden deep in one of the hulls unleashed sorcery as they died. It bound their souls to the battered timbers and denied them the grave's rest.",sp=0},{t="Mercy by the Blade",b="First Mate Fitzsimmons still hears his former shipmates' moans and cries at night in the taverns of Menethil Harbor. He believes that striking down their animated corpses can release them from their torment. He sends travelers into the rotting, drowned hulks to kill the cursed sailors, the seasoned marines, and his former peer, First Mate Snellig. Fitzsimmons asks them to bring back Snellig's personal snuffbox as proof that his friend has finally been laid to rest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was First Mate Snellig?",a="First Mate Snellig served aboard the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras with First Mate Fitzsimmons. Snellig drowned with the crew when the fleet wrecked off the northern Wetlands coast. A malevolent relic aboard the ships raised him as an undead horror, now haunting a flooded hold in one of the wrecks.",al={"snellig","first mate snellig","who is snellig"},it="target"},{q="Why are the sailors and marines cursed?",a="Fitzsimmons says a concealed, malignant treasure was aboard one of the fleet's vessels. When the ships wrecked along the coast, the artifact's dark energies bound the drowned crew's spirits to their rotting hulls, barring their passage beyond and condemning them to undead torment.",al={"why are they undead","third fleet curse","cursed sailors cause"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the sunken ships located?",a="The Third Fleet's ruined ships lie submerged off the northern Wetlands coast, north of Menethil Harbor. The cursed crew prowls the decks and surrounding waters, while Snellig haunts the cracked hull of the southern vessel.",al={"where are the ships","wreck location","where is snellig"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Fitzsimmons want Snellig's snuffbox?",a="First Mate Snellig's snuffbox was his personal keepsake in life. Returning it to Fitzsimmons proves that his cursed comrade has been released from his rotting prison beneath the waves.",al={"snelligs snuffbox","snuff box","why snuffbox"},it="item"},{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?",a="First Mate Fitzsimmons is a Kul Tiran sailor and the Third Fleet's only known living survivor. Grief and guilt keep him in Menethil Harbor, haunted by nightmares of his drowned brothers and seeking travelers to end their suffering.",al={"fitzsimmons","first mate fitzsimmons"},it="identity"},{q="Does killing the crew actually break the curse?",a="Striking down the sailors and marines gives their restless spirits temporary respite, but does not break the enchantment. The mysterious relic hidden aboard the wreckage remains at the curse's root.",al={"is the curse lifted","does this end the curse"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons want the cursed crew slain?",a="Fitzsimmons is haunted by being the sole living survivor of the Third Fleet. In his sleep, he is tormented by the doomed moans of his drowned shipmates, whose souls remain bound to the rotting hulls by a dark treasure. He hopes putting their walking corpses to rest will quiet their cries and begin lifting the terrible curse holding them.",al={"why kill the crew","fitzsimmons motive","why does fitzsimmons want this"},it="motive",add="8e82e35b"},{q="Why does Fitzsimmons need you instead of going himself?",a="Fitzsimmons is an old, broken sailor battered by the trauma of surviving the shipwreck that claimed his entire fleet. Drowning his sorrows in the tavern, he has neither the strength nor the heart to face the reanimated corpses of his former comrades himself, relying instead on capable adventurers to venture out to the wrecks.",al={"why does fitzsimmons need me","why cant fitzsimmons go","why not menethil guards"},it="why_me",add="7d36941a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you share a solemn duty to lay these tormented Kul Tiran sailors to rest. Kul Tiras has long supplied the Grand Alliance with its finest sailors.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can lay the innocent sailors to rest and cleanse the profane desecration wrought upon them, bringing light to dark waters.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you may feel kinship with these fallen sailors through the shared naval traditions of the kingdom of Kul Tiras."},kw={"cursed crew","cursed marine","cursed sailor","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","menethil","snellig","snuffbox","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:288","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:kul-tiras"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=289,ri={"Snellig's Snuffbox"}},src={"The Cursed Crew (Classic)"}}
E["quest:290"] = {t="quest",n="Lifting the Curse",z="wetlands",s="First Mate Fitzsimmons seeks to free his fallen crewmates from a restless curse. He believes a dark artifact aboard the wrecked Intrepid binds them, and Captain Halyndor's ghost guards the key to its strongbox.",h="First Mate Fitzsimmons seeks to free his fallen crewmates from a restless curse.",sec={{t="A Captain's Burden",b="First Mate Fitzsimmons survived the Third Fleet's fate, but memories of his comrades haunt him by day and by night. He believes an evil object locked in the Intrepid's strongbox is tied to the undeath gripping his shipmates. The wreck is watched by Captain Halyndor, whose ghost guards the key to the strongbox.",sp=0},{t="Unlocking the Depths",b="The Third Fleet's broken ships lie off the northern Wetlands coast. Inside the flooded hull of the Intrepid, a locked strongbox holds the relic at the heart of the crew's misery. To reach it, you face Halyndor's ghost on deck, take the rusted key, and enter the flooded hull. The artifact must be recovered so holy hands can cleanse it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What ship are you searching during this quest?",a="You are searching the Intrepid, a sunken ship of the Third Fleet off the northwestern Wetlands shore.",al={"which ship","intrepid shipwreck","where is the strongbox"},it="place"},{q="Who is Captain Halyndor?",a="Captain Halyndor commanded the Intrepid. His restless ghost haunts the ruined ship's deck and guards the key to its strongbox.",al={"who is halyndor","captain halyndor lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons want the strongbox opened?",a="Fitzsimmons believes a cursed object in the strongbox traps his fellow sailors' spirits in torment. He wants it opened so the artifact can be recovered and purified.",al={"fitzsimmons goal","why open strongbox","purpose of quest"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Intrepid's strongbox located?",a="The Intrepid's strongbox lies submerged in the lower hull, reached through a breach in the wreck's side beneath the waves.",al={"strongbox location","where is the chest","how to find strongbox"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who can cleanse the cursed object once it is recovered?",a="Fitzsimmons directs you to bring the recovered object to Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarven priest in Menethil Harbor, for cleansing.",al={"who cleanses the relic","who is glorin steelbrow","where take cursed thing"},it="next_step"},{q="What caused the shipwreck in the first place?",a="During the Second War, orc-controlled red dragons attacked the Third Fleet, burning and sinking its ships off the Wetlands coast. A cursed treasure aboard now keeps the drowned crews from rest.",al={"how did third fleet sink","third fleet wreckage cause"},it="history"},{q="What is the Intrepid Strongbox Key for?",a="The key belonged to Captain Halyndor and is required to unlock the Intrepid's strongbox in the wreckage. Inside lies the cursed object responsible for blighting the Third Fleet's sailors, which must be recovered before it can ever be cleansed.",al={"intrepid strongbox key","what does the key open","why do i need the key"},it="item",add="336b08f7"},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons send you instead of going himself?",a="Fitzsimmons is deeply traumatized and haunted by dreams of his dead crew and former commander. Stricken with guilt and fear, he cannot face the doomed wreckage of the Intrepid or the vengeful ghost of Captain Halyndor himself.",al={"why me fitzsimmons","why can't fitzsimmons do it","why fitzsimmons needs you"},it="why_me",add="1f8e42a3"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you have the spiritual authority to address afflictions and cleanse tainted relics. Fitzsimmons entrusts the strongbox's contents to the priesthood for purification.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you honor the sailors who served the Alliance in life by helping lay their tortured souls to rest while traveling through Menethil Harbor."},kw={"captain halyndor","fitzsimmons","glorin steelbrow","intrepid","lifting the curse","menethil harbor","strongbox","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","npc:glorin-steelbrow","quest:288","zone:wetlands"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",["end"]="Intrepid's Locked Strongbox",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=290,ri={"Intrepid Strongbox Key"}},src={"Lifting the Curse (Classic)"}}
E["quest:292"] = {t="quest",n="The Eye of Paleth",z="wetlands",s="Fitzsimmons asks you to recover The Eye of Paleth from the sunken Intrepid. Bring the cursed gem to Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor, where the dwarven priest can seek a way to purge its blight.",h="Fitzsimmons asks you to recover The Eye of Paleth from the sunken Intrepid.",sec={{t="A Blighted Relic",b="The locked strongbox aboard the Intrepid holds a blackened orb that pulses beneath the waters of Baradin Bay. It is The Eye of Paleth, warped from sacred light into a source of suffering. Its corruption is bound to the restless spirits and doom that claimed the sailors of the Third Fleet.",sp=0},{t="Seeking the Priesthood",b="Glorin Steelbrow examines the relic in Menethil Harbor. The dwarven priest of the Holy Light is stunned that such a sacred device belonged to the Third Fleet. He recognizes its unnatural taint and begins preparing rites to undo its dark influence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="The Eye of Paleth is an ancient, powerful sacred gem, normally tied to holy energies. The specimen aboard the sunken Third Fleet vessel Intrepid has become twisted and cursed, radiating dark magic.",al={"eye of paleth lore","what is paleth","cursed eye of paleth"},it="item"},{q="Where was the Eye recovered?",a="You recover the Eye from a locked strongbox in the flooded wreck of the Intrepid, just off the coast of the Wetlands.",al={"where do i find the eye","eye of paleth location","intrepid strongbox"},it="place"},{q="Why does Glorin Steelbrow care about the artifact?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven priest stationed in Menethil Harbor. His knowledge of the Holy Light lets him recognize ancient relics and begin rites to break sinister curses.",al={"who is glorin steelbrow","why steelbrow"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does Fitzsimmons know about the Eye?",a="Fitzsimmons survived the tragedy of the Third Fleet and remains haunted by it. Taking refuge in Menethil's tavern, he knew of the dark relic hidden in the wreckage, which tormented his fallen crewmates.",al={"fitzsimmons connection","why did fitzsimmons send me"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Eye cursed?",a="The Eye's corruption is tied to the supernatural deaths and restless undead haunting the wrecked ships of the Third Fleet. It absorbed dark energies during or after the catastrophe that sent the fleet to the ocean floor.",al={"why is it cursed","eye curse origin"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after giving the Eye to Glorin?",a="Glorin examines the cursed gem and sees it cannot remain blighted. He directs you to cleanse the relic of its corrupting influence.",al={"next quest","what to do with the eye"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, the defilement of a sacred artifact like The Eye of Paleth makes this investigation matter to your faith in the Holy Light.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share a dedication to reclaiming lost relics off the shores of Khaz Modan, with Ironforge clergy like Glorin Steelbrow to aid you.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the Third Fleet's destruction left Menethil Harbor vulnerable. Recovering its remnants can bring closure to lost comrades."},kw={"cursed eye of paleth","eye of paleth","fitzsimmons","glorin steelbrow","intrepid","menethil harbor","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:293","npc:glorin-steelbrow","quest:288","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:light"},m={start="Intrepid's Locked Strongbox",["end"]="Glorin Steelbrow",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=292},src={"The Eye of Paleth (Classic)"}}
E["quest:293"] = {t="quest",n="Cleansing the Eye",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Cleansing the Eye sends adventurers south to Stormwind with a cursed orb in need of aid. After recovering the Eye of Paleth, they seek Archbishop Benedictus to purge its lingering taint.",h="In the Wetlands, Cleansing the Eye sends adventurers south to Stormwind with a cursed orb in need of aid.",sec={{t="A Tainted Relic",b="The Eye of Paleth recovered from the marshlands bears no holy light. Shadow clings to it, along with the sorrow and trauma of the tragedy where it was lost. Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarf, recognizes the orb's power. Yet he lacks the divine craft to lift so heavy a curse.",sp=0},{t="Journey to the Cathedral",b="Human priests of the Holy Light first fashioned the Eyes of Paleth, so their highest order alone knows how to undo the defilement. Glorin sends adventurers south to Stormwind with the darkened orb, to Archbishop Benedictus, leader of the Church of the Holy Light. Benedictus knows the danger of leaving such a relic unpurified. He takes on the work of restoring its sacred light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="The Eyes of Paleth are sacred orbs crafted by human priests to shine with holy luminance. Untainted, their power aligns with the Holy Light. Corrupted, their energies grow volatile and perilous.",al={"eye of paleth lore","what is this orb","what is the eye of paleth"},it="item"},{q="Why can't Glorin Steelbrow cleanse the Eye himself?",a="Glorin Steelbrow cannot cleanse the Eye because he lacks the liturgical craft to banish its dark affliction. Human priests of the Holy Light made the relic, so cleansing its corruption requires authority from that tradition.",al={"why send me to stormwind","glorin cleansing","why benedictus"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Archbishop Benedictus?",a="Archbishop Benedictus is the venerable leader of the Church of the Holy Light. He resides in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light and guides the Alliance in matters of faith.",al={"who is benedictus","archbishop benedictus","stormwind archbishop"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Eye described as soiled or sorrowful?",a="Archbishop Benedictus says the orb bore witness to a great tragedy in the Wetlands. It absorbed that agony over time, and its lingering sorrow became a curse that warped its power.",al={"why is it cursed","eye of paleth tragedy","cursed eye of paleth"},it="history"},{q="What happens once Benedictus receives the orb?",a="Benedictus agrees to purify the orb. The Eyes of Paleth are meant to shine brightly, and their taint brings grave spiritual and physical danger to those nearby.",al={"does benedictus cleanse it","eye of paleth outcome"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is the Cathedral of Light located?",a="The Cathedral of Light stands in Cathedral Square, in Stormwind City's northern district. Archbishop Benedictus stands at the main altar in the heart of the sanctuary.",al={"where is cathedral of light","cathedral of light location","find benedictus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Glorin Steelbrow want the Eye of Paleth cleansed?",a="Glorin recognizes that the cursed Eye of Paleth is an intensely dangerous holy relic. Created by human priests of the Holy Light to shine bright, its magic turns hazardous and corrupting when tainted by tragedy and dark power. Because dwarven craft and his own skills cannot lift such a spiritual affliction, he insists it be delivered to Stormwind before its corruption causes further harm to you or the surrounding lands.",al={"why cleanse eye of paleth","glorin steelbrow motive","why send eye to stormwind"},it="motive",add="6f168d84"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For priests of the Holy Light, the Cursed Eye of Paleth shows how despair can corrupt sacred craft. Archbishop Benedictus's purification is needed to cleanse it.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins see reclaiming holy relics from dark marshes as a solemn duty. The Eye's corruption is an affront to be cleansed in Stormwind's hallowed halls.",["faction:Alliance"]="The dwarven outposts of the Wetlands and Stormwind's spiritual leaders work together through shared faith, binding the Alliance's kingdoms."},kw={"archbishop benedictus","cathedral of light","cleansing the eye","cursed eye of paleth","eye of paleth","glorin steelbrow","stormwind","wetlands"},rel={"quest:292","npc:archbishop-benedictus","npc:glorin-steelbrow","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:wetlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light"},m={start="Glorin Steelbrow",["end"]="Archbishop Benedictus",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=293},src={"Cleansing the Eye"}}
E["quest:294"] = {t="quest",n="Ormer's Revenge",z="wetlands",s="At Whelgar Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid and two companions are trapped above a raptor-swarmed dig. The dwarves uncovered massive prehistoric bones beneath the Wetlands, and the disturbance drew packs of mottled raptors that killed most of the crew.",h="At Whelgar Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid and two companions are trapped above a raptor-swarmed dig.",sec={{t="Unearthed Horrors",b="The dwarves came to Whelgar Excavation Site to uncover the massive prehistoric remains beneath the Wetlands muck. Their discovery brought the marsh’s native raptors to the dig. Packs of mottled predators swarmed the site, caught the excavators off guard, and tore through their ranks.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Stand",b="Only a handful of dwarves survived the slaughter. Ormer Ironbraid, Merrin Rockweaver, and Prospector Whelgar scrambled up a bluff above the pit, but aggressive packs still pin them there. Ormer is grieving and furious, yet stays to guard Merrin and the Prospector. He asks travelers to thin the Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers below, the opening salvo of his vengeance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the excavators here?",a="The raptors overran the dig after the dwarven archaeologists uncovered giant bones in the basin. The disturbance drew local packs from the marsh; they killed most of the crew and trapped three survivors on the high bluff.",al={"why are raptors here","whelgar excavation massacre","what killed the dwarves"},it="history"},{q="Who is Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer Ironbraid is a dwarven excavator stranded at Whelgar's Excavation Site. He stays to protect the shaken Prospector Whelgar and Merrin Rockweaver, while seeking bloody retribution against the raptors that killed his comrades.",al={"who is ormer","ormer ironbraid backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where do these raptors come from?",a="Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers are native Wetlands predators. They lurk on the muddy slopes and marshland west of the excavation bluff, and along paths leading toward the dig site's caves.",al={"where are mottled raptors","raptor locations wetlands"},it="origin"},{q="Why doesn't Ormer hunt the raptors himself?",a="Ormer is eager to kill raptors himself, but he must guard Prospector Whelgar and Merrin Rockweaver. He keeps watch so the terrified dwarves' refuge on the bluff is not overrun.",al={"why doesn't ormer fight","why is ormer stuck"},it="why_me"},{q="Does culling these raptors end Ormer's grudge?",a="No. Killing the common Mottled Raptors and Screechers is only the first step in Ormer's plan to avenge his fallen friends. Harsher strikes against the raptor brood will follow.",al={"is this the end of ormer's revenge","what happens next with ormer"},it="next_step"},{q="Why did uncovering the bones attract the raptors?",a="The Wetlands raptors are fiercely territorial and aggressive scavengers. Excavating the ancient giant remains disrupted the basin, drawing curious, hungry predators into the center of the dig camp.",al={"why did bones attract raptors","dinosaur bones raptors"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Ormer Ironbraid want the raptors killed?",a="When the dwarven team unearthed ancient bones at the dig site, ravenous raptors swarmed the grounds and slaughtered Ormer's coworkers. Ormer, Merrin Rockweaver, and Prospector Whelgar barely survived the onslaught and remain trapped atop the bluffs. Burning with grief and fury, Ormer wants to avenge his fallen brethren and begin clearing the vicious beasts away from the excavation.",al={"ormer ironbraid motive","why kill mottled raptors","ormer revenge why"},it="motive",add="87324e21"},{q="What are the Mottled Raptors and Screechers you are sent after?",a="You are sent against the Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers prowling just west of the excavation bluff. These aggressive reptiles native to the Wetlands swarmed the site as soon as the diggers exposed massive ancient bones, massacring the excavators and claiming the surrounding grounds as their feeding territory.",al={"who are you fighting","mottled screechers target","mottled raptors wetlands"},it="target",add="79eca2c5"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing your kin slain during an Explorers' League dig can make clearing the raptor-infested quarry an act of ancestral honor and righteous retribution.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can study how dangerous mottled raptors track through marsh terrain on the slopes outside the site."},kw={"mottled raptor","mottled screecher","ormer ironbraid","ormer's revenge","prospector whelgar","wetlands","whelgar excavation site"},rel={"npc:ormer-ironbraid","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Ormer Ironbraid",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=294},src={"Ormer's Revenge"}}
E["quest:295"] = {t="quest",n="Ormer's Revenge",z="wetlands",s="At the ruined Whelgar Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid sends you after the raptors that drove out his expedition. With the smaller scouts culled, he wants the Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws killed.",h="At the ruined Whelgar Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid sends you after the raptors that drove out his...",sec={{t="Escalating the Hunt",b="Ormer Ironbraid turns your blades on the adult raptors in the lower dig. You have already thinned the smaller juveniles that overran the upper camp, but Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws still threaten any hope of reclaiming the excavation. They tear through dwarven prospectors and leave the trenches strewn with shattered crates and abandoned picks.",sp=0},{t="Blood in the Trenches",b="Raptors have made their nests in the excavation pits. From the ridge above the dig, Ormer directs you into the mud to strike at the mature beasts. Prospector Whelgar and his crew hope to salvage ancient relics, but Ormer is consumed by vengeance. He demands a heavy toll of dead Scytheclaws and Razormaws before he turns to the site's apex terror.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Ormer so angry at these raptors?",a="The mottled raptors swarmed the Whelgar Excavation Site, drove out the dwarven team, and slaughtered those who could not escape. Ormer Ironbraid was displaced and left bitter, and he will not let the beasts control the dig without making them pay in blood.",al={"why ormer mad","ormer revenge reason","why kill raptors wetlands"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws found?",a="Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws prowl the lower dig trenches and surrounding earthworks at the Whelgar Excavation Site, east of Menethil Harbor and southwest of Dun Modr in the Wetlands.",al={"mottled scytheclaw location","mottled razormaw location","where to find raptors ormer"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer Ironbraid is a dwarven member of the Explorers' League stationed at the Whelgar Excavation Site. After the dig was overrun, he made it his personal mission to exterminate the raptor pack infesting their work.",al={"who is ormer","ormer ironbraid lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after culling these raptors?",a="After you cull the Scytheclaws and Razormaws, Ormer turns his attention to Sarltooth, the large raptor he believes leads the local pack. He directs you to end the source of the raptor infestation.",al={"what next after ormer revenge","ormer's revenge sequel","next quest after scytheclaws"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does this quest connect to other tasks in the excavation site?",a="Yes. As you hunt raptors in the lower dig for Ormer, you can also help Prospector Whelgar and his team with 'Uncovering the Past' by collecting fragmented earthen artifacts scattered across the same trenches.",al={"whelgar excavation quests","uncovering the past connection"},gp=true},{q="Why were the dwarves digging here in the first place?",a="The Explorers' League of Ironforge established the Whelgar Excavation Site to search for titan relics and uncover the ancient history of the dwarven race. Aggressive wildlife halted their work when it overran the dig.",al={"why excavate wetlands","whelgar excavation purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What are Mottled Scytheclaws and Mottled Razormaws?",a="These vicious raptor breeds prowl the lower tiers of the Whelgar Excavation Site. Known for their bloodthirst and razor-sharp talons, they overran the dwarven diggers and drove them from their work pits. Ormer now directs you to hunt down their deadliest varieties to break their dominance over the ruins.",al={"what are scytheclaws and razormaws","mottled scytheclaws","mottled razormaws","wetlands raptors"},it="target",add="2ccf3294"},{q="Why does Ormer need you to hunt the raptors instead of handling them himself?",a="Ormer and the surviving Prospectors have been driven up to the ridge above the dig site. With their excavation team scattered or slain, they lack the manpower to mount an aggressive counterattack alone and need capable adventurers willing to delve down into the infested pits on their behalf.",al={"why does ormer need help","why ormer doesnt kill raptors","why me ormer"},it="why_me",add="f1520877"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share the Explorers' League's fierce pride and its refusal to let wild beasts halt the search for your ancestral past.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face the Wetlands' Mottled raptors, territorial pack hunters that make tracking lethal in the enclosed, muddy trenches.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help reclaim the Whelgar Excavation Site and secure safe operations along the eastern road between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands."},kw={"dwarf","excavation","explorers league","mottled razormaw","mottled scytheclaw","ormer ironbraid","raptors","wetlands","whelgar excavation"},rel={"quest:294","npc:ormer-ironbraid","quest:299","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Ormer Ironbraid",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=295},src={"Ormer's Revenge (2)"}}
E["quest:296"] = {t="quest",n="Ormer's Revenge",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Ormer's Revenge begins with a demand for Sarltooth's death. Ormer Ironbraid believes the raptor led the attack that slaughtered dwarven excavators at Whelgar Excavation Site, and asks you to bring back one of its talons as proof.",h="In the Wetlands, Ormer's Revenge begins with a demand for Sarltooth's death.",sec={{t="A Strike at the Pack Leader",b="After the Explorer's League diggers were slaughtered at Whelgar Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid watched the raptors from his ridge. One beast stood larger than the rest. Sarltooth perched above the dig works, where Ormer saw it directing or leading the pack that drove the dwarves out. To Ormer, Sarltooth was more than a wild beast. He believed it had led the attack on King Magni Bronzebeard's subjects.",sp=0},{t="Justice in the Wetlands",b="Ormer demands death for the massacre. He sends you up the high paths along the excavation walls to kill Sarltooth. Bring back one of the raptor's formidable talons, and the fallen workers will be avenged. Ormer wants the marshes to know that attacks on dwarven expeditions will not go unanswered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sarltooth?",a="Sarltooth is a large, menacing raptor leading the pack at Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. Ormer Ironbraid believes Sarltooth directed the assault that massacred the dwarven diggers.",al={"what is sarltooth","who is the raptor boss","sarltooth lore"},it="target"},{q="Where is Sarltooth located?",a="Sarltooth prowls an elevated path along the western wall, in the northwest corner of Whelgar Excavation Site.",al={"find sarltooth","where does sarltooth spawn","sarltooth path"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ormer want Sarltooth dead instead of just driving him away?",a="Ormer sees the raptor attack as a crime against King Magni's subjects. Dwarven workers died while doing their jobs, and Ormer believes only Sarltooth's death can redeem the memory of the fallen.",al={"ormer revenge reason","why kill sarltooth"},it="motive"},{q="What proof does Ormer require?",a="Ormer demands one of Sarltooth's talons as proof that the massive predator has been slain.",al={"sarltooth proof","sarltooth talon"},it="item"},{q="Who were the victims at the excavation site?",a="The victims were dwarven archaeologists and laborers sent by the Explorer's League to unearth titan artifacts. Raptor packs caught them off guard and slaughtered them when they overran the dig.",al={"who died at whelgar","excavation site victims"},it="history"},{q="Does killing Sarltooth secure the excavation site?",a="Killing Sarltooth removes the pack's deadliest threat and brings retribution for the fallen. Raptors still crawl over the trenches, leaving the site dangerous and largely abandoned.",al={"is whelgar safe now","did ormer win"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, avenging the Explorer's League crew slaughtered at Whelgar Excavation Site honors King Magni's fallen subjects.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face one of the Wetlands' apex predators. Keen tracking skills will guide you up the ridge to the pack leader.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure dwarven expeditions in the marshlands and keep Alliance footholds between Ironforge and the northern lands intact."},kw={"explorer's league","ormer ironbraid","raptors","sarltooth","talon","wetlands","whelgar excavation site"},rel={"npc:ormer-ironbraid","quest:299","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Ormer Ironbraid",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=296,ri={"Sarltooth's Talon"}},src={"Ormer's Revenge (3)"}}
E["quest:299"] = {t="quest",n="Uncovering the Past",z="wetlands",s="Prospector Whelgar needs the Goaz Stone's four missing pieces from his overrun dig in the Wetlands. Its inscriptions await translation.",h="Prospector Whelgar needs the Goaz Stone's four missing pieces from his overrun dig in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="The Broken Stone",b="Before raptors overran the dig in the Wetlands, Prospector Whelgar unearthed the Goaz Stone. His first attempts to read its ancient script found broken references to a divine plan and a doomed prophecy. Four pieces had broken away, leaving passages scattered across the dig.",sp=0},{t="Braving the Dig Site",b="To restore the stone, you search the raptor guarded excavation for four fragments: Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru. The pieces lie among loose soil and half excavated relics, watched by aggressive Razormaws and Scytheclaws. Reaching them means facing the marsh's fiercest predators.",sp=0},{t="Chained Beneath the Land",b="The reassembled Goaz Stone bears the language of the Titans. As Whelgar translates its glyphs, he reads a chilling phrase: 'Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.' The tablet speaks of struggles from the world's dawn and evils buried beneath Azeroth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Goaz Stone?",a="The Goaz Stone is an ancient Titan relic Prospector Whelgar found at his Wetlands excavation. Its cryptic inscriptions speak of a divine plan and ancient beings bound deep underground.",al={"goaz stone lore","what is the goaz tablet","tablet fragments wetlands"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who gives the quest Uncovering the Past?",a="Prospector Whelgar offers it from a vantage point overlooking Whelgar's Excavation Site, east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Feral raptors drove him from his dig.",al={"who starts uncovering the past","where to get uncovering the past"},it="identity"},{q="What fragments are needed to complete the tablet?",a="The four fragments are Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru. They are scattered among loose soil mounds and ancient urns across the raptor overrun quarry floor.",al={"which fragments","tablet piece names","ados modr golm neru"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why can't Prospector Whelgar recover the fragments himself?",a="Prospector Whelgar is an elderly dwarven scholar. When vicious raptors invaded and took over the quarry, he had to retreat and could not fight through their packs alone.",al={"why doesn't whelgar get the stones","why whelgar asks you"},it="why_me"},{q="What do the translated Titan glyphs reveal?",a="When the four pieces are joined, Whelgar translates the Titan script as 'Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.' The words hint at ancient cosmic beings imprisoned during Azeroth's shaping.",al={"what does the goaz stone say","titan translation wetlands","old gods chained beneath the land"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Does this quest tie into any other nearby expeditions?",a="Yes. Ormer Ironbraid's Ormer's Revenge sends adventurers to thin the raptors in the same excavation quarry.",al={"quests near excavation site","ormer ironbraid connection","ormer's revenge link"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Prospector Whelgar want the tablet fragments recovered?",a="Prospector Whelgar uncovered a massive relic known as the Goaz Stone shortly before raptors overran the excavation site. The translated portions of its Titan script speak direly of a \"divine plan\" and a \"doomed prophecy,\" but the inscription abruptly breaks off in four missing sections. Fearing that time is short, Whelgar is desperate to reassemble the entire tablet so he can decipher the rest of the message and uncover the secrets buried beneath the dig.",al={"whelgar motive","why find fragments","why does whelgar need fragments"},it="motive",add="2fe7ef8c"},{q="What are the Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru fragments?",a="The Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru fragments are the four missing pieces broken off from the Goaz Stone. Each fragment holds a section of ancient Titan script needed to complete the inscription. Once fitted back into the primary stone, they allow Prospector Whelgar to finish translating the text, revealing ominous passages concerning ancient entities chained beneath the earth.",al={"what are the fragments","ados modr golm neru","tablet fragments meaning"},sp=1,it="item",add="f38df7d0"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Explorers' League prizes every relic for what it can reveal about dwarven origins. The Titan inscriptions on the Goaz Stone touch that ancient heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you support League excavations across the Wetlands. They strengthen the Alliance's presence and preserve valuable knowledge from wild or hostile hands."},kw={"ados","goaz stone","golm","modr","neru","old gods","prospector whelgar","titans","uncovering the past","wetlands","whelgar's excavation site"},rel={"npc:prospector-whelgar","quest:294","topic:titan","topic:old-god","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Prospector Whelgar",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=299,ri={"Ados Fragment","Golm Fragment","Modr Fragment","Neru Fragment"}},src={"Uncovering the Past"}}
E["quest:303"] = {t="quest",n="The Dark Iron War",z="wetlands",s="At Dun Modr, on the Wetlands' northern edge, Motley Garmason leads a desperate defense. The Dark Iron clan holds the town after saboteurs shattered the Thandol Span, leaving the Ironforge Mountaineers with a tenuous line as they wait for reinforcements that may never come.",h="At Dun Modr, on the Wetlands' northern edge, Motley Garmason leads a desperate defense.",sec={{t="A Front at the Northern Gate",b="Dun Modr guarded the southern end of the colossal Thandol Span, the bridge linking Khaz Modan to Lordaeron. Dark Iron saboteurs and demolitionists shattered its archway, severing Alliance travel before they overran the stronghold. Motley Garmason and a handful of surviving defenders withdrew to an observation camp just outside town. Without a counterattack, the northern gateway risks permanent Dark Iron dominion.",sp=0},{t="Buying Time for the Reserves",b="Dwarven regiments are deployed to distant Alliance battlefields, leaving Motley's small detachment largely to fend for itself. His scouts try to signal Ironforge for relief, but communications falter and promised reserves remain out of sight. To buy time and disrupt the enemy's entrenchments, Motley orders surgical strikes into Dun Modr's ruins. The aim is to thin the ranks of Dark Iron engineers, tunnelers, and front-line soldiers before they push farther south into the Wetlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Motley Garmason?",a="Motley Garmason is an Ironforge Mountaineer officer commanding Dun Modr's surviving garrison. From a camp just outside the occupied town, he coordinates scouting and guerrilla strikes against the Dark Iron forces.",al={"motley garmason","who is motley","dun modr commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Dun Modr so important to Ironforge?",a="Dun Modr guards the southern foot of the Thandol Span. The span is the sole overland highway linking Khaz Modan to the Arathi Highlands and northern Lordaeron, so control of Dun Modr means control of ground travel and supplies between those regions.",al={"why dun modr matters","dun modr importance","dun modr lore"},it="place"},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves fighting in the Wetlands?",a="The Dark Iron clan has long sought to undermine their Bronzebeard cousins and weaken the Alliance. By invading the Wetlands and destroying the Thandol Span, they cut Ironforge's supply lines to the north and open a hostile second front behind Alliance borders.",al={"why are dark irons here","dark iron wetlands","dark iron war reason"},it="target"},{q="What happened to the Thandol Span?",a="Dark Iron tunnelers and demolitionists planted concentrated explosives in the Thandol Span's foundational arches, severely damaging the bridge. They meant to cut off Ironforge reinforcements from Lordaeron before overrunning Dun Modr.",al={"thandol span destroyed","who blew up the bridge","thandol span explosion"},it="history"},{q="Where are the Ironforge reserve forces?",a="Ironforge's military is stretched across campaigns abroad and defenses at home. Garmason's scout, Roggo, struggles to reach high command reliably, leaving the Dun Modr outpost to hold the line with whatever local allies it can find.",al={"ironforge reserves","where are reinforcements","roggo reserve"}},{q="What happens after pushing back the Dark Irons in Dun Modr?",a="Clearing the foot soldiers and sappers buys crucial time. Roggo's intelligence reveals that Kam Deepfury, held in the Stormwind Stockade, helped plan the attack on the Thandol Span, and Motley asks you to bring him Deepfury's head.",al={"next quest after dark iron war","the fury runs deep quest","what follows the dark iron war"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Motley Garmason want this done?",a="Motley is desperate to reclaim Dun Modr and halt the Dark Iron advance into the Wetlands before Ironforge's territory is entirely compromised. The Dark Irons have already blown apart the Thandol Span and overrun the town, severing vital links to the north. Motley hopes that by applying immediate offensive pressure to their lines, he can hold the front together long enough for Ironforge reinforcements to arrive and drive them back for good.",al={"motley garmason motive","why fight the dark irons","why clear dun modr"},it="motive",add="07a4003e"},{q="Why does Motley Garmason need your help instead of his own troops?",a="Ironforge's standing military is stretched to the breaking point, fighting far from home in foreign lands on behalf of the Alliance. Left behind with only a handful of defenders after the Thandol Span and Dun Modr fell, Motley has no fresh soldiers at hand. His scouts are failing to raise the reserves, leaving him no choice but to rely on capable travelers like you to carry the fight.",al={"why does motley need me","why aren't the guards fighting","where are ironforge troops"},it="why_me",add="b2f42bee"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard dwarf, you know Dun Modr's loss is a bitter humiliation and a direct threat to Khaz Modan's sovereignty. Vengeance against ancestral enemies is called for.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the Thandol Span's destruction and Dun Modr's fall sever overland access between Stormwind's northern allies and the southern kingdoms.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the Dark Iron saboteurs' specialized explosives reveal a chilling mastery of structural demolition."},kw={"bronzebeard","dark iron","demolitionists","dun modr","ironforge","motley garmason","saboteurs","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:378","quest:631","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Motley Garmason",["end"]="Motley Garmason",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=303},src={"The Dark Iron War"}}
E["quest:304"] = {t="quest",n="A Grim Task",z="wetlands",s="Longbraid the Grim seeks vengeance in the Wetlands after Dun Modr falls. The Dark Iron assault shattered the Thandol Span and took the lives of his brother and many soldiers. Now he wants Balgaras the Foul slain, with the warlock's ear as proof.",h="Longbraid the Grim seeks vengeance in the Wetlands after Dun Modr falls.",sec={{t="The Ruins of Dun Modr",b="The northern Wetlands are scarred by fighting between Ironforge Mountaineers and Dark Iron infiltrators. Dun Modr fell during the siege, and the western bridge of the Thandol Span was shattered. Longbraid the Grim lost many loyal soldiers and his brother in the assault. He wants the Dark Iron clan to pay for those deaths.",sp=0},{t="A Cowardly Commander",b="Scouts such as Roggo have found that Balgaras the Foul commands the Dark Iron force occupying Dun Modr. The warlock hides while ordering his soldiers to carry out his dark designs. Longbraid hopes Balgaras's death will break the force's resolve and let Ironforge's survivors secure the passage north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul is a Dark Iron warlock commanding the force occupying Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands. Longbraid the Grim calls him a coward who avoids direct combat while sending Dark Iron troops to hold the region.",al={"balgaras","who is balgaras","dark iron leader dun modr"},it="target"},{q="Who is Longbraid the Grim?",a="Longbraid the Grim is a dwarf commander encamped outside Dun Modr's ruins. Dark Iron forces seized the settlement and destroyed the Thandol Span's western crossing, killing his brother and many of his soldiers.",al={"longbraid","longbraid the grim","quest giver dun modr"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Longbraid want Balgaras's ear?",a="Longbraid wants Balgaras's ear as proof of the warlock's death. Balgaras is elusive and often hides from open battle.",al={"why ear","ear of balgaras"},it="item"},{q="What happened to the Thandol Span?",a="Dark Iron dwarves destroyed the western bridge of the Thandol Span during their surprise attack on Dun Modr. The crossing between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands is cut off.",al={"thandol span bridge destroyed","why is thandol span broken"},it="history"},{q="Where is Balgaras hiding?",a="Balgaras hides among the captured fortifications and ruins around Dun Modr, behind his soldiers rather than out in the marshlands.",al={"where is balgaras","find balgaras"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Balgaras is slain?",a="Longbraid believes Balgaras's death will make the remaining Dark Iron troops easier to defeat before another commander arrives to reinforce them.",al={"after a grim task","what next dun modr"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Longbraid the Grim want Balgaras killed?",a="Longbraid lost many soldiers during the battle of Dun Modr, including his own brother, who perished when the Dark Iron dwarves shattered the Thandol Span's western bridge. Balgaras commands the hostile Dark Iron forces in the Wetlands, directing attacks while hiding safely behind his minions. By executing the warlock, Longbraid seeks vengeance for his fallen kin and soldiers, hoping to break the command structure of the Dark Iron band and grant peace of mind to the survivors.",al={"why kill balgaras","longbraid motive","why does longbraid want this done"},it="motive",add="7a4e9943"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, the Dark Iron clan's violence at Dun Modr is a personal affront and a fresh wound in the clans' long civil strife.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know the Thandol Span is the main land route between Khaz Modan and Lordaeron. Removing the Dark Iron saboteurs matters to the whole Alliance.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know the dangerous ends to which the Dark Irons turn their craft: Balgaras the Foul uses fel magic to direct the slaughter of Dun Modr's defenders."},kw={"a grim task","balgaras the foul","dark iron","dun modr","longbraid the grim","roggo","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"npc:longbraid-the-grim","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Longbraid the Grim",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=304,ri={"Ear of Balgaras"}},src={"A Grim Task"}}
E["quest:305"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of The Excavation Team",z="wetlands",s="Tarrel Rockweaver waits in the Wetlands for word from Merrin at the Whelgar Excavation Site. His wife has missed two weeks of letters, and he fears disaster at the eastern dig.",h="Tarrel Rockweaver waits in the Wetlands for word from Merrin at the Whelgar Excavation Site.",sec={{t="A Husband's Dread",b="Tarrel Rockweaver has heard nothing from his wife, Merrin, for two weeks. From her post at the Whelgar Excavation Site, she used to send him weekly letters about the work. Now Tarrel fears calamity has struck the camp. With dwarf authorities stretched thin, he turns to passing scouts to learn whether the diggers are still alive.",sp=0},{t="The Whelgar Dig",b="The Whelgar Excavation Site lies east in the Wetlands, where dwarves dig for ancient Titan relics and history. Crews working in the wild can face beasts and threats from below. The site is far from the main roads, and whatever stopped the letters has left the diggers beyond easy reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver is a dwarf in the Wetlands, worried because his wife Merrin has stopped writing from the eastern excavation site. He takes passing adventurers for scouts sent to investigate the silence.",al={"tarrel rockweaver","quest giver","who gives in search of the excavation team"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is a dwarf archaeologist working with the Whelgar Excavation team east of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. She wrote regularly to her husband until something stopped her letters.",al={"merrin rockweaver","tarrel wife","who is merrin"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Whelgar Excavation Site?",a="The Whelgar Excavation Site lies east of Menethil Harbor and southwest of Dun Modr in the Wetlands, among rocky ridges far from the main road.",al={"excavation site location","where to find merrin","where is whelgar excavation"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why did Merrin stop sending letters?",a="Merrin stopped sending letters because a threat at the dig cut the researchers off from normal courier routes and camp life.",al={"why did letters stop","what happened to excavation team","why no mail"},it="motive"},{q="Who is the 'Longbraid' mentioned by Tarrel?",a="Longbraid is a dwarven authority who promised to send scouts to check on the Whelgar Excavation team if contact failed. Tarrel assumes any capable adventurer who arrives to help was sent by Longbraid.",al={"who is longbraid","longbraid scout"},it="people"},{q="Is the excavation site safe to approach?",a="No. The Whelgar Excavation Site lies in dangerous Wetlands wilderness, and whatever stopped the team's weekly letters threatens anyone who reaches the dig.",al={"is the dig safe","whelgar dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Tarrel Rockweaver need an adventurer to find the excavation team?",a="Tarrel is fraught with worry in Menethil Harbor, but he is not an armed explorer or soldier capable of trekking through the perilous marshlands alone. Local officials like Longbraid promised to arrange an experienced scout to investigate the silence from the dig site. When you arrive, Tarrel seizes upon you as the capable help he was promised to brave the wilderness and check on his wife.",al={"why send me","why not guards","why cant tarrel go"},it="why_me",add="d2e8931d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Explorers' League takes pride in uncovering ancient history. The distress of your kin at the Whelgar Excavation calls for your attention.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know dwarven outposts and research across the marshlands help guard the Wetlands from the dangers of the wild."},kw={"explorers league","in search of the excavation team","longbraid","merrin rockweaver","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands","whelgar excavation"},rel={"npc:tarrel-rockweaver","npc:merrin-rockweaver","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Tarrel Rockweaver",["end"]="Merrin Rockweaver",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=305},src={"In Search of The Excavation Team"}}
E["quest:306"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of The Excavation Team",z="wetlands",s="Merrin Rockweaver sends word from the Whelgar's Excavation site after mottled raptors overrun the dig. Her letter tells Tarrel Rockweaver that she survived, while most of the expedition did not.",h="Merrin Rockweaver sends word from the Whelgar's Excavation site after mottled raptors overrun the dig.",sec={{t="A Message from the Ruins",b="Merrin Rockweaver has a report for you from the ridge above Whelgar's Excavation site. The team was uncovering rare artifacts and massive prehistoric fossils when packs of mottled raptors swept through the dig. Most of the crew died in the attack. Merrin and the other survivors remain cut off from Menethil Harbor.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Relief",b="At Menethil Harbor, Tarrel Rockweaver learns that his wife survived with at least two companions. Ormer's courage helped them escape, easing Tarrel's fear. The deaths of so many colleagues still weigh on the town and its frontier spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the excavation team in the Wetlands?",a="Packs of mottled raptors overran the dwarven expedition while it uncovered rare artifacts and massive ancient bones. Most of the diggers were slain, and a handful survived on the bluffs above the site.",al={"what happened to dig site","wetlands excavation disaster","why did excavation fail"},it="history"},{q="Who saved Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver credits Ormer with fighting off the raptors and escorting her and the Prospector to safety on the ridge.",al={"who saved merrin","ormer rockweaver","who is ormer"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver is Merrin's husband, waiting in Menethil Harbor. Worried by the silence from the dig site, he sought travelers to learn what had happened to her.",al={"who is tarrel","tarrel rockweaver location"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the dig site located?",a="The excavation site lies inland in the Wetlands, east of Menethil Harbor and southwest of Dun Modr.",al={"where is excavation","whelgar excavation location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What was the expedition digging for?",a="The team was digging for rare subterranean artifacts and large prehistoric fossils buried in the marshes under the direction of dwarven prospectors.",al={"what were they digging for","excavation artifacts"},it="purpose"},{q="Are there other survivors beside Merrin?",a="Yes. Merrin says Ormer and the chief Prospector escaped with her, making three known survivors.",al={"who else survived","excavation survivors"},it="residents"},{q="Why does Merrin Rockweaver want you to deliver her letter?",a="Merrin wants to reassure her husband Tarrel that she survived the savage attack on the dig site. The raptors overran their camp and slaughtered many of the archaeologists, leaving Merrin, Prospector Whelgar, and Ormer trapped in a makeshift shelter. Unable to break through the beasts themselves, she entrusts you with her letter so Tarrel learns they are alive and understands the grim fate of the expedition.",al={"why send merrins letter","merrin rockweaver motive","why deliver the note to tarrel"},it="motive",add="2f0bde8f"},{q="Why can't Merrin Rockweaver deliver the note herself?",a="Merrin and her fellow survivors are cut off and pinned down by aggressive mottled raptors. Leaving their shelter would expose them to the ferocious beasts that already tore through the rest of the excavation team. As an able-bodied traveler capable of cutting through the marshes and raptor packs, you can safely carry word back to Menethil Harbor when they cannot.",al={"why does merrin need me","why cant merrin leave the dig site","why does merrin need help"},it="why_me",add="f4e86a28"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the dangers King Magni's explorers face far from Ironforge. The disaster strikes at dwarven hopes of exploring the past.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know wild beasts threaten settlements and work across the Wetlands."},kw={"excavation","menethil harbor","merrin rockweaver","mottled raptors","ormer","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:305","npc:merrin-rockweaver","npc:tarrel-rockweaver","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Merrin Rockweaver",["end"]="Tarrel Rockweaver",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=306},src={"In Search of The Excavation Team (2)"}}
E["quest:321"] = {t="quest",n="Lightforge Iron",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Harbor, Glorin Steelbrow seeks the lost cargo of an elven destroyer. The Flying Osprey carried rare Lightforge iron when it sank with the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras during the Second War.",h="In Menethil Harbor, Glorin Steelbrow seeks the lost cargo of an elven destroyer.",sec={{t="A Sacred Cargo",b="The Flying Osprey sailed from Lordaeron with the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras. The elven destroyer carried a precious cargo of Lightforge iron and traveled beside the fleet for safety. But the Dragonmaw clan's enslaved red dragons swept down from the sky. They set the fleet ablaze, sending sailors and sanctified metal beneath the waves.",sp=0},{t="Plundered by the Tides",b="South of Menethil Harbor, the shattered Flying Osprey lies beneath the water. Its chest has been battered open and clawed through. Coastal murlocs scavenged the wreck and scattered the ingots, leaving little of the precious ore Glorin Steelbrow seeks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Flying Osprey?",a="The Flying Osprey was an elven destroyer sailing from Lordaeron during the Second War. It carried rare Lightforge iron alongside the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras for safety, until Dragonmaw's enslaved red dragons burned and sank the fleet.",al={"flying osprey lore","elven destroyer wetlands","what ship had the iron"}},{q="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarf stationed at Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. He seeks historical salvage and valuable materials from the sunken ships along the coast, especially legendary metals like Lightforge iron.",al={"glorin steelbrow","dwarf in menethil","who gives lightforge iron"},it="identity"},{q="What is Lightforge iron?",a="Lightforge iron is a rare, sanctified metal used to forge consecrated arms and armor. Smiths and champions of the Holy Light value its purity and spiritual resilience.",al={"lightforge metal","what is lightforge iron","lightforge ingots"},it="item"},{q="Why were the ships sunk in the Wetlands?",a="During the Second War, the Horde's Dragonmaw clan used the Demon Soul to enslave the Red Dragonflight. Dragonriders attacked Kul Tiras's Third Fleet off the Wetlands coast, burning the ships and sending them to the ocean floor.",al={"who sunk the third fleet","why are ships wrecked wetlands","red dragons wetlands fleet"},it="history"},{q="Why is the chest nearly empty?",a="Coastal murlocs clawed open the waterlogged chest aboard the Flying Osprey and plundered its cargo. Most of the ingots are gone, scattered along the marshy shore.",al={"where are the ingots","why claw marks on chest","who stole the lightforge iron"}},{q="Where is the wreckage of the Flying Osprey located?",a="The Flying Osprey lies among the coastal shoals just south of Menethil Harbor, along the western shore of the Wetlands. Its wreckage is split across the shallows near local murloc settlements.",al={"flying osprey location","where is the chest","wetlands shipwreck location"},gp=true},{q="Why does Glorin Steelbrow want Lightforge iron?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a priest seeking to recover the rare metal to prepare a weapon against Morbent Fel. The sunken cargo of the Flying Osprey offers a rare opportunity to salvage Lightforge iron, a precious elven commodity lost since the Second War. By sending you to recover it, he hopes to gather enough workable metal to craft arms worthy of its enduring legend.",al={"why glorin wants iron","glorin steelbrow lightforge iron motive","why find lightforge iron"},it="motive",add="915ea990"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see why smiths revere Lightforge iron. They prize its powerful blessings and unmatched structural integrity.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you know weapons made from Lightforge iron are deeply attuned to the Holy Light. Recovering even one lost ingot carries spiritual weight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the sunken ships off Menethil Harbor as solemn memorials to the Second War. Sailors from Kul Tiras and Lordaeron fell to dragonfire there."},kw={"flying osprey","glorin steelbrow","ingot","kul tiras","lightforge iron","menethil harbor","murloc","third fleet","waterlogged chest","wetlands"},rel={"npc:glorin-steelbrow","quest:270","quest:324","quest:288","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Glorin Steelbrow",["end"]="Waterlogged Chest",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=321},src={"Lightforge Iron (quest)"}}
E["quest:324"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Ingots",z="wetlands",s="Glorin Steelbrow needs Lightforge iron from a shipwreck off the Wetlands. The chest holds only one ingot, and the Bluegill murlocs have taken the rest.",h="Glorin Steelbrow needs Lightforge iron from a shipwreck off the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Plundered Shipwreck",b="The Flying Osprey lies broken off the Wetlands shore. Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarven priest, sent you to recover its Lightforge iron. The waterlogged chest in the cargo hold holds only a single ingot. Bluegill murlocs near the wreck have scavenged the rest of the shipment.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Sacred Metal",b="Lightforge iron is rare metal suited to sacred smithing. Glorin Steelbrow needs it for a weapon, so the bars cannot be left in Bluegill camps. Hunt the Bluegill raiders in the shallows near the broken hull and reclaim the scattered ingots for Glorin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What ship carried the Lightforge iron?",a="The Flying Osprey carried the Lightforge iron before it sank off the Wetlands coast. Its broken timbers lie partly submerged in the shallows.",al={"which ship","flying osprey","shipwreck name"},it="history"},{q="Why were the ingots not in the chest?",a="Only one ingot remained in the waterlogged chest. Bluegill murlocs had scavenged the rest of the shipment from the wreck.",al={"where are the ingots","why are murlocs holding iron","chest empty"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven priest of the Church of the Holy Light in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. A colleague of Bishop Farthing, he seeks Lightforge iron for a weapon to use against the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"glorin","who is glorin steelbrow","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What is special about Lightforge iron?",a="Lightforge iron is rare metal suited to holy enchantments and sacred smithing. Artisans use it to craft weapons aligned with the Holy Light.",al={"lightforge iron lore","what is lightforge iron","why is the iron important"},it="item"},{q="Which murlocs took the iron?",a="Bluegill murloc raiders took the missing bars. They prowl the shallows and beaches around the Flying Osprey wreck.",al={"who stole the ingots","which tribe","bluegill raiders"},it="target"},{q="What comes next after returning the ingots?",a="After Glorin Steelbrow receives all the ingots, he packs the sanctified metal in a crate and sends you to weaponsmith Grimand Elmore in Stormwind. There, the metal is forged in Blessed Arm.",al={"next quest","what does glorin do","blessed arm quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, recovering lost masterwork ore for a dwarven priest like Glorin Steelbrow honors your people's tradition of craftsmanship and reclaiming what was lost.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, recovering Lightforge iron helps preserve holy metal for weapons that champion the Light.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know the loss of fine Lightforge iron to a coastal murloc nest, where it lies unused instead of being worked at an anvil."},kw={"bluegill","flying osprey","glorin steelbrow","ingots","lightforge iron","murloc","waterlogged chest","wetlands"},rel={"quest:321","quest:322","npc:glorin-steelbrow","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc"},m={start="Waterlogged Chest",["end"]="Glorin Steelbrow",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=324},src={"The Lost Ingots"}}
E["quest:463"] = {t="quest",n="The Greenwarden",z="wetlands",s="First Mate Fitzsimmons sends Alliance travelers from Menethil Harbor northeast into the Wetlands marshes. They seek a mysterious being rumored to dwell among the beasts.",h="First Mate Fitzsimmons sends Alliance travelers from Menethil Harbor northeast into the Wetlands marshes.",sec={{t="Tavern Rumors and Bog Tales",b="Sailors and wanderers at Menethil Harbor trade stories of a beast lurking in the swamp. First Mate Fitzsimmons describes the Greenwarden as an appetite with legs and calls those who seek it gullible. Leave the dry road, he warns, and “ol’ Greenie” will bite you in two. To the folk on the docks, anything huge in the murky waters is another man-eating danger in the marsh.",sp=0},{t="The Guardian of the Marsh",b="East of the fork toward Dun Modr, Rethiel watches over the Wetlands as the Greenwarden. This towering ancient is bound to the wild growth there, not a mindless carnivore. From afar, he watches the sorrow of the spoiled land and calls on willing mortals to cleanse the blighted marsh.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Greenwarden?",a="The Greenwarden is Rethiel, an ancient nature guardian in the Wetlands. Sailors along the coast mistake him for a savage monster, but he protects the plants and wildlife.",al={"who is greenwarden","greenwarden identity","who is rethiel"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is in the marshlands east of the main road, near the fork toward Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands.",al={"greenwarden location","where is rethiel","greenwarden coordinates"},gp=true},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons think the Greenwarden is dangerous?",a="Fitzsimmons knows only the tavern rumors and superstitions of Menethil Harbor. With beasts overrunning the Wetlands, sailors assume any giant among the crocodiles and predators is a man-eating brute.",al={"why is fitzsimmons scared","is the greenwarden evil"},it="threat"},{q="What does Rethiel want with travelers?",a="Rethiel seeks champions to tend the Wetlands, which he says weep from festered wounds. He directs travelers to protect the wildlife and quell threats to the local ecosystem.",al={"what does the greenwarden do","rethiel purpose","why meet the greenwarden"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after finding the Greenwarden?",a="When you speak with Rethiel, he says nature speaks well of you, then gives you “Tramping Paws” to help with the troubles in the marsh.",al={"next quest after greenwarden","tramping paws quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Does this quest require fighting anything to complete?",a="No. You need only survive the trek through the Wetlands and speak with Rethiel at his grove in the marsh.",al={"greenwarden combat","do i fight greenwarden"},gp=true},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons send you to the Greenwarden?",a="Fitzsimmons doesn't have a personal stake or noble mission; he simply thinks you are an utter fool for asking about the creature. Convinced that anyone chasing rumors of 'the beast' is marching straight toward their doom, he cynically points you toward the marsh to satisfy your death wish—while jokingly offering to hold onto your gold before you get bitten in half.",al={"fitzsimmons motive","why send to greenwarden","why does fitzsimmons want greenwarden found"},it="motive",add="e3605feb"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Dockworkers may see Rethiel as a swamp monster, but druids recognize an ancient guardian attuned to nature’s balance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf far from Kalimdor, you may find a familiar, comforting echo of nature’s ancient wardens in the damp, muddy soils of Khaz Modan."},kw={"dun modr","fitzsimmons","greenwarden","menethil","rethiel","tramping paws","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","quest:276","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",["end"]="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=463},src={"The Greenwarden"}}
E["quest:464"] = {t="quest",n="War Banners",z="wetlands",s="At Menethil Harbor, Captain Stoutfist sends Alliance champions against Dragonmaw orcs gathering strength in the Wetlands. He wants their war banners claimed from a camp northeast of town.",h="At Menethil Harbor, Captain Stoutfist sends Alliance champions against Dragonmaw orcs gathering strength in...",sec={{t="Remnants of the Dragonmaw",b="The Dragonmaw clan once held the red dragonflight captive at Grim Batol during the Second War. When that control broke, the freed dragons hunted their captors nearly to extinction. The few orcs who survived fled Grim Batol into the high mountains east of Whelgar's Excavation, hiding from the red flight's wrath.",sp=0},{t="A Rising Encampment",b="Dragonmaw survivors have gathered again northeast of Menethil Harbor. They have raised a war camp and planted crimson standards in the marsh. Captain Stoutfist sees danger in an armed orc force so near the harbor town. He wants their ranks cut down and their banners torn away as proof of defeat.",sp=0},{t="The Legacy of Nekros",b="Nek'rosh leads the regrouped Dragonmaw orcs. He is the son of Nekros, the warlock who once commanded captive red dragons through dark sorcery. When that magic failed, Nekros was torn apart by the dragons he had held. His son now commands the survivors, consumed by vengeance against the great beasts that killed his father.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands?",a="The Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands are survivors of a clan that enslaved the red dragonflight during the Second War. The freed dragons hunted them, scattering those who survived Grim Batol into the mountains and marshes.",al={"dragonmaw orcs wetlands","who are dragonmaw","wetlands orcs"},it="people"},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist want their war banners?",a="Captain Stoutfist wants their banners as proof that Alliance soldiers have struck the camp and weakened its fighting strength. The encampment northeast of Menethil Harbor threatens the town.",al={"why collect banners","captain stoutfist banners"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to the Dragonmaw clan's dragons?",a="When the dark magic holding them failed, the red dragons turned on their Dragonmaw captors. They hunted the orcs across Khaz Modan and decimated the clan.",al={"what happened to the dragons","dragonmaw dragons"},it="history"},{q="Who leads the Dragonmaw clan now?",a="Nek'rosh leads the Dragonmaw survivors. He is Nekros's son and has rallied the orcs in vengeance against the red dragons who killed his father.",al={"dragonmaw leader","who is nek'rosh"},sp=1,it="leader"},{q="Where did the Dragonmaw hide before setting up this camp?",a="After fleeing Grim Batol, the surviving orcs hid in the rugged mountains east of Whelgar's Excavation. They later entered the Wetlands marsh and built their camp.",al={"where did dragonmaw hide","dragonmaw refuge"},it="place"},{q="Are these Dragonmaw orcs affiliated with Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Dragonmaw remnants act outside Warchief Thrall's new Horde in Kalimdor. They are renegades driven by vengeance and survival.",al={"are dragonmaw in horde","dragonmaw thrall horde"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Dragonmaw War Banner for?",a="To Captain Stoutfist, the war banners serve as undeniable physical proof that you struck into the heart of the Dragonmaw encampment. For the orcs, these standards represent their clan's renewed unity and martial defiance under Nek'rosh. Stripping them away not only demoralizes the re-emerging clan, but also verifies to the defenders of Menethil Harbor that their numbers and fortifications have taken a direct, punishing blow.",al={"dragonmaw war banner use","why collect banners","what are the war banners"},it="item",add="33d8bd47"},{q="Who are you sent against in this mission?",a="You are sent against the remnants of the Dragonmaw clan, savage orcs who survived the destruction of Grim Batol and the vengeance of the red dragons. Having regrouped in the mountains, they have pushed westward into the Wetlands and established a fortified war camp northeast of Menethil Harbor. Left unchecked, their growing numbers and relentless bloodlust pose a direct threat to the marsh roads and the harbor itself.",al={"who are we attacking","dragonmaw encampment target","who do i fight"},it="target",add="70d8988a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can see why Captain Stoutfist wants the Dragonmaw driven from Menethil Harbor's vicinity. Their camp threatens the shipping corridor linking Stormwind, Ironforge, and the northern realms.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Dragonmaw defiled the ancient stronghold of Grim Batol and brought war to the mountains around it. Each Dragonmaw warrior who falls brings a measure of long-delayed justice.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face hardened veterans of the Second War in their camp. They fight with reckless force, even without their draconic mounts."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","grim batol","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","nekros","war banners","wetlands"},rel={"npc:captain-stoutfist","quest:465","quest:473","subzone:grim-batol","zone:wetlands","topic:second-war"},m={start="Captain Stoutfist",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=464,ri={"Dragonmaw War Banner"}},src={"War Banners"}}
E["quest:465"] = {t="quest",n="Nek'rosh's Gambit",z="wetlands",s="At Menethil Harbor, Captain Stoutfist fears a Dragonmaw siege. Chieftain Nek'rosh has built engines to bombard the vulnerable port town, while fighting at Dun Algaz cuts off reinforcements. You are sent into the marshes to destroy the catapults before the attack begins.",h="At Menethil Harbor, Captain Stoutfist fears a Dragonmaw siege.",sec={{t="A Looming Siege",b="Dwarven scouts uncovered Nek'rosh's plan as Alliance fighters clashed with Dragonmaw raiders. The chieftain has overseen the building of full-scale siege catapults in the Wetlands encampments. He means to bring the engines to Menethil Harbor and batter its fortress walls, threatening the Alliance's main shipping hub on the western coast.",sp=0},{t="Cut Off at Dun Algaz",b="Fighting and greenskin activity have congested the mountain passes at Dun Algaz, isolating the lowlands from Ironforge's main garrisons. Without aid from Khaz Modan, Captain Stoutfist cannot spare troops to guard the harbor's perimeter. Menethil's survival depends on sabotaging the catapults before they can be brought against the town.",sp=0},{t="Fire in the Encampment",b="Scouts carry Dwarven Tinder into the heart of the Dragonmaw encampment. They must set the timber catapults ablaze and destroy them, stripping Nek'rosh of his artillery and denying his warriors the firepower to break Menethil's defenses. The engines must be ruined before the warlord himself can be confronted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nek'rosh?",a="Nek'rosh is the ruthless chieftain leading the remnants of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. He is directing a campaign to besiege Menethil Harbor.",al={"nekrosh","chieftain nek'rosh","who is nek rosh"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Menethil Harbor in such danger?",a="Menethil Harbor depends on naval trade and lies apart from Ironforge. Fighting congests the passes at Dun Algaz, blocking reinforcements by land and leaving the town unable to withstand a concentrated siege.",al={"menethil danger","why harbor vulnerable","threat to menethil"},it="threat"},{q="What is the goal of this mission?",a="You carry Dwarven Tinder into the Dragonmaw encampment to set their siege catapults ablaze and destroy them before they can be brought against Menethil Harbor.",al={"gambit objective","what do i do","catapult mission"},it="purpose"},{q="Who issues this assignment?",a="Captain Stoutfist gives the orders. The dwarf officer coordinates the harbor's local defense and the campaign against the Dragonmaw.",al={"quest giver","who gives nekrosh gambit","stoutfist role"},it="in_charge"},{q="What follows the destruction of the catapults?",a="After the catapults are destroyed, the threat must be ended by tracking down and executing Chieftain Nek'rosh himself.",al={"after catapults","next quest","what next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why can't Ironforge send troops to help Menethil?",a="The road from Loch Modan to the Wetlands runs through Dun Algaz. Hostile forces contest and ambush the pass, cutting off reliable ground travel.",al={"dun algaz block","why no reinforcements","ironforge help"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist want the catapults destroyed?",a="Captain Stoutfist discovered that Nek'rosh has constructed siege weaponry specifically to bombard and conquer Menethil Harbor. Because the fighting at Dun Algaz cuts the harbor off from Ironforge reinforcements, the settlement cannot withstand an organized artillery assault. Stoutfist needs those siege engines eliminated before the Dragonmaw can march on the town.",al={"stoutfist motive","why destroy catapults","why does stoutfist need this done"},it="motive",add="98c43a31"},{q="What are you targeting in the Dragonmaw encampment?",a="You are sent into the heart of the Dragonmaw encampment to locate and burn their newly built catapults. These crude siege engines pose an immediate existential threat to Menethil Harbor, giving the orcs the destructive power to shatter the town's defenses from afar.",al={"what are the targets","dragonmaw catapults target","who am i sent against"},it="target",add="837e41fd"},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist send an adventurer instead of his guards?",a="Menethil Harbor's garrison is stretched thin guarding the town against constant attacks and natural hazards, while reinforcements remain trapped behind the contested passes of Dun Algaz. Stoutfist cannot spare a detachment of his few remaining town guards for a deep infiltration raid into enemy territory, making an independent adventurer his best chance to sabotage the encampment.",al={"why me","why send me","why not send guards"},it="why_me",add="68f35499"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard dwarf, you know Menethil Harbor is your people's gateway to the western sea. Losing it to Dragonmaw siege weapons would cripple Ironforge's maritime connections.",["faction:Alliance"]="With fighting locking down Dun Algaz, the Alliance must depend on brave volunteers to disrupt the Dragonmaw war machine.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you rely on aggressive frontline tactics and brutal hand-to-hand fighting to storm an entrenched enemy camp and destroy its heavy siege artillery."},kw={"captain stoutfist","catapults","dragonmaw","dun algaz","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","nek'rosh's gambit","wetlands"},rel={"quest:464","quest:474","npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Captain Stoutfist",["end"]="Dragonmaw Catapult",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=465},src={"Nek'rosh's Gambit"}}
E["quest:469"] = {t="quest",n="Daily Delivery",z="wetlands",s="Einar Stonegrip keeps to the Wetlands while his hides make their way to Menethil Harbor. He asks travelers bound for town to carry cured crocolisk hides to a local tanner.",h="Einar Stonegrip keeps to the Wetlands while his hides make their way to Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Reluctant Courier",b="Einar Stonegrip hunts the wildlife of the Wetlands, especially the aggressive crocolisks along its waterways. He gathers plenty of valuable skins, but taking them home means traveling to Menethil Harbor. With his marriage to Sida going through a rough patch, Einar would rather remain in the field than face her. He hands his parcels to travelers passing toward town.",sp=0},{t="Commerce in Menethil",b="James Halloran tans hides in Menethil Harbor. Local hunters supply him with leather for boots and goods that merchants and sailors passing through the port can use. Einar has been away for a week, and Halloran guesses a quarrel with Sida explains the delivery by proxy. He wonders if his own wife should step in and make peace with her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Einar Stonegrip deliver the skins himself?",a="Einar says his wife, Sida, has been in foul humor lately. He stays in the Wetlands and asks passing travelers to carry his deliveries into Menethil Harbor to avoid facing her temper.",al={"why einar hiding","einar wife problem","why won't einar go home"},it="motive"},{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran tans leather in Menethil Harbor. He buys raw pelts and hides from local trappers, then cures them and sells boots and finished leather goods.",al={"halloran tanner","who is james halloran"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Sida?",a="Sida is Einar Stonegrip's wife, and she lives in Menethil Harbor. Her sour mood is why Einar stays in the marshes instead of going home.",al={"einar wife","who is sida"},it="people"},{q="What kind of skins are being transported?",a="The bundle holds crocolisk skins taken from the large reptiles in the Wetlands' bogs and waterways.",al={"what skins","daily delivery items"},it="item"},{q="Does Halloran know why Einar is avoiding Menethil Harbor?",a="Yes. When you hand over the bundle, Halloran says Einar has not visited in nearly a week and guesses trouble with Sida is the cause.",al={"does halloran know","tanner reaction"},it="ties"},{q="Where does this delivery take place?",a="The delivery starts with Einar Stonegrip along a road in the Wetlands and ends at James Halloran's workshop in Menethil Harbor on the western coast.",al={"where turn in","daily delivery location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you pass through Menethil Harbor, the maritime gateway between Ironforge's domain and the northern continents. Crocolisk leather helps outfit local guards and dockhands.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you make your trade in the Wetlands' lowlands, far from Ironforge. Einar's trouble at home keeps him in the marshes, where he hunts crocolisks and sends travelers with his hides."},kw={"crocolisk skins","einar stonegrip","james halloran","menethil harbor","sida","tanner","wetlands"},rel={"npc:einar-stonegrip","npc:james-halloran","npc:sida","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Einar Stonegrip",["end"]="James Halloran",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=469},src={"Daily Delivery"}}
E["quest:470"] = {t="quest",n="Digging Through the Ooze",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Harbor, Sida asks travelers to recover her bag from the ooze that swallowed it. She visits Ironbeard's Tomb regularly, but fled when foul oozes filled the barrows.",h="In Menethil Harbor, Sida asks travelers to recover her bag from the ooze that swallowed it.",sec={{t="A Panicked Retreat",b="Sida lives in Menethil Harbor and often travels northeast into the Wetlands to pay homage at Ironbeard's Tomb. On her latest visit, foul, dripping oozes had filled the ancient barrow. She panicked and hurled her satchel at one of them. The ooze swallowed the bag whole, giving Sida just enough time to flee back to the port town. Now she asks travelers to search for it.",sp=0},{t="Sludge of Ironbeard's Tomb",b="Ironbeard's Tomb lies near Dun Modr, the contested stronghold, and holds the remains of a storied dwarven hero. Corruption in the surrounding marshland draws amorphous, acidic slimes that consume anything in their path. Sida cannot remember which creature swallowed her belongings. Travelers must search the tomb grounds and cut through the creeping blight to find her drenched satchel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sida?",a="Sida is an Alliance traveler who lives in Menethil Harbor. She regularly visits Ironbeard's Tomb in the Wetlands, where oozes recently drove her into danger.",al={"sida","who gives quest","who is sida"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Ironbeard's Tomb lies in the northeastern Wetlands, south of Dun Modr. Corrosive wetland oozes infest the area around the stone barrow.",al={"ironbeard tomb location","where is ironbeard","where are the oozes"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Which ooze swallowed Sida's bag?",a="Sida panicked during the attack and cannot tell the oozes apart. Any of the slimes wandering outside Ironbeard's Tomb may have swallowed her bag.",al={"which ooze","ooze with bag","where is the bag"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why was Sida visiting Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Sida visits Ironbeard's Tomb each week to pay her respects to the ancient dwarf buried there. Oozes interrupted her peaceful tradition.",al={"why sida visit tomb","sida weekly visit"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after the bag is recovered?",a="When you return the slimy satchel to Menethil Harbor, Sida empties its contents onto the ground to retrieve her belongings. She finds the ruined container too repulsive to keep and offers the cleaned-off bag to whoever recovered it.",al={"what was in the bag","bag reward"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this related to the Dark Iron dwarves nearby?",a="Dun Modr, just north of the tomb, is caught up in conflict with the Dark Iron clan. The oozes at Ironbeard's Tomb are wild marsh predators native to the Wetlands' damp, rotting corners, not dwarven soldiers.",al={"dark iron connection","dun modr connection"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Sida need her bag back?",a="While making her weekly visit to Ironbeard's Tomb, Sida was ambushed by foul oozes. Panicking, she threw her pack at one of the creatures to distract it and make her escape. Although she survived the encounter unharmed, the contents inside her bag are irreplaceable to her, leaving her desperate to recover them before the acidic monstrosities digest them completely.",al={"why does sida want her bag","sida bag motive","why get sida's bag"},it="motive",add="93b8c575"},{q="What is inside Sida's Bag?",a="Sida never openly reveals exactly what was kept inside the bag, only insisting that she urgently needs its contents returned. When you bring it back, she immediately dumps the slimy contents onto the ground and scoops them up, handing you the ruined, ooze-coated container as a reward since she no longer has any use for the soiled leather.",al={"what is in sidas bag","sida bag contents","what is sida's bag for"},it="item",add="11eb18cd"},{q="What are the oozes at Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="The slimes creeping around Ironbeard's Tomb are mindless, ravenous monstrosities typical of the damp, decaying corners of the Wetlands. Drawn to the sunken ruin and rotting matter near Dun Modr, they consume anything organic in their path—including unsuspecting visitors like Sida.",al={"oozes at ironbeard's tomb","why are oozes at ironbeards tomb","ironbeard tomb oozes"},it="target",add="7f85207a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Ironbeard's Tomb holds the remains of an honored dwarven ancestor. For a Bronzebeard loyalist, foul oozes defiling the barrows are an affront.",["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor is the Alliance's main lifeline through the treacherous Wetlands. Helping rattled citizens keeps the vital port secure and orderly."},kw={"dun modr","ironbeard's tomb","menethil harbor","ooze","ooze-covered bag","sida","sida's bag","wetlands"},rel={"npc:sida","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr"},m={start="Sida",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=470,ri={"Sida's Bag"}},src={"Digging Through the Ooze"}}
E["quest:471"] = {t="quest",n="Apprentice's Duties",z="wetlands",s="James Halloran needs giant crocolisk hides after his apprentice is mauled in the marshes. The tanner in Menethil Harbor asks travelers to finish the dangerous harvest.",h="James Halloran needs giant crocolisk hides after his apprentice is mauled in the marshes.",sec={{t="A Harsh Apprenticeship",b="James Halloran sent his young apprentice into the Wetlands marshes to skin giant crocolisks. When the boy did not return, Halloran searched for him and found him badly mauled by the beasts. Menethil Harbor's tradesmen depend on materials from the surrounding country, where the bogs make such work dangerous.",sp=0},{t="Skins and Retribution",b="The town midwife believes Halloran's apprentice will survive, though the attack cost him a leg. Halloran needs hides for his trade and wants vengeance on the beasts that tore into the boy he loves like a son. He asks travelers to go north along the coast, past the murloc hovels, and hunt the giant crocolisks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a leatherworker and tanner in Menethil Harbor. He depends on hides gathered from Wetlands wildlife to keep his craft going.",al={"james halloran","who gives apprentice duties","menethil tanner"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Halloran's apprentice?",a="Halloran sent his apprentice into the marsh to gather giant crocolisk hides. The beasts mauled the boy and took his leg, but the town midwife expects him to survive.",al={"what happened to apprentice","who got mauled","apprentice leg"},it="conflict"},{q="Where are the giant crocolisks located?",a="Giant crocolisks prowl the Wetlands marshes and northern coast, beyond the coastal murloc settlements north of Menethil Harbor.",al={"where are giant crocs","crocolisk location wetlands","giant crocolisk spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What prerequisite quest leads to this task?",a="Before this, Halloran asked travelers to hunt smaller crocolisks in 'Young Crocolisk Skins.' Now he asks them to hunt the giant variety that wounded his apprentice.",al={"prereq for apprentice duties","previous quest","crocolisk quest chain"},gp=true},{q="Why does Halloran still want the skins after the tragedy?",a="Halloran needs hides to keep his trade supplied, and he is angry at the beasts that maimed the boy he loves like a son. He welcomes a traveler willing to hunt and kill them.",al={"why need skins","halloran motivation"},it="motive"},{q="Does Halloran offer you an apprenticeship?",a="Halloran briefly jokes about taking you on as his new apprentice after seeing your work, then dismisses the idea. You are far too old, he says, and clearly bound for a different destiny.",al={"can i become apprentice","apprentice offer"},it="for_you"},{q="What is the Giant Crocolisk Skin for?",a="James Halloran is a tanner and leatherworker based in Menethil Harbor. He crafts tough goods from the hides of local beasts, and the sturdy, thick leather harvested from the Wetlands' giant crocolisks is raw material for his trade.",al={"giant crocolisk skin use","why skins","halloran crocolisk skin"},it="item",add="af87185e"},{q="What are the giant crocolisks?",a="They are massive, predatory reptiles native to the marshes and coastal waters of the Wetlands. Fiercely territorial and notoriously aggressive, they dwell north along the coast beyond the murloc camps, posing a deadly hazard to any traveler or novice skinner who wanders too close.",al={"giant crocolisks wetlands","what are giant crocs","crocolisks in wetlands"},it="target",add="4e327c1e"},{q="Why does James Halloran need you instead of handling it himself?",a="Halloran's own apprentice was mauled and lost a leg while attempting the task, proving far too dangerous for an ordinary craftsman. With his apprentice in critical care under the local midwife, Halloran remains in Menethil Harbor to mind his shop and watch over the boy, turning to an armed adventurer to safely cull the beasts.",al={"why cant halloran get skins","why me halloran","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="42f5987b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor links Khaz Modan with the rest of the Alliance. The port depends on the safety and self-sufficiency of its local craftsmen.",["class:Hunter"]="Giant crocolisks are formidable marsh predators. Tracking them tests your skill at finding your way through murky waters and aggressive wildlife."},kw={"apprentice's duties","crocolisk","giant crocolisk","james halloran","leatherworking","menethil harbor","murloc hovels","wetlands","young crocolisk skins"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","quest:484","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:murloc"},m={start="James Halloran",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=471,ri={"Giant Crocolisk Skin"}},src={"Apprentice's Duties"}}
E["quest:472"] = {t="quest",n="Fall of Dun Modr",z="wetlands",s="At Dun Modr, a northern fortress has fallen to a violent Dark Iron assault. In Menethil Harbor, a severely wounded survivor seeks an Alliance adventurer to go north and learn whether commander Longbraid the Grim or any of the garrison survived.",h="At Dun Modr, a northern fortress has fallen to a violent Dark Iron assault.",sec={{t="A Northern Bulwark Broken",b="For generations, Dun Modr has guarded northern Khaz Modan and the vital road and bridge across the Thandol Span, linking the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands. After an ambush at the bridge, the garrison fell back to regroup inside the fortress. Before they could restore their defenses, overwhelming Dark Iron forces struck, slaughtering the defenders and driving them into a desperate flight.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Flight",b="Harlo Barnaby, a young defender, was gravely wounded when a stray axe struck his back during the retreat. Believing him doomed, Longbraid the Grim and the remaining troops strapped Barnaby to their last surviving horse and sent him south to Menethil Harbor. He survived and awoke in the harbor tavern, burdened by survivor's guilt and entirely unaware whether any of his comrades had escaped alive.",sp=0},{t="The Grim Remnant",b="Longbraid the Grim still lives in the northern marshes near the captured fortress, holding a battered handful of survivors together. The veteran commander is relieved to learn that Harlo survived his grievous wound, but Dun Modr remains firmly in Dark Iron hands. Cutthroats and saboteurs occupy its halls and threaten the corridor between Khaz Modan and the human lands to the north.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dark Iron dwarves overran and captured Dun Modr. The garrison had already been ambushed at the nearby Thandol Span, and the attackers struck before its defenders could secure the town, wiping out most of the regiment.",al={"why is dun modr destroyed","who attacked dun modr","dun modr lore"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Harlo Barnaby?",a="Harlo Barnaby is an Ironforge soldier who was stationed at Dun Modr and barely survived its fall. A thrown axe struck his back during the retreat, so his commander strapped him to the garrison's sole surviving horse and sent him south to Menethil Harbor for medical care.",al={"who is harlo","harlo barnaby lore","wounded soldier in menethil"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Longbraid the Grim located?",a="Commander Longbraid the Grim took refuge in the wilderness just outside occupied Dun Modr, near the northern highway toward the Thandol Span.",al={"where is longbraid","longbraid location","find longbraid"},sp=1,it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Dun Modr strategically important?",a="Dun Modr is the Wetlands' northernmost settlement and fortification. It guards the southern approach to the Thandol Span, the only land bridge linking Khaz Modan with the Arathi Highlands and Lordaeron.",al={"why care about dun modr","thandol span connection"},it="history"},{q="Who are the attackers at Dun Modr?",a="The attackers are Dark Iron dwarves, members of the Dark Iron clan from the south who have pushed north into the Wetlands to destroy infrastructure such as the Thandol Span and harass Ironforge's territory.",al={"who took dun modr","dark irons in wetlands"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after finding Longbraid?",a="After you confirm Longbraid is alive and bring him news that Barnaby survived, Longbraid enlists you in a grim mission of vengeance against the Dark Iron forces occupying Dun Modr's ruins.",al={"fall of dun modr follow up","what comes after fall of dun modr"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Harlo Barnaby want you to find Longbraid?",a="Harlo barely escaped the slaughter at Dun Modr with his life, having been struck in the back by a stray axe as the regiment sounded the retreat. Though he woke safely in Menethil Harbor, he is tormented by the fate of his comrades. He refuses to give up hope that his commander, Longbraid, survived the rout, and desperately needs to know if any remnant of his unit still stands against the Dark Iron invaders.",al={"why find longbraid","harlo barnaby motive","why send to dun modr"},it="motive",add="b6379bde",nx={8}},{q="Why can't Harlo Barnaby search for Longbraid himself?",a="Harlo's wounds are far too severe for travel. After taking a Dark Iron axe to the back during the chaotic flight from Dun Modr, his surviving comrades barely managed to bundle him onto their last remaining mount before he lost consciousness. He only recently woke in Menethil Harbor, weak and battered, leaving him entirely reliant on able-bodied adventurers to march north into the hostile marshes on his behalf.",al={"why does harlo need me","why cant harlo go","why not harlo barnaby"},it="why_me",add="67f9d3fa"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, the slaughter of Ironforge mountaineers and the desecration of Dun Modr by clan kin from the south is a bitter personal insult that demands blood in return.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Dun Modr's fall cuts safe overland travel between Ironforge and northern Alliance operations in the Arathi Highlands, leaving the corridor open to sabotage."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","harlo barnaby","longbraid the grim","menethil harbor","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"npc:harlo-barnaby","npc:longbraid-the-grim","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:304","quest:631","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Harlo Barnaby",["end"]="Longbraid the Grim",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=472},src={"Fall of Dun Modr"}}
E["quest:473"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Captain Stoutfist",z="wetlands",s="After the fighting at Dun Algaz, Report to Captain Stoutfist sends proven fighters into Menethil Harbor's keep. The harbor is an Alliance military post, where Valstag Ironjaw directs you to Captain Stoutfist as the Dragonmaw threat spreads across the Wetlands.",h="After the fighting at Dun Algaz, Report to Captain Stoutfist sends proven fighters into Menethil Harbor's...",sec={{t="A Widening Threat",b="Dwarven mountaineers have watched the narrow passes of Dun Algaz for years. The Dragonmaw clan's return reaches beyond Loch Modan, though, as the orcs push outward, raise encampments, and threaten the marshlands. Valstag Ironjaw knows that holding the pass is only the first step in protecting the road to Ironforge.",sp=0},{t="The War Room of Menethil",b="Captain Stoutfist oversees Menethil Harbor's defenses from the war room inside Menethil Keep. Dark Iron saboteurs, local beasts, and marsh murlocs all threaten the port, so the captain depends on capable volunteers to counter dangers beyond the walls. Valstag sends you to carry out direct orders against the Dragonmaw war machine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Captain Stoutfist?",a="Valstag Ironjaw, stationed in Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor, sends you to Captain Stoutfist after you prove yourself in battle against the local Dragonmaw orcs.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","valstag ironjaw"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Captain Stoutfist located?",a="Captain Stoutfist is inside Menethil Keep, in the western Wetlands town of Menethil Harbor. He stands over tactical maps in the keep's war room.",al={"captain stoutfist location","where is stoutfist","menethil war room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw orcs a priority for Menethil Keep?",a="The Dragonmaw hold ancient strongholds throughout the Wetlands and threaten the trade roads between Menethil Harbor and Ironforge. Their forces are pressing beyond Dun Algaz, and the garrison cannot ignore their growing encampments.",al={"why fight dragonmaw","dragonmaw threat","orcs in wetlands"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after reporting to Captain Stoutfist?",a="After you report to Captain Stoutfist, he enlists you in the offensive against the Dragonmaw. He sends you to their encampments to strike down their war banners in the marsh.",al={"what next","followup quest","after report to stoutfist"},it="next_step"},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands?",a="The Dragonmaw are remnants of the old Horde who enslaved red dragons at Grim Batol during the Second War. Grim Batol was broken, but surviving warbands remain entrenched across the marshlands, raiding travelers and defying Alliance authority.",al={"dragonmaw lore","who are dragonmaw","wetlands orcs"},it="people"},{q="Why is Menethil Harbor stretched so thin?",a="Menethil Harbor faces constant threats from marsh wildlife, encroaching murlocs, and hostile Dark Iron dwarves trying to undermine the port. With garrison forces defending the walls and docks, Captain Stoutfist relies on outside champions to strike distant orc outposts.",al={"menethil defense","why are troops busy","harbor problems"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Valstag Ironjaw want me to report to Captain Stoutfist?",a="Valstag recognizes that the threat posed by the Dragonmaw clan is spreading far beyond the pass at Dun Algaz. The orcs are growing bolder across the Wetlands, and Captain Stoutfist is organizing Menethil Harbor's defense. Valstag directs capable fighters straight to the war room so Stoutfist can put proven veterans to work where the garrison needs them most.",al={"why send to stoutfist","valstag motive","why report to captain stoutfist"},it="motive",add="9a52d26e"},{q="Why does Valstag need an adventurer instead of the local guards?",a="The garrison at Menethil Keep is hard-pressed defending the town and key mountain passes from multiple fronts. With the Dragonmaw clan showing aggressive force beyond Dun Algaz, regular troops cannot be spared for every offensive operation. Valstag singles you out because you have already proven yourself in combat against the orcs, making you exactly the seasoned volunteer Captain Stoutfist requires.",al={"why me","why not use guards","why recruit adventurers"},it="why_me",add="8cdd6c80"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know that defending the trade line between Menethil Harbor and Ironforge's gates is vital to Khaz Modan's security.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Menethil Harbor is the primary gateway for goods and reinforcements between the southern kingdoms and Khaz Modan. Orc raids on the road would cripple Alliance trade.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you bring the raw combat prowess Valstag Ironjaw seeks when he sends seasoned front-line fighters to Captain Stoutfist's command."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","dun algaz","menethil harbor","menethil keep","valstag ironjaw","war room","wetlands"},rel={"npc:captain-stoutfist","npc:valstag-ironjaw","quest:464","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-algaz","subzone:war-room"},m={start="Valstag Ironjaw",["end"]="Captain Stoutfist",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=473},src={"Report to Captain Stoutfist"}}
E["quest:474"] = {t="quest",n="Defeat Nek'rosh",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, the Alliance campaign against the Dragonmaw reaches its final strike. With their siege engines sabotaged, the defenders turn on Chieftain Nek'rosh to secure Menethil Harbor. His severed head must be brought to Captain Stoutfist to break the threat to the coastal port.",h="In the Wetlands, the Alliance campaign against the Dragonmaw reaches its final strike.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Dragonmaw",b="The Dragonmaw have long plagued the marshlands of Khaz Modan, entrenched in fortified camps and threatening Menethil Harbor's sea lanes. After discovering and burning the clan's catapults, the marsh's defenders strike at the warband's leader. Chieftain Nek'rosh commands the local orcs and remains the last obstacle to breaking the siege. His death leaves the remaining raiders without their leader's direction.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Harbor",b="Bring Nek'rosh's severed head to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor, and Ironforge's garrison will claim a major victory. Without their heavy siege weapons or their chieftain, the Dragonmaw suffer a blow they are unlikely to recover from quickly. Menethil Harbor is the Alliance's main lifeline between Lordaeron and Khaz Modan. With Nek'rosh fallen, the port's docks and trade vessels are safer from sudden attack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nek'rosh?",a="Nek'rosh leads the remaining Dragonmaw in the Wetlands. From their camps, he organized an assault on Menethil Harbor with siege catapults before the Alliance struck back.",al={"chieftain nek'rosh","who is nekrosh","nekrosh wetlands"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Menethil Harbor want Nek'rosh dead?",a="Nek'rosh threatens Menethil Harbor directly. Under his command, the Dragonmaw built war catapults to bombard the port and cripple the vital shipping lanes linking Khaz Modan to other Alliance lands.",al={"why kill nekrosh","captain stoutfist motives"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders the death of Nek'rosh?",a="The order to strike comes after the Dragonmaw catapults are set on fire. Captain Stoutfist, who commands Menethil Harbor's defense, receives the chieftain's severed head.",al={"who gives defeat nekrosh","where to turn in nekrosh head"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens to the Dragonmaw clan after Nek'rosh is defeated?",a="With their catapults destroyed and their chieftain slain, the Dragonmaw lose leadership and morale. Stragglers still haunt the marshlands, but their immediate campaign against Menethil Harbor is crushed.",al={"dragonmaw after nekrosh","what happens to wetlands orcs"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Dragonmaw clan doing in the Wetlands?",a="The Dragonmaw settled in the Wetlands and the neighboring highlands of Grim Batol during the Second War. After the Horde's defeat, renegade remnants lingered in the swamps, raiding trade routes and harboring deep hatred for the Alliance and the dwarves of Khaz Modan.",al={"why are dragonmaw in wetlands","dragonmaw wetlands lore"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Menethil Harbor so crucial to the Alliance?",a="Menethil Harbor is Ironforge's only major seaport on the western coast. Its ferries carry troops, trade goods, and travelers across the Great Sea to Kalimdor and north toward Lordaeron.",al={"importance of menethil","menethil harbor strategic value"},it="place"},{q="What is Nek'rosh's Head for?",a="Captain Stoutfist needs irrefutable proof that the leader of the Dragonmaw in the Wetlands has fallen. Carrying Nek'rosh's head back to Menethil Harbor confirms that the chieftain can no longer rally his forces or mount another siege against the harbor, assuring the garrison that the threat is genuinely broken.",al={"why take nek'rosh's head","nek'rosh's head purpose","what do you do with nek'rosh's head"},it="item",add="55fbf5d4"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Khaz Modan, you know the Dragonmaw as a lingering scar on your people's ancestral borders. Defeating Nek'rosh protects dwarven roads and Ironforge's western sea trade.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you depend on Menethil Harbor's sea route linking Ironforge and Stormwind with Kalimdor and the northern waters.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Chieftain Nek'rosh in his fortified war camp, testing your martial grit against one of the marsh's fiercest orc commanders."},kw={"captain stoutfist","catapult","chieftain","dragonmaw","ironforge","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","wetlands"},rel={"quest:465","npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Dragonmaw Catapult",["end"]="Captain Stoutfist",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=474,ri={"Nek'rosh's Head"}},src={"Defeat Nek'rosh"}}
E["quest:484"] = {t="quest",n="Young Crocolisk Skins",z="wetlands",s="In Menethil Harbor, prominent tanner James Halloran needs fresh skins from young marsh crocolisks. Their cured hides are in demand across the sea, so steady hunting keeps his trade supplied. Bringing him the softer skins earns his trust and leads to more leatherworking chores.",h="In Menethil Harbor, prominent tanner James Halloran needs fresh skins from young marsh crocolisks.",sec={{t="A Harbor's Export",b="Menethil Harbor links the Eastern Kingdoms to distant continents, and its busy local economy draws on the surrounding marsh. James Halloran tans and cures hides from the region's abundant reptilian predators for trade across the sea. Merchants and ships carry his leather goods to distant ports, keeping pressure on his workshop to maintain a steady supply.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Young Marsh Lurkers",b="Einar brings Halloran regular hauls of mature hides, but those are too firm for some luxury goods. Halloran relies on passing travelers to fill the shortage of softer leather by hunting young crocolisks in the shallow bogs just outside Menethil's palisades. The skins must stay intact for Halloran's careful curing process.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a prominent tanner in Menethil Harbor. His cured crocolisk skins are known across the world and shipped to foreign ports across the Great Sea.",al={"james halloran lore","who is the tanner","halloran menethil"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Halloran need young crocolisk skins specifically?",a="Young crocolisks have softer, more pliable hides than adults. Their skins suit luxury goods and fine leatherwork that the stiffer adult hides cannot provide.",al={"why young crocs","softer skins","crocolisk hides use"},it="item"},{q="Who is Einar?",a="Einar is a local hunter stationed in the Wetlands who works with James Halloran. He regularly treks into the marsh to cull wild crocolisks and bring raw skins to the harbor workshop.",al={"einar wetlands","hunter einar","einar lore"},it="people"},{q="Where are these young crocolisks found?",a="Young crocolisks live in the waterways, reeds, and marshy shallows around Menethil Harbor, just beyond the town gates and docks.",al={"croc locations","where are the young crocs","wetlands young crocs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after bringing the skins to Halloran?",a="Impressed by the hides' quality, Halloran asks for help with other chores around his tanning operation. He gives you the usual work of an apprentice to keep his workshop moving.",al={"quest followup","next quest after young crocolisk skins","halloran next task"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is crocolisk leather valuable in Menethil Harbor?",a="Crocolisk leather is valuable in Menethil Harbor because merchants and sailors prize the exotic, waterproof marsh hides cured by skilled artisans. The harbor connects Ironforge and Stormwind with overseas territories such as Kalimdor.",al={"menethil leather trade","crocolisk skin value"},it="history"},{q="Why does James Halloran want these crocolisk skins?",a="James Halloran runs a thriving tanning business out of Menethil Harbor. His cured crocolisk leathers are renowned across the seas, shipped out aboard vessels bound for distant ports. Because the trade is so lucrative, he relies on a steady flow of materials to fulfill export demands. His regular hunter, Einar, has left him low on the softer hides of younger beasts, so Halloran is willing to pay good coin to any traveler who can quickly restock his workshop.",al={"why does halloran need skins","halloran motive crocolisk","why crocolisk skins halloran"},it="motive",add="178df367"},{q="Why are young crocolisks roaming near Menethil Harbor?",a="The Wetlands are an expansive network of bogs, waterways, and flooded flats, making them an ideal natural breeding ground for crocolisks. The shallow waters and reed beds directly outside Menethil Harbor provide abundant prey and shelter for nesting females and their hatchlings. While the harbor walls keep the town relatively safe, the marshes surrounding it crawl with young crocs eager to ambush small critters or unwary travellers wading past.",al={"why young crocolisks wetlands","menethil crocolisks","wetlands crocs near town"},it="target",add="d20147d6"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter passing through the Wetlands, you can gather clean hides from native predators without spoiling the leather.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help Menethil Harbor's maritime trade and supply lines flow across the Great Sea."},kw={"crocolisk","einar","james halloran","leather","menethil harbor","skins","tanning","wetlands"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","quest:471","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands"},m={start="James Halloran",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=484,ri={"Young Crocolisk Skin"}},src={"Young Crocolisk Skins"}}
E["quest:631"] = {t="quest",n="The Thandol Span",z="wetlands",s="After a blast shatters the northern crossing, Rhag Garmason asks travelers to search for a missing dwarf scout. The Dark Iron clan has attacked Dun Modr, cutting off communication and stranding its defenders without reinforcements. Ol' Rustlocke may hold a clue to the sabotage.",h="After a blast shatters the northern crossing, Rhag Garmason asks travelers to search for a missing dwarf...",sec={{t="Thunder Over the Span",b="A blast has torn through the bridge between Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. Bronzebeard soldiers at the border were caught in the devastation when Dark Iron dwarves attacked Dun Modr. Their ranks are thinned, and their strongholds are under siege. The survivors, led by Longbraid the Grim, hold their ground against the attackers.",sp=0},{t="A Scout Sent East",b="Longbraid sent veteran scout Ebenezer Rustlocke to inspect the eastern span and see whether a crossing or a northern route remained usable. Days have passed without a report. Dun Modr is under siege, and Rhag Garmason and the garrison have too few soldiers to search the enemy-held rubble for him.",sp=0},{t="Grim Discovery",b="Ol' Rustlocke lies dead among the eastern bridge's debris. His body and the parchment in his fist show that he fell into a Dark Iron ambush while scouting. The Dark Irons still threaten the route between Khaz Modan and Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Thandol Span?",a="The Thandol Span crosses the chasm between northern Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. This dwarven bridge is the main land route from Khaz Modan to the northern lands of Lordaeron.",al={"thandol span","what is thandol bridge","wetlands bridge"},it="place"},{q="Who attacked the Thandol Span?",a="The Dark Iron dwarf clan attacked the bridge and nearby Dun Modr. They used explosives to sever the span, crippling Alliance travel and catching the Bronzebeard defenders off guard.",al={"who blew up the bridge","thandol span explosion","who attacked dun modr"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Ol' Rustlocke?",a="Ebenezer Rustlocke was a trusted dwarven scout serving Longbraid the Grim. He was sent to inspect the eastern bridge after the explosion and was killed by Dark Iron forces during his mission.",al={"ebenezer rustlocke","who is rustlocke","missing scout"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Where is Rhag Garmason located?",a="Rhag Garmason is near Dun Modr, just south of the Thandol Span in northern Wetlands. He helps coordinate the defense while the garrison is cut off from Ironforge.",al={"rhag garmason location","where is rhag","quest giver dun modr"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why hasn't Ironforge sent help to Dun Modr?",a="The attack came suddenly, the bridge is destroyed, and Dun Modr is under siege. The isolated defenders are too stretched to send couriers or divert troops, so they rely on passing travelers to carry word.",al={"why no reinforcements","ironforge help wetlands","dun modr reinforcement"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after finding Rustlocke's corpse?",a="Rustlocke's remains hold a parchment showing that Kam Deepfury had explosives stashed just across the span. The parchment begins an effort to destroy the cache before it reaches the remaining bridge, then seek aid from the Alliance camp at Refuge Pointe.",al={"next quest after rustlocke","thandol span continuation","after the thandol span"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Rhag Garmason want Ol' Rustlocke found?",a="A massive explosion tore through the Thandol Span, claiming many dwarven defenders before the Dark Iron assault. In the chaos, Longbraid dispatched Ol' Rustlocke to scout the eastern bridge to see if the position could be held or secured, but days have passed without a single word. Rhag Garmason and the survivors desperately need to know Rustlocke's fate and whether the bridge can still serve their defense.",al={"why find rustlocke","rhag garmason motive","why search for rustlocke"},it="motive",add="60853ee9"},{q="Why does Rhag Garmason need an adventurer's help?",a="Dun Modr is actively under siege by Dark Iron dwarves, and the surviving garrison is stretched beyond its limits. With no reinforcements arriving from Ironforge and casualties mounting by the hour, Rhag Garmason and his fellow soldiers cannot spare a single guard from their defensive lines to mount a search party across the bridge.",al={"why me rhag garmason","why cant the dwarves find rustlocke","why help dun modr"},it="why_me",add="8b9f1c8c"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may see the destruction of the Thandol Span as an insult to dwarven stonework and a blow against Khaz Modan by your hated Dark Iron kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the Thandol Span is the only overland supply route linking Stormwind and Ironforge to Alliance forces in Arathi and Hillsbrad."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","garmason","longbraid","rustlocke","span","thandol","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-modr","quest:634","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Rhag Garmason",["end"]="Ebenezer Rustlocke's Corpse",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=631},src={"The Thandol Span"}}
E["quest:632"] = {t="quest",n="The Thandol Span",z="wetlands",s="At the Thandol Span, Rhag Garmason waits for word from a missing scout. He sent adventurers to check on Ol' Ebenezer Rustlocke after the dwarf stopped reporting from the great stone crossing. The search beneath its arches may reveal a threat to northern supply lines.",h="At the Thandol Span, Rhag Garmason waits for word from a missing scout.",sec={{t="A Scout's Final Stand",b="Longbraid the Grim sent Ebenezer Rustlocke to watch over the Thandol Span's structure and security. When the scout stopped reporting, foul play was feared. Beneath the crossing's arches, you find Rustlocke dead. Dark Iron invaders ambushed him from the shadows.",sp=0},{t="Deepfury's Orders",b="A set of written orders bearing the name Deepfury lies near Rustlocke's clenched fingers. The parchment points to deliberate Dark Iron operations meant to destabilize the crossing, not a random robbery or isolated border skirmish. When you bring the evidence to Garmason, the garrison shifts from a routine search to urgent wartime defense.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ebenezer Rustlocke?",a="Ebenezer 'Ol' Rustlocke was an Alliance dwarf sent to scout the Thandol Span and keep watch there. Dark Iron dwarves caught him off guard and killed him beneath the bridge.",al={"who is rustlocke","ol rustlocke","ebenezer rustlocke"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Who killed Rustlocke?",a="Dark Iron operatives ambushed Rustlocke beneath the Thandol Span under orders from Kam Deepfury.",al={"who killed rustlocke","who ambushed rustlocke","rustlocke corpse"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What is found on Rustlocke's body?",a="A parchment containing Deepfury's Orders lies beside Rustlocke's clenched fist. It records covert Dark Iron plots against the northern bridge.",al={"what was in his hand","deepfury's orders","parchment on rustlocke"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who is Rhag Garmason?",a="Rhag Garmason is an Alliance officer stationed south of the Thandol Span in the Wetlands. He secures traffic between the dwarven territories and the north.",al={"rhag garmason","who is garmason"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Thandol Span so heavily contested?",a="The Thandol Span is the only overland bridge linking Khaz Modan and the Wetlands with the Arathi Highlands and Lordaeron. The Alliance needs it for its supply lines.",al={"why thandol span matters","thandol span importance"},it="place"},{q="What happens after giving the orders to Rhag Garmason?",a="After you give Rhag Garmason the orders, he sends you to destroy a cache of Dark Iron explosives just across the span in the Arathi Highlands, thwarting their sabotage.",al={"what happens next","thandol span follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why must you carry the orders back from Rustlocke's corpse?",a="Ebenezer Rustlocke cannot speak or carry warnings anymore, but the parchment resting beside his clenched fist reveals that the Dark Iron dwarves have launched an active plot against the Thandol Span. If Rhag Garmason does not learn of the ambush and inspect Deepfury's written orders, the Alliance forces guarding the bridge will remain blind to the sabotage unfolding beneath their feet.",al={"why report rustlocke corpse","why take deepfury orders","rustlocke corpse motive"},it="motive",add="d453191c"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you learn that Dark Iron forces have reached far north of the Searing Gorge. Their infiltration threatens your kin in Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the Thandol Span links Ironforge and Stormwind to northern Alliance strongholds. Rustlocke's discovery matters to the security of the continent."},kw={"arathi","dark iron","deepfury","ebenezer rustlocke","rhag garmason","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:631","subzone:thandol-span","zone:wetlands","quest:634","topic:alliance"},m={start="Ebenezer Rustlocke's Corpse",["end"]="Rhag Garmason",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=632},src={"The Thandol Span (2)"}}
E["quest:633"] = {t="quest",n="The Thandol Span",z="wetlands",s="On the Thandol Span, a murder exposes a threat to Ironforge's northern road. Ebenezer Rustlocke has been killed, and Rhag Garmason finds that Kam Deepfury has hidden explosives to cut that route.",h="On the Thandol Span, a murder exposes a threat to Ironforge's northern road.",sec={{t="A Plot Revealed",b="A recovered document reveals what happened beneath the Thandol Span. Ebenezer Rustlocke was murdered in its substructure, and the papers expose a further act of sabotage. Kam Deepfury, the Dark Iron agitator who first destroyed part of the bridge, has not stopped. His network planted a second cache of heavy munitions just across the northern border in the Arathi Highlands, ready to finish the destruction.",sp=0},{t="Saving the Lifeline",b="The Span links the southern kingdoms of Khaz Modan and Stormwind to the north's war-torn lands. Rhag Garmason orders an immediate strike against the sabotage cache in Arathi, before Deepfury's conspirators can use it. Destroying the munitions ends the immediate danger and preserves Ironforge's access to the north. Garmason still has too few troops to defend the gap.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury is the Dark Iron dwarf mastermind behind the sabotage of the Thandol Span. After collapsing the first arch, he cached more explosives across the chasm in the Arathi Highlands to destroy the remaining bridge.",al={"kam deepfury","who bombed thandol span","thandol span mastermind"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Thandol Span so strategically vital?",a="The Span is the only land bridge across the immense chasm between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. If it falls, the Alliance loses its main overland supply route between Ironforge, Stormwind, and its allies holding ground in northern Lordaeron.",al={"why is thandol span important","thandol span lore"},it="place"},{q="What happened to Ebenezer Rustlocke?",a="Ebenezer Rustlocke was an Ironforge defender murdered beneath the bridge. His investigation and recovered papers led Rhag Garmason to uncover Deepfury's hidden explosive cache.",al={"ebon rustlocke death","who was rustlocke"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Where is the cache of explosives hidden?",a="The explosives were hidden in a cache just across the Span, on the Arathi Highlands side. Deepfury's conspirators could quickly carry them to the surviving span structure.",al={"explosives location","where are the explosives","cache location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the order to destroy the explosives?",a="Rhag Garmason, a dwarf officer stationed on the Wetlands side of the Thandol Span, orders the cache found and demolished to honor Rustlocke's sacrifice and protect the remaining bridge.",al={"who starts this quest","rhag garmason"}},{q="What happens after the munitions are destroyed?",a="After the munitions are destroyed, the immediate sabotage threat is over, but Rhag Garmason knows his garrison cannot hold the damaged bridge indefinitely without help. While waiting for Ironforge's reserves, he sends a plea for reinforcements to Captain Nials at the Alliance camp in Refuge Pointe, in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"what next after thandol span","plea to the alliance quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rhag Garmason want the explosives destroyed?",a="Rhag Garmason learned from Rustlocke's recovered parchment that Kam Deepfury planned to detonate another blast using a hidden stockpile across the bridge. One of the Thandol Span's crossings is already shattered; if the Dark Iron conspirators manage to blow up the remaining span, the vital Alliance supply route connecting Khaz Modan to Lordaeron and the Arathi Highlands will be severed entirely.",al={"rhag garmason motive","why destroy explosives","thandol span why destroy explosives"},it="motive",add="a60c1dfd"},{q="Why does Rhag Garmason send an adventurer instead of his own guards?",a="Rhag and the few dwarven defenders at the bridgehead are critically stretched thin, holding the position against hostile incursions while desperately waiting for reinforcements to arrive. With Ebenezer Rustlocke already fallen to the conspirators, Rhag cannot spare anyone from the line to slip across into enemy-held territory in Arathi, leaving you as their only hope to avert catastrophe.",al={"why me","why send me","why doesn't Rhag send guards"},it="why_me",add="b9ac4adc"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the sons of Ironforge, defending the Thandol Span protects King Magni's lifeline to northern allies and strikes a blow against traitorous Dark Iron infiltrators.",["faction:Alliance"]="Holding the Span is essential for the safety of the continent. If the crossing falls, moving Alliance armies and resources into Arathi and Lordaeron becomes exponentially more dangerous.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the destructive power of Deepfury's munitions cache, built to demolish colossal titan-style dwarven stonework."},kw={"arathi highlands","dark iron","ebon rustlocke","explosives","kam deepfury","magni bronzebeard","rhag garmason","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:631","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","npc:kam-deepfury","zone:arathi","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Rhag Garmason",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=633},src={"The Thandol Span (3)"}}
E["quest:634"] = {t="quest",n="Plea To The Alliance",z="wetlands",s="At the shattered Thandol Span, Plea To The Alliance carries a desperate call for aid from Dun Modr's dwarven survivors. Dark Iron infiltrators slaughtered the garrison, and the dwarves appeal to the human forces at Refuge Pointe, though the Alliance is stretched thin.",h="At the shattered Thandol Span, Plea To The Alliance carries a desperate call for aid from Dun Modr's dwarven...",sec={{t="A Cry Across the Chasm",b="Dun Modr lies devastated, and Dark Iron dwarves have sabotaged the Thandol Span. The survivors hold a precarious foothold at the Wetlands' northern rim. Ironforge's main reserves have yet to arrive, so Rhag Garmason and Longbraid the Grim look north to the Arathi Highlands. They learn that Alliance forces have made camp at Refuge Pointe. Garmason sends an emissary across the shattered bridge to ask Captain Nials for urgent military aid.",sp=0},{t="The Plight of Stromgarde",b="At Refuge Pointe, Captain Nials offers sympathy to Longbraid's soldiers, but cannot spare a single fighter. Stromgarde has fallen into ruin, overrun by Syndicate rogues, Boulderfist ogres, and Witherbark trolls. Its surviving defenders are committed to reclaiming their ancestral capital. Bound by honor and pressed by their own desperate struggle, Nials sends word that the dwarves at the Span must stand alone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the plea to Refuge Pointe?",a="Rhag Garmason, near the ruined bridgehead of the Thandol Span on the Wetlands border, sends the plea for Longbraid the Grim and Dun Modr's remaining defenders.",al={"who gives plea to the alliance","rhag garmason quest","who asks for help"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the dwarves need help from Refuge Pointe?",a="Dark Iron clan infiltrators attacked Dun Modr and sabotaged the Thandol Span. While the survivors await Ironforge's heavy reserves, they lack the numbers to retake their settlement and secure the crossing alone.",al={"why need alliance help","why ask refuge pointe","dun modr reinforcements"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Captain Nials refuse to send soldiers?",a="Captain Nials cannot spare troops because Stromgarde has collapsed into ruins. The human forces at Refuge Pointe are committed to reclaiming Stromgarde from the Syndicate, ogres, and forest trolls.",al={"why no help from nials","why refuge pointe refuses","captain nials answer"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Refuge Pointe located?",a="Refuge Pointe lies just off the main road in the central Arathi Highlands, north of the Thandol Span crossing between the Wetlands and Arathi.",al={"refuge pointe location","where is captain nials","how to find refuge pointe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="The Dark Iron clan overwhelmed and sacked Dun Modr after infiltrating through the mountains to sever the land route between the southern dwarven lands and the northern Alliance territories.",al={"dun modr lore","what happened dun modr","who attacked dun modr"},it="history"},{q="What happens after Captain Nials turns down the request?",a="Captain Nials sends his regrets to Longbraid the Grim and confirms that no human reinforcements are coming. The dwarven survivors at the bridge must rely on their own wits, wandering adventurers, and distant Ironforge reinforcements.",al={"what next plea to the alliance","next quest after plea","chain continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rhag Garmason ask you to deliver the plea instead of going himself?",a="Rhag Garmason and the surviving Mountaineers are pinned down holding their precarious foothold at the Thandol Span. With Dun Modr overrun and Ironforge reserves still far away, they cannot spare a single dwarf from guard duty to run north through dangerous lands.",al={"why me plea alliance","why Rhag sends you","why cant Rhag go to refuge pointe"},it="why_me",add="0e006c4d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Dun Modr's isolation is painful: even longtime human allies are too besieged to lend a hand.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you witness Captain Nials' sorrow as he weighs Alliance brotherhood against Stromgarde's survival.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this exchange shows how fractured its northern Eastern Kingdoms remain, with local garrisons fighting separate, desperate battles without shared reserves."},kw={"arathi highlands","captain nials","dark iron","dun modr","longbraid","refuge pointe","rhag garmason","stromgarde","thandol span"},rel={"subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","quest:472","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Rhag Garmason",["end"]="Captain Nials",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=634},src={"Plea To The Alliance"}}
E["quest:647"] = {t="quest",n="MacKreel's Moonshine",z="wetlands",s="Foggy MacKreel sleeps through his watch on the broken Thandol Span after drinking too much of his own moonshine. Now he needs an Alliance traveler to hurry a fresh batch to Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore and settle his debt.",h="Foggy MacKreel sleeps through his watch on the broken Thandol Span after drinking too much of his own...",sec={{t="A Guard's Hangover",b="Foggy MacKreel keeps watch on the shattered Thandol Span, where the hours are wet, cold, and dull. To bear the damp chill, he drinks his homemade moonshine, a brew so fierce he likens its aftereffects to siege engines pounding across his skull. One drink too many leaves him passed out through his shift. Longbraid the Grim commands the dwarves defending the Span, and Foggy cannot afford another lapse in discipline.",sp=0},{t="A Race Against the Clock",b="Foggy also owes Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore a longstanding debt. He promised a batch of his personal brew to settle the account, but his hangover and watch duties leave him minutes from missing the deadline. With gryphons and swift feet, you race across the Arathi Highlands to Southshore with the jug, before Bilger decides Foggy has skipped out on his tab again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foggy MacKreel?",a="Foggy MacKreel is a dwarf on the broken part of the Thandol Span, reached from the Arathi Highlands side. He brews extremely stout moonshine and often drinks too freely while on duty.",al={"foggy mackreel","who is foggy","quest giver mackreel"},it="identity"},{q="Why is this delivery so urgent?",a="Foggy passed out drunk during his watch and fell badly behind schedule. He has barely a quarter of an hour to get the moonshine from the Thandol Span to Southshore and settle his overdue tab with Brewmeister Bilger.",al={"why is there a timer","why 15 minutes","mackreel moonshine timer"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Brewmeister Bilger is a master dwarven brewer in the coastal settlement of Southshore, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He appreciates stout alcohol and has an outstanding business agreement with Foggy MacKreel.",al={"brewmeister bilger","who is bilger","bilger southshore"},it="target"},{q="How does one get the moonshine to Southshore in time?",a="There is no boat from the Span to Southshore. If you know the Refuge Pointe flight path, take a gryphon from Refuge Pointe to Southshore, then find Brewmeister Bilger in town before the time runs out.",al={"how to deliver moonshine","fastest way southshore mackreel","moonshine delivery route"},gp=true},{q="Who is Longbraid?",a="Longbraid the Grim is the dwarf commander outside Dun Modr in the Wetlands, leading the defenders of the Thandol Span. Foggy dreads Longbraid discovering that he drank himself unconscious while on watch.",al={"captain longbraid","longbraid menethil"},it="people"},{q="Why can't Foggy MacKreel deliver the moonshine himself?",a="Foggy MacKreel indulged far too heavily in his own moonshine the night before and ended up passing out cold during his watch. With a throbbing headache, his official guard post to answer for under Longbraid the Grim, and a rapidly expiring deadline to clear his debts with Brewmeister Bilger, he is in no shape or position to run off to Southshore on his own.",al={"why me mackreel","why deliver moonshine","foggy moonshine why me"},it="why_me",add="d39890fd"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the misery of a terrible hangover made worse by an unpaid brewing debt to a fellow kinsman.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you cross the overland route linking the Thandol Span with Alliance-held Southshore in Hillsbrad."},kw={"bilger","foggy","longbraid","mackreel","menethil","moonshine","southshore"},rel={"npc:foggy-mackreel","npc:brewmeister-bilger","zone:wetlands","subzone:southshore"},m={start="Foggy MacKreel",["end"]="Brewmeister Bilger",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=647},src={"MacKreel's Moonshine (quest)"}}
E["quest:98190"] = {t="quest",n="A Friend of the Family",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Harbor fears its relics will fall to local enemies. The harbor authorities send the Menethil Statuette to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep for safekeeping.",h="Menethil Harbor fears its relics will fall to local enemies.",sec={{t="A Precarious Harbor",b="Menethil Harbor links the northern Eastern Kingdoms to the south. The port honors the late King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron, but treacherous marshes and enemies surround it. With threats mounting, harbor leaders fear the exposed outpost cannot protect relics from the fallen northern kingdom.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Threat",b="Dragonmaw orcs still infest the Wetlands. The clan has a dark past and a taste for ruthless advantage. Harbor defenders fear the orcs would pillage the Menethil Statuette for conquest, then defile it or turn it to their own ends.",sp=0},{t="Straight to the Highlord",b="The courier carries the relic straight to Stormwind Keep, bypassing the usual military and bureaucratic channels. There it goes to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon, regent to the young King Anduin Wrynn. The capital's leaders are trusted to safeguard a piece of Lordaeron's heritage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Menethil Statuette?",a="The Menethil Statuette is a valuable heirloom tied to Lordaeron's royal line and King Terenas Menethil II. Its history links the northern kingdom with the Alliance, making it a target for scavengers and enemies.",al={"menethil relic","what is the statuette","statuette lore"},it="item"},{q="Why can't the statuette stay in Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor is isolated among hostile swamps, dark iron dwarves, murlocs, and orcs. Its garrison fears the settlement cannot protect such a meaningful relic.",al={"why move the statuette","is menethil harbor unsafe"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw and why do they want it?",a="The Dragonmaw are orcs entrenched in the Wetlands. Harbor officials fear they would plunder prestigious Alliance relics, even at the cost of their warriors, and desecrate or misuse them.",al={"dragonmaw threat","why do orcs want statuette"},it="threat"},{q="Why deliver the relic directly to Bolvar Fordragon?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is Stormwind's regent and protector of young King Anduin. Giving him the relic directly bypasses administrative delays and places it in the capital's strongest hands.",al={"why bolvar","why bypass chain of command"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Highlord Bolvar Fordragon located?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is in the throne room of Stormwind Keep, beside the boy-king Anduin Wrynn.",al={"bolvar location","where is bolvar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does Menethil Harbor connect to King Terenas?",a="Menethil Harbor honors King Terenas Menethil II, who led Lordaeron and supported the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War. He died during the Third War.",al={"why is it called menethil harbor","terenas menethil connection"},it="history"},{q="Why are you chosen to carry the Menethil Statuette to Stormwind?",a="Menethil Harbor is isolated and perpetually threatened by hostile forces across the Wetlands, leaving its garrison stretched thin defending the port. You have already proven your capability and trustworthiness by recovering the heirloom. Entrusting an capable, independent traveler avoids depleting the town's local defense and keeps the mission discrete while moving through dangerous territory.",al={"why send me","why not send guards","why deliver statuette"},it="why_me",add="ece51c60"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, protecting an heirloom of the Menethil dynasty preserves Lordaeron's proud, tragic memory and affirms Stormwind's duty as the last great human kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, delivering the relic honors the historic northern Alliance and keeps its symbol from the Dragonmaw.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may see the Menethil name as a reminder of the founding patron of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Protecting the relic is a solemn duty for a holy warrior."},kw={"bolvar","dragonmaw","fordragon","harbor","menethil","statuette","stormwind","terenas","wetlands"},rel={"item:menethil-statuette","npc:bolvar-fordragon","subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:wetlands","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Automatic",["end"]="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=98190},src={"A Friend of the Family"},fv=true}
E["quest:98197"] = {t="quest",n="Spoils of War",z="wetlands",s="As the Dragonmaw move, Valstag Ironjaw seeks timber and iron from Menethil Harbor. He needs them to strengthen the town’s defenses.",h="As the Dragonmaw move, Valstag Ironjaw seeks timber and iron from Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="Harbor Stores",b="Menethil Harbor once served the Old Horde as a staging ground for an invasion of Hillsbrad. The fleet built there drew on resources stolen from Khaz Modan. Some supplies remain in the harbor, and Valstag asks you to bring him the timber and iron for the town’s defenses.",sp=0},{t="A New Supply",b="Valstag thanks you for bringing the materials. With them, the town need not depend only on shipments from Theramore or Auberdine.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Valstag need from Menethil Harbor?",a="Valstag asks you to recover Khaz Modan timber and iron from Menethil Harbor.",al={"what does he need","timber and iron","harbor supplies"}},{q="Why are Khaz Modan supplies in the harbor?",a="The Old Horde built a fleet at Menethil Harbor using resources stolen from Khaz Modan.",al={"why is timber there","khaz modan iron","old horde supplies"}},{q="What will the materials be used for?",a="Valstag says the materials will help strengthen the town’s defenses as the Dragonmaw move.",al={"why gather supplies","defenses","what are they for"}},{q="Who is Valstag Ironjaw?",a="Valstag Ironjaw asks you to recover timber and iron from Menethil Harbor.",al={"who's valstag","valstag","ironjaw"}},{q="Where did the Old Horde use Menethil Harbor?",a="The Old Horde used Menethil Harbor as a staging ground for its naval invasion of Hillsbrad.",al={"old horde harbor","menethil history","hillsbrad invasion"}},{q="Why does Valstag welcome these supplies?",a="The materials mean the town need not depend only on shipments from Theramore or Auberdine.",al={"why thank you","theramore shipments","auberdine supplies"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help strengthen the town’s defenses against the Dragonmaw.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may know the Old Horde built its fleet here with resources stolen from Khaz Modan."},kw={"dragonmaw","khaz modan iron","khaz modan timber","menethil harbor","old horde","spoils of war","town defenses","valstag ironjaw"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","npc:valstag-ironjaw","subzone:auberdine","topic:old-horde","topic:alliance","zone:wetlands"},m={id=98197},src={"In-game quest text: Spoils of War"},fv=true}
E["quest:98208"] = {t="quest",n="Bloom of the Heavens",z="wetlands",s="Sylessa Duskwhisper searches the waters south of Menethil Harbor for Bloom of the Heavens. The sacred flower Nord'el was lost when the night elf vessel Flying Osprey wrecked alongside ships of the Kul Tiran Third Fleet. Murlocs now occupy the wreck, where Nord'el lies among the ruins.",h="Sylessa Duskwhisper searches the waters south of Menethil Harbor for Bloom of the Heavens.",sec={{t="A Relic of Mount Hyjal",b="Sylessa Duskwhisper has come from Auberdine to Menethil Harbor to recover Nord'el. The flower was gathered beneath a full moon atop Mount Hyjal, and holds deep meaning for the night elves. Those who now live in Teldrassil treasure relics from their ancestral mountain as reminders of their heritage.",sp=0},{t="The Fate of the Flying Osprey",b="Many moons ago, the night elf vessel Flying Osprey wrecked on the rocky coast south of Menethil Harbor while sailing with the Kul Tiran Third Fleet. Its ruined hull rests in the shallows. Fierce murloc raiders have made the wreck their home and defend it from anyone seeking the night elf cargo.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Nord'el?",a="In Darnassian, Nord'el means Bloom of the Heavens. Night elves gather this sacred flower after it blossoms beneath a full moon atop Mount Hyjal, their ancestral mountain home.",al={"what is nordel","nordel flower","what is bloom of the heavens"}},{q="What was the Flying Osprey?",a="The Flying Osprey was a night elf vessel sailing with the Kul Tiran Third Fleet. Many moons ago, it wrecked on the Wetlands coast just south of Menethil Harbor, scattering its cargo.",al={"flying osprey ship","what ship wrecked","kul tiran third fleet wetlands"}},{q="Who is Sylessa Duskwhisper?",a="Sylessa Duskwhisper is a night elf emissary who sailed from Auberdine and Teldrassil to Menethil Harbor to recover the lost bloom for her people.",al={"who is sylessa duskwhisper","quest giver menethil","night elf in menethil"}},{q="Why is the shipwreck dangerous?",a="Fierce murloc raiders occupy the coastal wreck south of Menethil Harbor. They claim the remains of the Flying Osprey, making salvage dangerous for Sylessa.",al={"why are murlocs at the wreck","who guards the wreck","wreckage south of menethil"}},{q="Why is Nord'el so important to the night elves?",a="Night elves gathered Nord'el atop Mount Hyjal, their former home, before they founded Teldrassil. Its sacred harvest beneath the full moon gives the flower deep cultural and emotional value.",al={"why is the flower important","why does sylessa want nordel"}},{q="Where can the wreckage be found?",a="The Flying Osprey lies on the rocky coast just south of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Hostile murlocs occupy the wreck.",al={"where is the wreckage","where is the flower","shipwreck location wetlands"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can treasure Nord'el as a botanical relic of Mount Hyjal, gathered before your people moved their home to Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Flying Osprey sailed alongside the Kul Tiran Third Fleet before both met disaster off Menethil Harbor.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know Nord'el as a rare night elf flower gathered beneath the full moon atop Mount Hyjal, a remarkable botanical specimen."},kw={"auberdine","bloom of the heavens","flying osprey","menethil harbor","mount hyjal","murlocs","nord'el","sylessa duskwhisper","teldrassil","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:hyjal","subzone:auberdine","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc"},m={id=98208},src={"In-game quest text: Bloom of the Heavens"},fv=true}
E["quest:98209"] = {t="quest",n="Bloom of the Heavens",z="wetlands",s="Across the Great Sea, Nord'el is bound for Auberdine after its recovery in the Wetlands. For night elves still grieving the loss of their immortality, the flower carries the grace of Elune.",h="Across the Great Sea, Nord'el is bound for Auberdine after its recovery in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Perilous Retrieval",b="In the Wetlands, Sylessa recovers Nord'el, the legendary flower, despite an attack by local murlocs. Worn out by her escape, she entrusts the plant to you for its voyage across the Great Sea to Auberdine. From Menethil Harbor, a boat sails directly to Darkshore, linking the Eastern Kingdoms with northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Sign of Elune's Grace",b="When Nord'el reaches Auberdine, Elder Thundris Windweaver is astonished. He believed the sacred bloom had vanished forever. Night elves still bear the cost of surrendering their immortality after the Battle of Mount Hyjal, and Nord'el's survival feels like a blessing from Elune. Thundris prepares to send the delicate plant to Darnassus, where it can be cultivated and preserved for future generations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Nord'el?",a="Nord'el is a sacred flower the night elves long thought lost. Its survival after many years is a treasured sign of Elune's favor and nature's resilience.",al={"what is nord'el","nordel flower","sacred bloom"}},{q="Who gives the quest Bloom of the Heavens?",a="Sylessa in the Wetlands gives you Nord'el to carry. She recovered the sacred bloom despite an ambush and pursuit by hostile murlocs, but the ordeal left her too exhausted to make the journey herself.",al={"who gives bloom of the heavens","wetlands quest giver nordel","sylessa wetlands"}},{q="Where does Nord'el need to be delivered?",a="Carry Nord'el across the sea to Elder Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, on the coast of Darkshore. A boat sails directly from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine.",al={"where do i bring nord'el","thundris windweaver location","auberdine delivery"}},{q="Why is Nord'el so significant to the night elves?",a="Elder Thundris Windweaver sees Nord'el's survival as a beacon of hope. The sacred flower recalls Elune's grace and the kaldorei's endurance after they sacrificed their immortality during the Third War.",al={"why is nord'el important to night elves","nordel lore","immortality night elves nordel"}},{q="What will happen to the flower after reaching Auberdine?",a="After Nord'el reaches Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver arranges to have it carried inland to Darnassus. There, night elf botanists and priests can nurture and cultivate it.",al={"what happens to nord'el next","nord'el darnassus","where does thundris send nord'el"}},{q="How do you travel from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine?",a="Take the boat from Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands across the Great Sea to Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"how to get to auberdine from wetlands","menethil boat to auberdine","boat to darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Nord'el as a precious remnant of Kalimdor's sacred heritage. It is also a sign of Elune's care as the kaldorei adapt to the loss of their immortality.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can cross from Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms to Auberdine and Darnassus in northern Kalimdor.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can appreciate Nord'el's recovery. This sacred flower was thought lost for ages and needs cultivation in Darnassus."},kw={"auberdine","bloom of the heavens","darkshore","darnassus","elune","menethil harbor","nord'el","sylessa","thundris windweaver","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","quest:4761","topic:murloc"},m={id=98209},src={"In-game quest text: Bloom of the Heavens"},fv=true}
E["quest:98245"] = {t="quest",n="Razormaw Needling",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Howin Kindfeather seeks Razormaw teeth for dragon whelp armor. He plans to make awls that can stitch the scales together against dragonfire.",h="In the Wetlands, Howin Kindfeather seeks Razormaw teeth for dragon whelp armor.",sec={{t="Tools of Retribution",b="Howin Kindfeather means to strike back at the foes who have plagued the Wetlands: the Dark Iron dwarves, the Dragonmaw orcs, and the drakes they brought into battle. He is making armor from dragon whelp scales to guard against dragonfire. Their hides are too tough for ordinary tools to sew.",sp=0},{t="Fangs as Needles",b="Howin needs sharp, sturdy tools to pierce the whelp hide. He looks to the Razormaw raptors that stalk Raptor Ridge in the northeast and Saltspray Glen in the northwest. Their needle-sharp incisors make strong awls. These can pierce dragon scales without shattering under pressure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Razormaw Needling?",a="Howin Kindfeather gives the work in the Wetlands. He bears a deep grudge against the Dark Iron dwarves, the Dragonmaw clan, and the drakes they rode. He seeks to make whelp scale armor that can resist dragonfire.",al={"who gives razormaw needling","who is howin kindfeather","quest giver razormaw needling"}},{q="Why does Howin Kindfeather need Razormaw incisors?",a="Howin is making protective armor from tough dragon whelp scales, but their hide is hard to stitch. Razormaw incisors are sharp and sturdy enough to make awls that pierce the scales without breaking.",al={"why does howin want raptor teeth","purpose of razormaw incisors","what are the teeth for"}},{q="Where are the Razormaw raptors located?",a="Razormaw raptors prowl Raptor Ridge in the northeast Wetlands and Saltspray Glen in the northwest, toward the coast.",al={"where to find razormaw raptors","razormaw raptor location wetlands","where are the raptors"}},{q="What is Howin Kindfeather making with the whelp scales?",a="Howin is stitching dragon whelp scales into protective gear. The scales guard against fiery breath and offer protection from dragons and the Dragonmaw clan's drakes.",al={"what armor is howin making","whelp scale armor wetlands","why whelp scales"}},{q="Why does Howin hate the Dark Irons and Dragonmaw?",a="Howin despises the Dark Iron clan and the Dragonmaw orcs, who enslaved red dragons during the Second War. Both factions left scars on the Wetlands and surrounding mountains. Howin wants to redress the balance.",al={"why hate dark irons and dragonmaw","howin enemies","why does howin hate dragonmaw"}},{q="What does Howin turn the raptor incisors into?",a="Howin turns the raptor incisors into durable awls. Their natural taper lets them punch through tough hides and leather for sewing, and pierce dragon scales without snapping.",al={"what is an awl","razormaw awls","how are raptor teeth used as tools"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share the bitter hatred Wildhammer and Ironforge dwarves hold for the Dark Iron clan and the Dragonmaw orcs. Both ravaged the Wetlands and Grim Batol.",["faction:Alliance"]="Protective gear against dragonfire aids the Alliance's ongoing struggle against dragonkin and Dragonmaw forces holding the eastern marshes."},kw={"dark iron","dragonmaw","howin kindfeather","raptor ridge","raptors","razormaw incisors","razormaw needling","saltspray glen","wetlands","whelp scales"},rel={"subzone:raptor-ridge","subzone:saltspray-glen","zone:wetlands"},m={id=98245},src={"In-game quest text: Razormaw Needling"},fv=true}
E["quest:98246"] = {t="quest",n="Trying Times",z="wetlands",s="Before Howin Kindfeather can fly through the Wetlands, Bassbeak needs a meal. He seeks a dozen intact eggs from the fierce Razormaw raptors.",h="Before Howin Kindfeather can fly through the Wetlands, Bassbeak needs a meal.",sec={{t="Appeasing a Hungry Gryphon",b="Howin Kindfeather tends Bassbeak in the Wetlands. The dwarf will not fly with his gryphon until her hunger is eased. A hungry gryphon can be stubborn and unpredictable. She may lash out, so a proper meal must come before any flight through the marshes.",sp=0},{t="The Razormaw Bounty",b="Howin seeks food for Bassbeak among the Razormaw raptors. Their nests lie at Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest. Razormaw eggs have yolks as large as a gnome's head. Howin wants those substantial meals to satisfy Bassbeak before she faces the dangers of the Wetlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Howin Kindfeather?",a="Howin Kindfeather is a dwarf who tends Bassbeak, his gryphon in the Wetlands. He asks for fresh raptor eggs to feed her before carrying out his plans.",al={"who is howin kindfeather","howin kindfeather wetlands","quest giver trying times"}},{q="Who is Bassbeak?",a="Bassbeak is Howin Kindfeather's gryphon. When hungry, she grows irritable and dangerous, making it unsafe to ride her before she has eaten.",al={"who is bassbeak","bassbeak the gryphon","howins gryphon"}},{q="Why does Howin need raptor eggs?",a="Howin seeks Razormaw raptor eggs because he says untainted food is scarce in the Wetlands. Their large, nourishing yolks can satisfy Bassbeak's appetite.",al={"why raptor eggs","why feed eggs to gryphon","what are the eggs for"}},{q="Where can Razormaw raptors be found?",a="Razormaw raptors live at Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest in the Wetlands. Their nests hold the eggs Howin seeks.",al={"where are razormaw raptors","where to find razormaw eggs","wetlands raptor locations"}},{q="Why do the eggs need to be perfect?",a="Howin asks for eggs without cracks or flaws so Bassbeak gets fresh, untainted food instead of spoiled scraps.",al={"why must eggs be perfect","cracked eggs trying times"}},{q="What is Howin planning to do with Bassbeak?",a="Howin has a broader plan for Bassbeak, but its details wait until she is fed and calm enough to fly safely amid the region's dangers.",al={"what is howins plan","what are howin and bassbeak planning"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Healthy gryphons matter to Alliance travel and communication across Khaz Modan, especially when local dangers threaten regional security.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know an ill-tempered gryphon can be as dangerous as an enemy. Feed and care for her before flight.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may hear Howin compare Razormaw egg yolks to a gnome's noggin, a vivid dwarven measure."},kw={"bassbeak","gryphon","howin kindfeather","raptor ridge","razormaw eggs","saltspray glen","trying times","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:raptor-ridge","subzone:saltspray-glen","zone:wetlands"},m={id=98246},src={"In-game quest text: Trying Times"},fv=true}
E["quest:98283"] = {t="quest",n="Carnage",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Rethiel the Greenwarden asks you to draw Carnage from its lair. The Razormaw alpha's plague-driven frenzy has thrown the marshes out of balance.",h="In the Wetlands, Rethiel the Greenwarden asks you to draw Carnage from its lair.",sec={{t="A Broken Balance",b="The Razormaw raptors once kept wild growth in check across the Wetlands. Now a bloodthirsty alpha named Carnage rules the pack. It slaughters without restraint and terrorizes its own kind. The marshes are in turmoil.",sp=0},{t="Luring the Alpha",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden watches over the Green Belt and believes corruption has taken hold of Carnage. Diseased Rotclaw bears came down from Loch Modan. You gather their malignant entrails and place the foul meat in Carnage's cave below Raptor Ridge. The frenzied alpha attacks, and its suffering can end.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Carnage?",a="Carnage is the monstrous alpha of the Razormaw raptors in the Wetlands. Disease has driven the beast mad, leaving slaughter behind and terrifying its own pack.",al={"who is carnage","carnage raptor","what is carnage"}},{q="Who gives the quest Carnage?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden gives the work. He watches over the Green Belt in the Wetlands and seeks to restore the region's corrupted natural balance.",al={"who gives carnage quest","where to turn in carnage","rethiel wetlands"}},{q="Why must Carnage be destroyed?",a="Rethiel seeks Carnage's death because unnatural sickness has driven the beast mad. Its madness shattered the Razormaw hierarchy and devastated the local ecology.",al={"why kill carnage","why does rethiel want carnage dead"}},{q="How is Carnage lured out?",a="You lure Carnage by placing the malignant flesh and entrails of diseased bears in its cave below Raptor Ridge, to the northeast.",al={"how to summon carnage","how to lure carnage","where is carnage cave"}},{q="What are the diseased bears mentioned by Rethiel?",a="The diseased bears are Rotclaws that came down from Loch Modan. Lingering corruption has maddened them, and their tainted flesh draws out the crazed raptor alpha.",al={"what are rotclaw bears","where do diseased bears come from"}},{q="What role did the Razormaw raptors originally serve in the Wetlands?",a="The Razormaw raptors normally keep the Wetlands' natural plant and animal life from overgrowing. In doing so, they help maintain ecological balance. Carnage's madness disrupted that role.",al={"what role do razormaw play","why raptors matter in wetlands"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share Rethiel's grief over the Wetlands' broken balance. Sickness has warped predators like Carnage into mindless terrors.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the danger when plague-driven fury strips an alpha predator of its instincts. Then it turns against its own kind."},kw={"carnage","loch modan","raptor ridge","razormaw","rethiel the greenwarden","rotclaw","the green belt","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","subzone:green-belt","subzone:raptor-ridge","zone:wetlands","quest:463","zone:lochmodan"},m={id=98283},src={"In-game quest text: Carnage"},fv=true}
E["quest:98291"] = {t="quest",n="Death to the Dragonmaw",z="wetlands",s="At Dragonmaw Retreat, Howin Kindfeather asks you to thin the Dragonmaw ranks. He hopes to reach Grim Batol and reclaim it for the Wildhammers, or learn more about it.",h="At Dragonmaw Retreat, Howin Kindfeather asks you to thin the Dragonmaw ranks.",sec={{t="Dragonmaw Retreat",b="Dragonmaw orcs have gathered along the retreat, where red dragons routed them before. Howin needs their numbers reduced before he can approach Grim Batol. He points you east along the road to find them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Howin Kindfeather?",a="Howin Kindfeather hopes to get back into Grim Batol and reclaim it for the Wildhammers, or at least learn more about it.",al={"who's Howin","Howin guy"}},{q="Why does Howin want help?",a="Howin says Dragonmaw orcs are marching through Dragonmaw Retreat. He needs their numbers thinned before he can approach Grim Batol.",al={"why help Howin","what does Howin need"}},{q="Where are the Dragonmaw orcs?",a="The Dragonmaw orcs are along Dragonmaw Retreat. Howin points you east along the road to find them.",al={"where dragonmaw","Dragonmaw location"}},{q="Who should I look for?",a="Howin names Dragonmaw Reclaimers, Dragonmaw Soulbinders, and Dragonmaw Infiltrators.",al={"which orcs","Dragonmaw types"}},{q="What happened at Dragonmaw Retreat?",a="Red dragons routed the Dragonmaw orcs at Dragonmaw Retreat before.",al={"Dragonmaw history","why retreat"}}},kw={"dragonmaw infiltrators","dragonmaw orcs","dragonmaw reclaimers","dragonmaw retreat","dragonmaw soulbinders","grim batol","howin kindfeather","wildhammers"},rel={"subzone:grim-batol","zone:wetlands"},m={id=98291},src={"In-game quest text: Death to the Dragonmaw"},fv=true}
E["quest:98310"] = {t="quest",n="Gleaning Our Future",z="wetlands",s="Prospector Whelgar sees a way to learn more from the Goaz Stone. Four larger golems bear names that match its missing pieces.",h="Prospector Whelgar sees a way to learn more from the Goaz Stone.",sec={{t="Four Inscriptions",b="You've found missing pieces of the Goaz Stone. Prospector Whelgar points to four larger golems named Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru. He asks you to use the stone near each one, then bring their hearts back. He hopes they will reveal more of its markings.",sp=0},{t="Faint Words",b="When Prospector Whelgar brings the hearts close to the Goaz Stone, new writing shimmers into view: “Curse of Flesh... they will fail.” He cannot make out what the words mean. He wants to take the stone somewhere safe for further study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Whelgar want me to bring back?",a="Prospector Whelgar asks you to use the Goaz Stone near Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru, then bring back their hearts.",al={"whelgar wants what","golem hearts","bring back hearts"}},{q="Where are the four golems?",a="Ados is at the Dragonmaw Gates near Grim Batol. Modr is just outside Dun Modr to the north. Golm lies beneath Grim Batol, east of Dun Algaz. Neru is behind Direforge Hill to the northeast.",al={"where are ados modr golm neru","golem locations","where find the golems"}},{q="Why does Whelgar want the golem hearts?",a="The golems bear inscriptions that match missing pieces of the Goaz Stone. Whelgar hopes their hearts will reveal more of its markings.",al={"why hearts","what are hearts for","goaz stone pieces"}},{q="What does Whelgar think of the golems?",a="Whelgar suspects the constructs will be tougher than the warder.",al={"are golems tough","whelgar warning","golem strength"}}},kw={"ados","gleaning our future","goaz stone","golem hearts","golm","inscriptions","modr","neru","prospector whelgar","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","npc:prospector-whelgar","subzone:dragonmaw-gates","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:dun-algaz","subzone:direforge-hill"},m={id=98310},src={"In-game quest text: Gleaning Our Future"},fv=true}
E["quest:98824"] = {t="quest",n="Prehistoric Prism",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands, Prospector Whelgar finds a relic marked by the keepers. He sends you with it to Ironforge, where the Explorers' League can study the titans' legacy.",h="In the Wetlands, Prospector Whelgar finds a relic marked by the keepers.",sec={{t="An Ancient Discovery",b="Prospector Whelgar finds a remarkable artifact while surveying the Wetlands. Intricate keeper inscriptions cover its many facets, and Whelgar authenticates the titan-like markings. He urges you to carry the relic to Ironforge, where scholars can study it. Whelgar hopes the discovery will enter the official catalogue, with both your recovery and his authentication properly credited.",sp=0},{t="A Gift to the Museum",b="High Explorer Magellas receives the relic for the Explorers' League in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. Its maker marks confirm its authenticity. Magellas says the light passing through its polished facets recalls wonders he saw on his first excavation in Uldaman. Your donation preserves the artifact for study and adds to the League's records of the titans' legacy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Prehistoric Prism?",a="Prospector Whelgar asks you to carry the relic to Ironforge after authenticating the titan-like inscriptions on its facets in the Wetlands.",al={"who gives prehistoric prism","where does prehistoric prism start","quest giver prehistoric prism"}},{q="Where do you deliver the Prehistoric Prism?",a="You deliver the relic to High Explorer Magellas in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge, and he accepts it for the museum's collection.",al={"who to turn in prehistoric prism","where to turn in prehistoric prism","prehistoric prism completion"}},{q="What kind of artifact is the Prehistoric Prism?",a="The relic is an ancient, multifaceted artifact bearing the unmistakable marks of the keepers. Light passing through its crystalline form recalls relics found in Uldaman.",al={"what is prehistoric prism","is prehistoric prism titan","what is the relic"}},{q="Why is the Hall of Explorers interested in the prism?",a="The Explorers' League collects and catalogs authentic relics of titan origin. High Explorer Magellas studies artifacts like this to deepen understanding of ancient history.",al={"why does magellas want it","why donate prism","hall of explorers prism"}},{q="How does the prism relate to Uldaman?",a="High Explorer Magellas compares the light refracted through the artifact to relics he examined on his first archaeological dig in Uldaman, noting its keeper markings.",al={"does uldaman relate to the prism","uldaman connection","prism uldaman"}},{q="Does your name get recorded in the museum's catalogue?",a="Prospector Whelgar's authentication and your recovery of the relic are to be recorded in the Explorers' League's historical archives.",al={"prehistoric prism catalog","do you get credited","history credit prism"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, recovering genuine titan relics speaks to your people's search for their makers' origins and the Explorers' League's purpose.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, your discovery enriches the scholarly collections in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers."},kw={"hall of explorers","high explorer magellas","ironforge","prehistoric prism","prospector whelgar","titan relic","uldaman","wetlands"},rel={"npc:prospector-whelgar","subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","topic:titan","subzone:uldaman","zone:wetlands"},m={id=98824},src={"In-game quest text: Prehistoric Prism"},fv=true}
E["subzone:angerfang-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Angerfang Encampment",z="wetlands",s="Dragonmaw orcs gather at Angerfang Encampment in the central Wetlands, threatening nearby dwarven settlements. Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher leads the renegades as they prepare to strike Menethil Harbor.",h="Dragonmaw orcs gather at Angerfang Encampment in the central Wetlands, threatening nearby dwarven settlements.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Bogs",b="Dragonmaw warriors hold the marsh around Angerfang Encampment in the central Wetlands. Barricades and watchtowers guard the camp, where warriors, bonewarders, and dark spellcasters loyal to the old ways gather. From these defenses, the clan raids travelers on the roads and menaces nearby dwarven digs, including Whelgar's Excavation Site.",sp=0},{t="Nek'rosh's Ambition",b="Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher leads the Dragonmaw from Angerfang. He is the son of Nekros, the warlock who enslaved the red dragonflight at Grim Batol. Nek'rosh hates the Alliance and has gathered catapults and raised war banners for an assault on Menethil Harbor. Alliance commanders in the port city send champions into the camp to seize the banners, break the war machines, and kill Nek'rosh before his attack can set the harbor ablaze.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules the Angerfang Encampment?",a="Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher rules the Dragonmaw at Angerfang. He is the son of the notorious Dragonmaw warlock Nekros Skullcrusher, and directs regional raiding parties while planning to conquer Menethil Harbor.",al={"who leads angerfang","angerfang boss","who is in charge here","nekrosh camp"},it="in_charge"},{q="Are the orcs here allied with Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Dragonmaw here remain independent of Thrall's New Horde and cling to the dark heritage of the Old Horde. They are hostile to Alliance and Horde travelers alike, and Thrall's warriors consider them feral outcasts and hunt them for armor crafting materials.",al={"are dragonmaw horde","are angerfang friendly to horde","is angerfang part of thralls horde"},it="allies"},{q="Why is the Alliance focused on destroying this camp?",a="Captain Stoutfist and Menethil Harbor's dwarven defenders learned that Nek'rosh had gathered catapults and a large force at Angerfang to bombard and conquer the harbor. The Alliance attacks first to break the siege before it begins.",al={"why attack angerfang","captain stoutfist angerfang","why kill nekrosh"},it="threat"},{q="Why do warlocks seek out this encampment?",a="Dragonmaw dark spellcasters at Angerfang carry Rods of Channeling, dark ritual tools sought by practitioners of the demonic arts who need to complete the Tome of the Cabal.",al={"warlock quest angerfang","tome of the cabal wetlands","rod of channeling angerfang"},it="item"},{q="What is Angerfang Encampment?",a="Angerfang Encampment is the primary stronghold of the Dragonmaw orcs in the central Wetlands. Sprawling across the murky terrain, this fortified outpost serves as the staging ground and rallying point for Dragonmaw forces plotting to conquer the region and march against Menethil Harbor.",al={"what is angerfang encampment","angerfang camp wetlands","about angerfang encampment"},it="place",add="02ce636e"},{q="What happened at Angerfang Encampment?",a="Following the Second War and their eventual retreat into the marshes, the remnants of the Dragonmaw clan established this encampment as their main base of operations. Under the command of Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, the clan amassed siege weapons and catapults here, actively preparing a campaign to destroy the Alliance stronghold at Menethil Harbor.",al={"angerfang encampment lore","history of angerfang encampment","what happened at angerfang"},it="history",add="5926baf0"},{q="Is Angerfang Encampment dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally perilous. The encampment swarms with disciplined Dragonmaw battlemasters, seasoned raiders, dark warlocks, and shadowwarders. Unprepared travelers venturing too close face overwhelming numbers and hostile orcs determined to crush any outsider.",al={"angerfang dangerous","how dangerous is angerfang encampment","is angerfang camp safe"},it="danger",add="c64d3749"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Menethil Harbor's defenders, Angerfang threatens the coast. Bringing down Nek'rosh's war banners and taking his head is vital to securing the coastal trade routes.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may seek the Rods of Channeling carried by the camp's dark shadowwarders. These artifacts are needed for the bindings written within the Tome of the Cabal."},kw={"angerfang","dragonmaw","menethil","nek'rosh","skullcrusher","stoutfist","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:465","quest:474","quest:464","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:1758","quest:1846"},src={"Angerfang Encampment"}}
E["subzone:baradin-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Baradin Bay",z="wetlands",s="In Baradin Bay, reefs and wrecks make each crossing perilous. Its waters lie between Khaz Modan, the Wetlands, the Arathi Highlands, and southern Lordaeron. Kul Tiras once patrolled the bay with a powerful navy during the Second War.",h="In Baradin Bay, reefs and wrecks make each crossing perilous.",sec={{t="A Strategic Waterway",b="Baradin Bay links the harbors of the Eastern Kingdoms. Menethil Harbor lies on its Wetlands shore, and Southshore stands in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Shallow sandbanks and jagged shoals threaten ships, as do murlocs, crocolisks, and deep-sea sharks.",sp=0},{t="Graveyard of the Fleets",b="During the Second War, Kul Tiras and the Horde fought across Baradin Bay. The broken hulls of the Kul Tiran Third Fleet, called the Lost Fleet, lie half-submerged along the Wetlands coast. Other ships sank at Drowned Reef. Hostile spirits, salvagers, and sea beasts haunt the waters around the ruined ships.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What major ports are located along Baradin Bay?",a="Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands and Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills are the bay's chief ports, sustaining naval travel across the sea.",al={"baradin bay ports","harbors in baradin bay","where does baradin bay lead"},it="place"},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks along the bay's coast?",a="The wrecks along the Wetlands shore belong to the Lost Fleet, the Kul Tiras Third Fleet destroyed during the Second War. Other ships sank on Drowned Reef off the Arathi coast.",al={"wetlands shipwrecks","why are ships sunken here","lost fleet origin"},it="history"},{q="What threats can be found in the waters of Baradin Bay?",a="Murlocs and swamp crocolisks threaten the shallows. Deeper waters hold predatory crabs, sharks, and restless spirits of drowned sailors.",al={"baradin bay monsters","murlocs in baradin bay","is it safe to swim in baradin bay"},it="threat"},{q="Which territories border Baradin Bay?",a="Baradin Bay borders northwestern Dun Morogh, the Wetlands, the Arathi Highlands, southern Hillsbrad, and Gilneas.",al={"what zones border baradin bay","baradin bay geography"},it="place"},{q="What is Baradin Bay?",a="Baradin Bay is a vast arm of the Great Sea tucked along the western coastline of the central Eastern Kingdoms. Its waters stretch from northwestern Dun Morogh in Khaz Modan all the way north toward the southern reaches of Gilneas and Hillsbrad. It serves as a vital maritime corridor linking kingdoms such as Stromgarde, Gilneas, and Ironforge's coastal holdings, with Menethil Harbor resting prominently upon its southern shores.",al={"baradin bay overview","where is baradin bay","what is this bay"},it="place",add="3e0a5d97"},{q="Is Baradin Bay dangerous?",a="Venturing into Baradin Bay's waters is far from safe. The shallows along the coast are infested with aggressive murlocs and hungry crocolisks, while the open, deeper waters harbor ferocious sharks and giant crabs. Beyond natural perils, treacherous reefs and lingering naval dangers have claimed dozens of vessels over the years, leaving waterlogged hazards lurking just beneath the surface.",al={"baradin bay threats","danger in baradin bay","is it safe to swim baradin bay"},it="danger",add="9b3de034"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Baradin Bay links operations in Khaz Modan with outposts in Arathi and Hillsbrad. Naval hazards and wreckage make every crossing risky.",["race:Human"]="For humans, especially those tracing their lineage to Kul Tiras or Lordaeron, Baradin Bay is solemn ground where Second War sailors rest beneath the waves."},kw={"baradin bay","drowned reef","great sea","kul tiras","lost fleet","menethil harbor","southshore","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:lost-fleet","subzone:drowned-reef","subzone:southshore","topic:kul-tiras","topic:second-war","subzone:faldir-s-cove"},src={"Baradin Bay"}}
E["subzone:black-channel-marsh"] = {t="subzone",n="Black Channel Marsh",z="wetlands",s="Raptors prowl Black Channel Marsh beside the road to Menethil Harbor. The mire lies in the Wetlands’ southwest, where travelers and couriers face danger along the coast.",h="Raptors prowl Black Channel Marsh beside the road to Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="Peril on the Menethil Road",b="Black Channel Marsh spreads across the low ground southwest of the main road to Menethil Harbor. Caravan drivers and couriers know the danger there. The raised road may seem safe, but territorial raptors live among the stagnant channels and thick reeds. Hungry beasts often stray into the road, ambushing recruits and weary travelers who wander even a little from the path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Black Channel Marsh located?",a="Black Channel Marsh lies in the southwestern Wetlands, along the southern side of the main road into Menethil Harbor.",al={"where is black channel marsh","black channel marsh location","wetlands black channel"},it="place"},{q="Why is this marsh considered dangerous for travelers?",a="Raptors lair throughout the marsh and hunt near its edge. They prowl close to the road, catching travelers and inexperienced adventurers unaware.",al={"why is it dangerous","threats in black channel marsh","raptors on road"},it="danger"},{q="Who travels through here most often?",a="Alliance messengers, dwarven merchants, and travelers going between Ironforge and Menethil Harbor’s docks often use the road beside the marsh.",al={"who uses this road","travelers here"},it="people"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track or tame fierce Wetlands raptors beside the main road, though the marsh makes dangerous ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you rely on this road to connect Menethil Harbor with the rest of Khaz Modan, while raptors remain a constant danger."},kw={"black channel marsh","marsh","menethil harbor","raptors","swamp","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor"},src={"Black Channel Marsh"}}
E["subzone:bluegill-marsh"] = {t="subzone",n="Bluegill Marsh",z="wetlands",s="In western Wetlands, Bluegill Marsh is claimed by the hostile Bluegill tribe. Their huts and waterways are guarded by Gobbler, and travelers risk being surrounded in the shallows.",h="In western Wetlands, Bluegill Marsh is claimed by the hostile Bluegill tribe.",sec={{t="A Swarming Hazard",b="Bluegill murlocs crowd the muddy flats and reed beds of the western Wetlands. Their tribe has built crude camps in the stagnant water and claims the marsh as its own. They live and hunt in close-knit packs. Travelers and scouts from Menethil Harbor risk ambush from every direction when they wade into Bluegill territory, where the chieftain Gobbler prowls the shallows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Bluegill Marsh?",a="Bluegill Marsh is a boggy subzone in the western Wetlands. It is the main home and nesting ground of the aggressive Bluegill murlocs.",al={"where is bluegill marsh","what is this place","wetlands murloc swamp"},it="place"},{q="Who rules over the marsh?",a="Gobbler, a powerful and vicious murloc, rules the Bluegill tribe. He watches over its clustered camps and strikes down land-walkers who enter the waters.",al={"murloc leader wetlands","gobbler","who leads the bluegill murlocs"},it="residents"},{q="Why is it dangerous to travel here alone?",a="Bluegill murlocs gather in bands of two or three around their huts and shorelines. Their numbers and the deep, slowing mud make it easy to overwhelm a lone traveler.",al={"why are there so many murlocs","is bluegill marsh hard","murloc aggro"},it="danger"},{q="Why do travelers venture into Bluegill Marsh?",a="Scouts and adventurers from nearby settlements such as Menethil Harbor venture into Bluegill Marsh to thin the aggressive murloc population and recover stolen goods from their camps.",al={"why go here","bluegill marsh quests","reasons to visit"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is it called Bluegill Marsh?",a="The marsh takes its name directly from the Bluegill murlocs who have established multiple camps throughout its murky waters. Their aggressive tribe dominates the western wetlands here, making the area infamous under their banner.",al={"why bluegill marsh","bluegill marsh name meaning","where does bluegill marsh get its name"},it="name",add="c61162da"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Near Menethil Harbor, the aggressive Bluegill murlocs threaten travelers and supply lines crossing the western Wetlands."},kw={"bluegill","bluegill marsh","gobbler","menethil","murloc","swamp","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:murloc"},src={"Bluegill Marsh"}}
E["subzone:deepwater-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Deepwater Tavern",z="wetlands",s="At Menethil Harbor, the Deepwater Tavern gives travelers a place to rest and find work. The inn is a meeting spot and resupply stop, where harbor rumors mingle with the chance of a brawl.",h="At Menethil Harbor, the Deepwater Tavern gives travelers a place to rest and find work.",sec={{t="Heart of Menethil Harbor",b="In Menethil Harbor, the Deepwater Tavern shelters travelers from the marsh's rain and difficult roads. Sailors, dockworkers, merchants, and weary adventurers gather beneath its timber beams to trade news, meet, warm themselves, and patch their wounds. Local merchants and a resident first aid trainer serve those bound for the marsh or setting out across the Great Sea. The tavern is lively, and disputes over spilled ale can turn into brawls. Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn is known to spark them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Deepwater Tavern located?",a="The Deepwater Tavern stands near the waterfront of Menethil Harbor, the Wetlands' main port on Khaz Modan's western coast.",al={"deepwater tavern location","where is deepwater tavern","menethil harbor inn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services are available inside the tavern?",a="The tavern offers lodging and refreshments, along with local merchants and a resident first aid trainer. These make it a resupply and healing stop for adventurers traveling through the marshlands.",al={"deepwater tavern services","menethil tavern trainers","what can i find at deepwater tavern"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who frequently starts brawls in the tavern?",a="Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn, a shifty troublemaker, frequently starts brawls among the tavern's rowdy patrons and sailors.",al={"bar brawl menethil","tapoke slim jahn","who starts fights at deepwater tavern"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the tavern so busy?",a="Menethil Harbor is a major shipping and naval gateway between Khaz Modan and Kalimdor. As the town's sole major inn, the Deepwater Tavern draws a steady flow of sailors, mercenaries, and Alliance adventurers heading into the Wetlands.",al={"why visit deepwater tavern","why is deepwater tavern popular"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Deepwater Tavern?",a="The Deepwater Tavern is the primary inn and community hub of Menethil Harbor, the bustling Alliance seaport in the Wetlands. Sailors, merchants, travelers, and adventurers passing through Khaz Modan stop here to rest, buy provisions, seek medical aid, or pick up local work. It remains one of the liveliest gathering points in the marshlands.",al={"what is deepwater tavern","deepwater tavern wetlands","menethil harbor tavern"},it="place",add="d7fa1340"},{q="Is Deepwater Tavern dangerous?",a="While the tavern sits safely under Alliance protection inside Menethil Harbor, it is far from quiet. Drunken patrons and colorful regulars frequently stir up violent fistfights on the taproom floor, often provoked by troublemakers like Tapoke Slim Jahn. Keep your wits about you, but you face little genuine peril beneath its roof.",al={"is deepwater tavern safe","brawls deepwater tavern","danger deepwater tavern"},it="danger",add="e51423df"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member traveling between Ironforge and the open sea, you can use the Deepwater Tavern as an indispensable rallying point and place to rest."},kw={"deepwater tavern","first aid trainer","innkeeper","menethil harbor","tapoke slim jahn","tavern brawl","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},src={"Deepwater Tavern"}}
E["subzone:direforge-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Direforge Hill",z="wetlands",s="Hostile Dark Iron dwarves hold Direforge Hill in the northeastern Wetlands, southeast of Dun Modr and northeast of the Green Belt.",h="Hostile Dark Iron dwarves hold Direforge Hill in the northeastern Wetlands, southeast of Dun Modr and...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Dark Sorcery",b="Dark Iron dwarves hold the northeastern Wetlands hill under Balgaras the Foul, a Dark Iron dwarf warlock. Their encampment lies southeast of Dun Modr.",sp=0},{t="The Threat to the Wetlands",b="Travelers crossing the northeastern Wetlands face the hostile Dark Iron encampment on Direforge Hill. Balgaras the Foul commands the dwarves there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Direforge Hill located?",a="Direforge Hill stands in the northeastern Wetlands, southeast of Dun Modr and northeast of the Green Belt. It lies northwest of the rocky bluffs of Raptor Ridge.",al={"direforge hill location","where is direforge hill","direforge wetlands"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls Direforge Hill right now?",a="Hostile Dark Iron dwarves occupy Direforge Hill under the command of Balgaras the Foul, a warlock.",al={"who is at direforge hill","who lives at direforge hill","direforge hill mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Why is Direforge Hill significant to the Wetlands?",a="Direforge Hill holds a hostile Dark Iron campsite in the northeastern Wetlands. Balgaras the Foul and his dwarves threaten travelers through the region.",al={"why is direforge hill important","direforge threat","what is happening at direforge hill"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul is a Dark Iron dwarf warlock who commands the forces encamped at Direforge Hill. His corrupted arts and aggressive presence in the hills make him a priority target for those defending the marsh.",al={"balgaras","balgaras the foul lore","who is balgaras"},it="leader"},{q="What is Direforge Hill?",a="Direforge Hill is an elevated ridge in the northeastern reaches of the Wetlands, situated southeast of Dun Modr and northwest of Raptor Ridge. It serves as an entrenched forward encampment for the hostile Dark Iron dwarves operating in the region.",al={"what is direforge hill","direforge hill info","direforge wetlands"},it="place",add="5340135d"},{q="Is Direforge Hill dangerous?",a="Direforge Hill is exceptionally dangerous. The encampment is swarming with aggressive Dark Iron dwarves and their vicious warlocks, all organized under the ruthless leadership of Balgaras the Foul. Intruders who wander up the ridge are quickly attacked on sight.",al={"is direforge hill safe","direforge danger","direforge hill threats"},it="danger",add="c35b9f4a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard dwarf of Ironforge, seeing the Dark Iron clan's treachery reach the Wetlands, especially under warlocks like Balgaras, is an outrage answered with cold steel.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid passing through the Wetlands, you must contend with the hostile Dark Iron encampment on Direforge Hill."},kw={"balgaras","balgaras the foul","dark iron dwarves","direforge","direforge hill","dun modr","green belt","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:green-belt","subzone:raptor-ridge","quest:463"},src={"Direforge Hill"}}
E["subzone:dragonmaw-gates"] = {t="subzone",n="Dragonmaw Gates",z="wetlands",s="At the Dragonmaw Gates, heavy fortifications bar the road climbing from the eastern Wetlands. They guard the ascent to Grim Batol, a mountain fortress in the cursed dwarven ruins.",h="At the Dragonmaw Gates, heavy fortifications bar the road climbing from the eastern Wetlands.",sec={{t="Sentinels of Grim Batol",b="Carved into rugged peaks along the eastern Wetlands, the Dragonmaw Gates seal the winding road to Grim Batol. The barriers take their name from the Dragonmaw orcs, who held the dwarven mountain city during the Second War. The road remains a fortified checkpoint, and the ascent still brings danger. Powerful drakes haunt the pass, while grim reminders of the clan's dark history linger in the mountains.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Threshold",b="The Dragonmaw orcs were broken and scattered after the Demon Soul was destroyed, but the mountain path remains dangerous. Powerful red dragons have been seen watching the winding slopes and perches around the gates. Monstrous drakes and Dragonmaw remnants still lurk in the nearby hills, and the gates remain a firm barrier against travelers bold enough to venture into the heights.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the Dragonmaw Gates lead?",a="The gates seal the winding mountain path ascending east from the Wetlands directly into Grim Batol and the surrounding mountain heights.",al={"path past dragonmaw gates","what is behind dragonmaw gates","road past gates"},it="place"},{q="Why are they called the Dragonmaw Gates?",a="The gates take their name from the Dragonmaw orcs, who occupied Grim Batol during the Second War and used foul sorcery to enslave red dragons.",al={"why called dragonmaw gates","dragonmaw gate name","dragonmaw orcs wetlands"},it="name"},{q="Can travelers pass through the gates?",a="The massive gates are firmly shut and heavily defended, barring normal passage into the high mountains.",al={"can you open dragonmaw gates","getting through dragonmaw gates"},gp=true},{q="Who guards the road around the gates?",a="Fierce red dragonspawn and drakes haunt the road and rugged nearby passes, along with scattered orcs and dark threats clinging to the mountain slopes.",al={"who is at dragonmaw gates","dragons at dragonmaw gates","axtroz dragonmaw gates"},it="residents"},{q="What happened at the Dragonmaw Gates?",a="These imposing gates were fortified by the Dragonmaw orcs when they held the mountain fortress of Grim Batol and controlled the red dragonflight during the Second War. After the orcs were defeated and driven out, red dragons led by the drake Axtroz came to watch over the approaches to the mountain.",al={"dragonmaw gates history","what happened at dragonmaw gates","dragonmaw gates past"},it="history",add="fb3392df"},{q="How dangerous are the Dragonmaw Gates?",a="They are exceptionally dangerous. The red dragons guarding the roadway, led by powerful drakes like Axtroz, do not welcome mortal trespassers near the approach to Grim Batol. Beyond the dragons, hostile Dragonmaw orcs still haunt the surrounding Wetlands hills, making any venture toward the gates a perilous journey for travelers.",al={"is dragonmaw gates dangerous","dragonmaw gates danger","are dragonmaw gates safe"},it="danger",add="3dd629b0"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the gates mark the sealed threshold to Grim Batol, an ancestral home abandoned after the War of the Three Hammers and later desecrated by the Dragonmaw orcs.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance watches the gates warily, knowing that anything emerging from the high road threatens the stability of the entire Wetlands."},kw={"axtroz","dragonmaw clan","dragonmaw gates","grim batol","mountain pass","red dragonflight","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:grim-batol","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Dragonmaw Gates"}}
E["subzone:dun-algaz"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Algaz",z="wetlands",s="Dragonmaw orcs have laid siege to Dun Algaz, cutting easy passage between Ironforge’s lands and Menethil Harbor. The fortified pass and its tunnels link Loch Modan with the Wetlands.",h="Dragonmaw orcs have laid siege to Dun Algaz, cutting easy passage between Ironforge’s lands and Menethil...",sec={{t="A Chokepoint Between Realms",b="Dun Algaz cuts through the jagged peaks between Loch Modan and the Wetlands. The pass predates the War of the Three Hammers. After the Wildhammer clan was driven from Ironforge, its people used this route to migrate north. Stone tunnels, bastions, and watchposts guard the way. Whoever holds Dun Algaz controls the only overland road from the dwarven heartlands to Menethil Harbor on the western sea.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Resurgence",b="During the Second War, the Old Horde retreated to Dun Algaz after its defeat at Dun Modr. The pass became its final southern bulwark against Sir Anduin Lothar’s forces. The Alliance reclaimed it for a time, but Dragonmaw orcs have overrun the stronghold again. Dwarven Mountaineers have fallen back to the upper tunnels, leaving the mountain corridor a deadly gauntlet for travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Dun Algaz so dangerous right now?",a="Dragonmaw orcs have descended from the surrounding mountains and seized the lower pass and stronghold. Dwarven Mountaineers have been pushed back to the upper pass near Algaz Station, leaving the main road swarming with hostile orcs who ambush travelers between Loch Modan and the Wetlands.",al={"why are there orcs in dun algaz","dun algaz orcs","who controls dun algaz"},it="danger"},{q="Why is this pass so important to the dwarves?",a="Dun Algaz is the main overland route from Ironforge and Loch Modan to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Menethil Harbor is Khaz Modan’s main shipping gateway to the rest of the Alliance territories, making the pass vital for supplies, troops, and trade.",al={"dun algaz importance","why does ironforge need dun algaz"},it="purpose"},{q="Did Dun Algaz play a role in the Second War?",a="Yes. After their defeat at Dun Modr, the Orcish Horde fell back across the Thandol Valley to make Dun Algaz a defensive stronghold. Sir Anduin Lothar ordered an assault to drive them from Khaz Modan, but the Alliance could not fully root out the Horde, leaving Dun Algaz among its final strongholds in the region.",al={"dun algaz second war","anduin lothar dun algaz"},it="history"},{q="What is the history between Dun Algaz and the Wildhammer dwarves?",a="Long before the Second War, the Wildhammer dwarves were driven from Ironforge during the ancient War of the Three Hammers. They traveled through Dun Algaz to migrate north into the Wetlands and eventually settle in Grim Batol.",al={"wildhammer dun algaz","war of the three hammers pass"},it="ties"},{q="What is Dun Algaz?",a="Dun Algaz is a series of carved tunnels and mountain ramparts that cut through the peaks connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands. Once a secure dwarven stronghold and the primary overland corridor between Ironforge and the northern shores, this fortified pass ensures critical transit between the heart of Khaz Modan and Menethil Harbor.",al={"what is dun algaz","dun algaz pass","dun algaz gate"},it="place",add="e0cd650e"},{q="Who controls Dun Algaz?",a="Dun Algaz has fallen largely into the hands of the Dragonmaw orcs. Although dwarven Mountaineers still guard the upper tunnels and secure the northern approach from Loch Modan, hostile Dragonmaw raiders have entrenched themselves throughout the lower reaches and mountain roadways, seizing control of the pass.",al={"who lives in dun algaz","who controls dun algaz","who runs dun algaz"},it="residents",add="f60a7bc4"},{q="Why was Dun Algaz abandoned by the dwarves?",a="The stronghold was abandoned after fierce assaults by remnants of the Dragonmaw clan. Overwhelming dwarven defenders stationed within the stronghold, the orcs forced the Ironforge mountaineers to retreat and consolidate their lines at the upper tunnel of the pass, leaving much of the road unmaintained and occupied by enemy forces.",al={"why was dun algaz abandoned","why is dun algaz ruined","why did dwarves leave dun algaz"},it="ruin",add="59a004f5"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Dun Algaz as an ancestral highway cut through the spine of Khaz Modan. Dragonmaw orcs now occupy its dwarven bastions and threaten the supply lines to Menethil Harbor, an ongoing insult and security crisis.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Dun Algaz is a critical route for supplies and troops, joining Menethil Harbor with Loch Modan and Ironforge."},kw={"algaz gate","algaz station","dragonmaw","dun algaz","loch modan","menethil harbor","mountain pass","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","zone:lochmodan","subzone:algaz-station","topic:dragonmaw-clan","quest:455","topic:second-war","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Dun Algaz"}}
E["subzone:dun-modr"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Modr",z="wetlands",s="Dun Modr has fallen to Dark Iron dwarves, leaving the Thandol Span's southern approach in hostile hands. The fortress once changed hands in a fierce struggle during the Second War.",h="Dun Modr has fallen to Dark Iron dwarves, leaving the Thandol Span's southern approach in hostile hands.",sec={{t="A Contested Bastion",b="At Wetlands' northern edge, Dun Modr commands the main road between Khaz Modan and the northern human kingdoms. That route has drawn armies to the fortress across the decades. During the Second War, the Orcish Horde seized the dwarven stronghold and used it to launch raids and resist Alliance armies. Stromgarde warriors sailed from Tol Barad to reclaim it, and the Orcs struck back in a bloody struggle. Alliance forces under Lord Anduin Lothar eventually drove the invaders south across the Thandol Span, returning the fortress to dwarven hands.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Iron Incursion",b="Dun Modr lay exposed while Ironforge's attention was divided and many of its finest mountaineers served the Alliance abroad. Dark Iron invaders took advantage, sabotaged the Thandol Span with explosives, then swarmed the fortress. Led by the warlock Balgaras the Foul, they overcame the defenders and drove out the Bronzebeard garrison. Mountaineers now hold a grim perimeter just down the road, seeking aid to drive out the occupiers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Dun Modr so important?",a="Dun Modr commands the main northern road through the Wetlands to the Thandol Span. Whoever holds the fortress can control overland traffic, supplies, and military movement between Khaz Modan and northern Lordaeron.",al={"why does dun modr matter","importance of dun modr","dun modr strategic value"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls Dun Modr right now?",a="Dark Iron dwarves hold Dun Modr, led there by the warlock Balgaras the Foul. Bronzebeard Mountaineers loyal to Ironforge watch from a nearby camp and hope to reclaim the fortress.",al={"who is in dun modr","who runs dun modr","who lives in dun modr"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to Dun Modr during the Second War?",a="The Orcish Horde seized Dun Modr and used it as a forward base. Stromgarde forces attacked from Tol Barad, and fierce clashes followed until Anduin Lothar's Alliance forces drove the Horde from the region.",al={"second war dun modr","orcs in dun modr","did horde take dun modr"},it="history"},{q="Who is Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul is the Dark Iron warlock leading the occupation of Dun Modr. His forces damaged the Thandol Span and drove the local Ironforge defenders from the fortress.",al={"balgaras the foul lore","balgaras who","dark iron leader dun modr"},it="leader"},{q="What is Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr is an ancient, fortified dwarven city standing along the main northern road in the Wetlands, just south of the Thandol Span. Once a bustling stronghold with its own smithy and inn, it historically guarded the gateway between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms of Lordaeron.",al={"what is dun modr","dun modr lore","about dun modr"},it="place",add="9363f36e"},{q="Why is Dun Modr ruined?",a="While Ironforge sent its mountaineers and soldiers to fight far across Azeroth for the Alliance, Dark Iron dwarves struck the vulnerable region from within. They sabotaged the Thandol Span, overran the depleted defenses of Dun Modr, and left the city smoking in ruin.",al={"why is dun modr destroyed","dun modr fall","what ruined dun modr"},it="ruin",add="72873e9f"},{q="Is Dun Modr dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Dun Modr is swarming with hostile Dark Iron dwarves, led by the wicked warlock Balgaras the Foul. Travelers attempting to cross north across the Thandol Span risk being ambushed unless they tread carefully or lend aid to the embattled dwarven mountaineers stationed nearby.",al={"dun modr threats","dun modr danger","is it safe near dun modr"},it="danger",add="3c329954"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing a storied Bronzebeard mountain settlement in Dark Iron hands is a bitter insult, and calls for vengeance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face a threat to the route across the Thandol Span, which links Ironforge with the northern Alliance remnants."},kw={"balgaras the foul","dark iron","dun modr","ironforge","mountaineers","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:thandol-span","quest:303","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-algaz","topic:second-war","topic:anduin-lothar","quest:631","zone:ironforge"},src={"Dun Modr"}}
E["subzone:green-belt"] = {t="subzone",n="Green Belt",z="wetlands",s="In eastern Wetlands, Green Belt lies below the ridges of Grim Batol. Bog beasts, crocolisks, and toxic oozes roam its marshes, while Rethiel the Greenwarden keeps watch alone.",h="In eastern Wetlands, Green Belt lies below the ridges of Grim Batol.",sec={{t="A Wild and Contested Fen",b="Green Belt fills the eastern interior of Wetlands, where mossy waters make travel hazardous. Massive crocolisks, shifting oozes, and shambling bog beasts roam the fen. Deep within it, a solitary watch post is manned by Rethiel the Greenwarden, a night elf who studies the fen's ecology and keeps its hostile creatures in check.",sp=0},{t="Remnants of the Second War",b="Wreckage from a Dragonmaw clan caravan lies scattered in the muck, left behind after the catastrophic battle at nearby Grim Batol. Crimson whelplings linger around the broken carts and crushed cages, reminders of the clan's past enslavement of Alexstrasza and her red dragon brood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Green Belt located?",a="Green Belt occupies the eastern half of Wetlands, along the soggy lowlands between the main road and the foothills rising toward Grim Batol.",al={"green belt location","where is green belt","green belt wetlands map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is a night elf keeping watch alone in the Wetlands marsh. Far from his ancestral home of Kalimdor, he seeks to preserve nature's balance in the swamp and enlists travelers to deal with corrupting beasts and oozes.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel the greenwarden","night elf in green belt"},it="identity"},{q="Why are there red whelps and broken wagons here?",a="The broken wagons are the remains of a Dragonmaw clan supply caravan caught in the aftermath of the Second War, when the orcs were routed from Grim Batol and their hold over the red dragonflight was shattered.",al={"dragonmaw caravan","why are there whelps in wetlands","red whelps wetlands"},it="history"},{q="What threats wander the Green Belt?",a="Dangerous crocolisks, toxic living oozes, and towering bog beasts roam Green Belt, blending into the sodden vegetation.",al={"green belt mobs","dangers in green belt","what monsters live here"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Green Belt?",a="The Green Belt is a wild, overgrown expanse situated in the eastern Wetlands. Unlike the drier roads and dwarven excavations to the west and south, this sodden tract remains largely untamed marshland, characterized by thick bog growth, muddy pools, and the solitary presence of the mysterious keeper known as Rethiel the Greenwarden.",al={"what is green belt","green belt wetlands","about green belt"},it="place",add="b9266860"},{q="Who lives in the Green Belt?",a="No civilized settlement claims the Green Belt. Aside from native swamp predators, the only notable resident watching over these wild wetlands is Rethiel the Greenwarden. He makes his vigil here in solitude, monitoring the natural balance and defending the marsh against encroaching blights.",al={"who lives in green belt","green belt inhabitants","green belt residents"},it="residents",add="453ecde9"},{q="How dangerous is the Green Belt?",a="Venturing into the Green Belt poses serious perils for unwary travelers. The murky waters teem with aggressive crocolisks, shifting oozes, and towering bog beasts. Moreover, remnants of shattered Dragonmaw wagons attract untamed red whelps that aggressively strike down anyone intruding into their territory.",al={"is green belt dangerous","green belt dangers","threats in green belt"},it="danger",add="e91fe995"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may find Rethiel the Greenwarden's lonely watch in an Eastern Kingdoms swamp surprising. His presence recalls the Cenarion circle and night elven devotion to healing wild lands wherever they lie.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how twisted oozes and unchecked bog beasts disrupt the marsh's natural harmony. The fen is a concern for keepers of the wild."},kw={"bog beasts","dragonmaw","green belt","grim batol","oozes","rethiel","wetlands","whelps"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","zone:wetlands","subzone:grim-batol","topic:dragonmaw-clan","quest:463"},src={"Green Belt"}}
E["subzone:grim-batol"] = {t="subzone",n="Grim Batol",z="wetlands",s="Grim Batol's gates remain sealed above the eastern Wetlands. The Wildhammer dwarves abandoned the fortress after a curse during the War of the Three Hammers, and the Dragonmaw orcs later used it as a dragon-breeding lair.",h="Grim Batol's gates remain sealed above the eastern Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Fortress Twice Cursed",b="Thane Khardros Wildhammer carved Grim Batol from the jagged mountains east of the marsh after the ancient civil war among the three clans. During the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorceress Modgud laid siege to the fortress. Khardros struck her down, but before she died, Modgud cast a foul shadow across its stones. The lingering taint made the halls uninhabitable, and the surviving Wildhammer dwarves abandoned their kingdom and migrated north into the Hinterlands.",sp=0},{t="Chains of the Dragon Queen",b="During the Second War, Orgrim Doomhammer sent the Dragonmaw clan to claim Grim Batol. The warlock Nekros Skullcrusher led the orcs, who used the ancient artifact called the Demon Soul to enslave the red Dragonqueen Alexstrasza deep beneath the mountain. Chained there, Alexstrasza was forced to hatch broods for the Horde's war effort until a small band of heroes shattered the artifact. Freed, the enraged Dragon Aspect incinerated the orcs within. Grim Batol was left a desolate ruin, watched closely by surviving red dragons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can players enter Grim Batol?",a="No. The colossal stone gates at the end of the mountain road remain barred to travelers. You can visit only the gates and exterior battlements in the eastern Wetlands mountains.",al={"can i go inside grim batol","is grim batol open","grim batol gate"},gp=true},{q="Why did the Wildhammer dwarves abandon it?",a="During the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorceress Modgud laid a vile shadow curse on Grim Batol before she was slain. The taint made the fortress unlivable, driving the Wildhammers to abandon it and build Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.",al={"why did dwarves leave grim batol","wildhammer curse","modgud curse"},it="ruin"},{q="What happened to the Dragonmaw orcs who lived here?",a="The mage Rhonin and his companions shattered the Demon Soul, freeing the captive Dragonqueen Alexstrasza from her chains. Enraged by her captivity, she and her brood incinerated Nekros Skullcrusher and broke the Dragonmaw presence in the fortress.",al={"dragonmaw grim batol","what happened to the orcs here","nekros skullcrusher"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Grim Batol right now?",a="Grim Batol is an abandoned ruin. Remnants of the Dragonmaw clan and wild beasts linger in the surrounding crags, while the Red Dragonflight watches the cursed mountain to guard against a return of its dark history.",al={"who owns grim batol","who lives in grim batol now"},it="residents"},{q="What is Grim Batol?",a="Grim Batol is an ancient, sprawling mountain fortress carved into the eastern peaks beyond the Wetlands. Though its towering gates and battlements overlook the marshes, the vast majority of the stronghold extends deep underground. Founded by the Wildhammer clan after their exile from Ironforge, it served as their proud capital before dark sorcery corrupted the halls, leaving it a gloomy, foreboding bastion that has seen centuries of sorrow, occupation, and war.",al={"what is grim batol","grim batol fortress","about grim batol"},it="place",add="7aeea9cc"},{q="Is Grim Batol dangerous?",a="Grim Batol is exceptionally dangerous and strictly sealed away from travelers. Lingering dark sorcery from the War of the Three Hammers still taints its interior, and the skies and approaches around its colossal gates are patrolled by elite, hostile red dragons watchful of any trespassers. Between the lingering corruption within and the deadly guardians without, any approach to the stronghold invites immediate peril.",al={"how dangerous is grim batol","is grim batol safe","threats at grim batol"},it="danger",add="06dc57c0"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For a dwarf, Grim Batol recalls the War of the Three Hammers: a once-proud sister city to Ironforge, made unlivable by Dark Iron sorcery.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Grim Batol recalls the Second War, when the Dragonmaw clan used enslaved dragons to conquer the skies before their violent ruin."},kw={"alexstrasza","demon soul","dragonmaw","grim batol","modgud","nekros","wetlands","wildhammer"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:wildhammer-clan","topic:dragonmaw-clan","topic:second-war","zone:hinterlands","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:dun-algaz"},src={"Grim Batol"}}
E["subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironbeard's Tomb",z="wetlands",s="West of the road to Dun Modr, Ironbeard's Tomb lies defiled and overrun by acidic oozes. A stone statue watches over the outdoor graveyard, where travelers search the slime for lost possessions.",h="West of the road to Dun Modr, Ironbeard's Tomb lies defiled and overrun by acidic oozes.",sec={{t="A Befouled Resting Place",b="Ironbeard's Tomb overlooks the marshes beside the road north to Dun Modr. A great stone statue, believed to show Ironbeard, watches over the burial plot. Black and crimson oozes have overrun the crypt below, tainting the resting place. Dwarves no longer bring their dead here. Those who enter the vaults search among the remains swallowed by the slimes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Ironbeard?",a="Little is recorded about Ironbeard, but the statue and crypt suggest he was an honored dwarf in the Wetlands. His likeness watches over the hillside above the cemetery.",al={"ironbeard lore","who is ironbeard","statue identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the tomb abandoned?",a="Acidic black and crimson oozes have overrun the crypt. The burial grounds are defiled and dangerous, so mourning families no longer bring their dead here.",al={"why abandoned","oozes in tomb","what happened to the crypt"},it="ruin"},{q="Why do adventurers explore Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Travelers search the slimes for swallowed possessions, especially Sida's lost bag, while trying to fight back the infestation.",al={"why go here","sida bag","tomb quests"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Ironbeard's Tomb located?",a="Ironbeard's Tomb sits in north-central Wetlands, in a hill just west of the main road north toward Dun Modr.",al={"tomb location","how to get to ironbeard tomb","ironbeard wetlands map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Ironbeard's Tomb is an ancient dwarven burial site situated in the northern reaches of the Wetlands, just west of the road leading toward Dun Modr. The site consists of an underground crypt, an overgrown graveyard, and a stone statue erected in honor of Ironbeard himself.",al={"what is this place","ironbeard tomb lore","about ironbeards tomb"},it="place",add="7c55bc22"},{q="Is Ironbeard's Tomb dangerous?",a="The grounds are deeply hazardous. The sacred crypt and surrounding graveyard have been entirely defiled by foul oozes, ranging from black and crimson slimes to monstrous varieties that consume anything in their path. Because of these foul beasts, the living no longer venture here to honor their departed.",al={"how dangerous is ironbeard tomb","ironbeards tomb monsters","threats at ironbeard tomb"},it="danger",add="6532c17b"},{q="Why is it called Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="The resting place takes its name from Ironbeard, the dwarven figure interred within the crypt. A prominent dwarven statue watches over the graveyard, commemorating his memory, though the tomb itself has fallen into decay and neglect.",al={"why ironbeard tomb","who is the tomb named after","ironbeards tomb name origin"},it="name",add="0a492c86"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing a clan hero's resting place infested by mindless marsh oozes is a bitter disgrace on the road toward the Thandol Span."},kw={"crypt","dun modr","graveyard","ironbeard","ironbeard's tomb","oozes","sida","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr","npc:sida","zone:stormwind"},src={"Ironbeard's Tomb"}}
E["subzone:lost-fleet"] = {t="subzone",n="Lost Fleet",z="wetlands",s="The Lost Fleet lies broken off the Wetlands’ northern coast, along Baradin Bay. The Kul Tiras Third Fleet was destroyed in the Second War by red dragons enslaved by the Dragonmaw clan, and its wrecks are haunted by cursed undead sailors.",h="The Lost Fleet lies broken off the Wetlands’ northern coast, along Baradin Bay.",sec={{t="A Tragic End in the Second War",b="On its last voyage in the Second War, the Kul Tiras Third Fleet came under attack from red dragons enslaved by the Dragonmaw clan. Dragonflame engulfed its ships, and the Wave Mistress and the Intrepid crashed onto the shallows and reefs of northern Bluegill Marsh. Almost the entire contingent drowned or burned. First Mate Fitzsimmons was the lone living survivor.",sp=0},{t="The Curse of Paleth",b="The sailors of the Third Fleet did not find rest in their watery grave. Deep in the Intrepid’s sunken cargo hold lay the Cursed Eye of Paleth, a forbidden artifact hoarded by the ship’s greedy commander, Captain Halyndor. The relic corrupted the drowned crews and bound their spirits to the broken timbers as raving, cursed undead. Only the ghost of First Mate Snellig retains any semblance of sanity. He wanders the marshy shore while his former crewmates lash out violently at anyone who comes near the wrecks.",sp=1,bt={"q288.4"}}},faq={{q="What is the Lost Fleet?",a="The Lost Fleet is the wreckage of several Kul Tiras warships from the Third Fleet, lying off the Wetlands’ northern coast in Baradin Bay. Destroyed in the Second War, the ships are haunted by their undead crews.",al={"lost fleet","what is this place","wetlands shipwrecks","third fleet"},it="place"},{q="How were these ships destroyed?",a="During the Second War, red dragons enslaved by the orcish Dragonmaw clan ambushed and burned the fleet. Dragonflame reduced the ships to burning hulks that foundered along the coast.",al={"who sank the ships","how did they sink","what destroyed the fleet"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are the sailors here undead?",a="A curse binds the sailors’ spirits to the wrecks. First Mate Fitzsimmons seeks help to learn why they cannot rest.",al={"why are they ghosts","undead sailors","curse of paleth"},it="threat"},{q="Did anyone survive the destruction of the fleet?",a="First Mate Fitzsimmons of the Wave Mistress is the only known living survivor of the disaster. He reached safety and now lives at Menethil Harbor.",al={"any survivors","did anyone live","fitzsimmons"}},{q="What happened to the Lost Fleet?",a="During the Second War, the Kul Tiras Third Fleet was attacked on its last voyage by red dragons enslaved by the Dragonmaw clan. Dragonfire engulfed the wooden vessels, and several burning hulls—including the Wave Mistress and the Intrepid—sank in Baradin Bay off the northern shore of Bluegill Marsh. First Mate Fitzsimmons of the Wave Mistress was the only survivor.",al={"lost fleet history","what happened to the third fleet","lost fleet background"},it="history",add="c633bffd"},{q="Who haunts the Lost Fleet?",a="The shattered hulls are populated entirely by the restless dead. Cursed sailors and marines roam the rotting decks under the thrall of Captain Halyndor, commander of the sunken Intrepid. The only spirit along the shore to keep his wits is the ghost of First Mate Snellig, while living folk avoid the bay altogether.",al={"who lives at lost fleet","lost fleet ghosts","lost fleet undead"},it="residents",add="e2b996c0"},{q="Is the Lost Fleet dangerous?",a="Yes, approaching these ruins carries extreme peril. The watery wreckage crawls with hostile undead sailors and marines who strike without mercy, capable of inflicting debilitating afflictions upon any living intruder.",al={"is lost fleet safe","lost fleet dangers","lost fleet threat"},it="danger",add="8b2f2e55"},{q="Why is it called the Lost Fleet?",a="Originally known as the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras, these vessels earned the title of the Lost Fleet—or the Doomed Fleet—after meeting total annihilation against the Dragonmaw clan's enslaved dragons during the Second War. Sunk far from their homeland and swallowed by the marshy waters of Baradin Bay, their tragic end left them remembered as ships lost to both the sea and the living world.",al={"why called lost fleet","lost fleet name origin","doomed fleet meaning"},it="name",add="0a869193"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The hulks remind the Alliance of the heavy toll Kul Tiras and the Alliance paid in the Second War. The fallen deserve respect, and their cursed torment must end.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Alliance smiths hear tales of the sunken fleet. Another ship from the same squadron, the Flying Osprey, went down carrying rare ingots of Lightforge iron."},kw={"baradin bay","bluegill marsh","doomed fleet","eye of paleth","fitzsimmons","halyndor","intrepid","lost fleet","snellig","third fleet","wave mistress","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:baradin-bay","subzone:bluegill-marsh","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","quest:270","quest:288","quest:290","quest:292"},src={"Lost Fleet"}}
E["subzone:menethil-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Menethil Bay",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Bay carries Alliance traffic along the western coast of the Wetlands. The sheltered waters open into Baradin Bay, with Menethil Harbor to the north and Dun Morogh's steep cliffs to the south. Crocolisks prowl the shallows, and sunken vessels lie below.",h="Menethil Bay carries Alliance traffic along the western coast of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Sheltered Waters of the Wetlands",b="Menethil Bay opens from the Wetlands into the Great Sea as part of Baradin Bay. Menethil Harbor lies to the north, Black Channel Marsh to the east, and Dun Morogh's coastal bluffs to the south. Crocolisks of many sizes prowl the shallow margins and marshy shores, making the water dangerous for travelers without a guide. The bay carries Alliance sea traffic, and near its mouth rests the ruined Flying Osprey, a warning of the wreckage beneath the surface.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Menethil Bay located?",a="Menethil Bay runs along the western coast of the Wetlands, within Baradin Bay. Menethil Harbor lies to the north, Black Channel Marsh to the east, and Dun Morogh's northern cliffs to the south.",al={"where is menethil bay","menethil bay location","wetlands bay"},it="place"},{q="What creatures live in Menethil Bay?",a="Crocolisks of many sizes live along the bay's marshy shores and shallow inlets. They ambush unwary swimmers, and leatherworkers hunt them for their valuable hides.",al={"menethil bay mobs","what is in the bay","crocolisks in menethil bay"}},{q="What is the sunken ship in the bay?",a="The wreck near the entrance to Menethil Bay is the Flying Osprey, lost beneath the coastal waters near the harbor approaches.",al={"shipwreck menethil bay","flying osprey","sunken ship wetlands"},it="history"},{q="Why is the bay important to the Alliance?",a="Menethil Bay shelters Menethil Harbor, the primary naval gate linking Ironforge and the northern lands of Khaz Modan to Kalimdor and the south. Ships traveling to and from Theramore and Darkshore cross these waters.",al={"importance of menethil bay","alliance port wetlands","menethil harbor water"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Menethil Bay dangerous?",a="Yes, its waters harbor aggressive wildlife that poses a serious threat to unwary travelers and divers. The bay crawls with crocolisks of various ages and sizes, known for their thick hides and vicious bites. Navigating through the inlet or exploring shipwrecks like the Flying Osprey requires constant vigilance against these predatory beasts.",al={"is menethil bay safe","menethil bay danger","threats in menethil bay"},it="danger",add="9552f6cb"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Menethil Bay is the sea approach to Menethil Harbor and protects the fragile route linking Ironforge and Stormwind to Kalimdor."},kw={"baradin bay","crocolisk","dun morogh","flying osprey","menethil bay","menethil harbor","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:baradin-bay","subzone:black-channel-marsh","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Menethil Bay"}}
E["subzone:menethil-harbor"] = {t="subzone",n="Menethil Harbor",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Harbor links the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor from its island off the Wetlands' western shore. Stone battlements and Menethil Keep's towers guard the port, where merchants, off-duty soldiers, and salty adventurers gather.",h="Menethil Harbor links the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor from its island off the Wetlands' western shore.",sec={{t="A Fortified Haven",b="Menethil Harbor honors King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron and offers the Alliance a haven on the Wetlands coast. Its remote marshland setting leaves it exposed, so massive walls, a single bridged causeway, and Menethil Keep's four stone watchtowers guard the town.",sp=0},{t="Gateway Across the Great Sea",b="Menethil Harbor is a crossroads for Alliance ships crossing the ocean to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and, by way of Southshore, Auberdine in Darkshore. The ships carry trade and diplomats, while off-duty Kul Tiran marines spend their wages at the Deepwater Tavern. Peace remains fragile. The Dragonmaw clan contests inland supply paths through Dun Algaz, and Dark Iron raiders press the northern marshes. Captain Stoutfist and the harbor garrison stay on constant alert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the ships in Menethil Harbor sail to?",a="Ships from Menethil Harbor cross the Great Sea to Kalimdor. Passenger vessels sail regularly to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh, then north to Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills and onward to the night elven haven of Auberdine.",al={"menethil harbor boat","where does the boat go","menethil ferries","kalimdor boats"},gp=true},{q="Who rules Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor is an Alliance settlement under Ironforge's authority. Captain Stoutfist commands the town guard and directs harbor defense from Menethil Keep, keeping the docks secure from swamp beasts, renegade orcs, and inland raiders.",al={"who is in charge of menethil","menethil harbor leader","who leads menethil"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the town named Menethil?",a="Menethil Harbor was named for King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron. His leadership united the human, dwarven, and elven realms into the original Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"why menethil harbor","menethil name origin","who is menethil"},it="name"},{q="What threats does the harbor face right now?",a="The Dragonmaw clan lurks in the Wetlands hills and regularly tries to cut off the pass through Dun Algaz, starving the port of reinforcements. Dark Iron incursions to the north near Dun Modr and marauding raptors add to the garrison's troubles.",al={"is menethil harbor in danger","menethil threats","wetlands orcs menethil"},it="threat"},{q="What is Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor is a fortified dwarven port town perched on an island on the western edge of the Wetlands. Sheltered behind thick stone ramparts and the looming towers of Menethil Keep, it serves as the Alliance's primary gateway across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, linking the Eastern Kingdoms with Theramore Isle and Auberdine. It is a bustling, rugged haven crowded with sailors, merchants, soldiers, and travelers.",al={"what is this town","menethil town","about menethil harbor"},it="place",add="0f75d9a0"},{q="What happened at Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor has long stood as the Alliance's fortified port on the Wetlands coast. In recent times the Dragonmaw clan has pushed into Dun Algaz, threatening to cut the harbor off from Loch Modan, while Dark Iron dwarves have seized Dun Modr to the north, leaving Captain Stoutfist's garrison on constant alert.",al={"history of menethil","menethil history","past of menethil harbor"},it="history",add="13315efd"},{q="Is Menethil Harbor dangerous?",a="Inside the gates, the town is protected by sturdy ramparts, dwarven guards, and the cannons of Menethil Keep. Beyond its walls, however, the Wetlands are treacherous. Dragonmaw orcs scheme in the hills, raptors prowl the marshlands, and smugglers and brawling sailors frequent the local tavern. While safe for honest travelers to rest and trade, caution is wise whenever you step near the marsh or dockside shadows.",al={"is menethil safe","danger in menethil harbor","menethil threats"},it="danger",add="f08a7377"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For an Alliance traveler heading west, Menethil Harbor is a vital staging ground and the sole maritime bridge linking the Eastern Kingdoms to Theramore.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see your people's stonework throughout this port, though it bears a human king's name. Dwarves man the Ironforge guards who hold Khaz Modan's outer threshold."},kw={"auberdine","boat","deepwater","docks","ferry","harbor","menethil","stoutfist","theramore","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:deepwater-tavern","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:auberdine","npc:captain-stoutfist","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","subzone:dun-algaz"},src={"Menethil Harbor"}}
E["subzone:menethil-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Menethil Keep",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Keep commands the skyline above Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Four watchtowers guard the Alliance port, and Captain Stoutfist leads its militia from within the stone walls.",h="Menethil Keep commands the skyline above Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Bastion of the Harbor",b="Menethil Keep rises over Menethil Harbor’s wooden docks and the Wetlands marshes. Four stone watchtowers overlook the town and bay, watching for seaward raiders, renegades, and swamp beasts pushing into the area. Within the fortress, Captain Stoutfist directs the town militia and organizes patrols to defend the port and protect Alliance interests across the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Menethil Keep used for?",a="Menethil Keep houses the Menethil Harbor militia and the Alliance command post in the Wetlands. Captain Stoutfist leads the local garrison from its stone walls, directing the harbor’s defenses and organizing adventurers to face threats across the marsh.",al={"purpose of menethil keep","menethil keep role","what is this castle"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is in charge of Menethil Keep?",a="Captain Stoutfist commands Menethil Keep and the Menethil militia. He coordinates the harbor’s defense against Dark Iron dwarf raiders, marsh beasts, and pirates.",al={"who leads menethil keep","keep commander","captain stoutfist"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is the keep located?",a="Menethil Keep stands inside Menethil Harbor on the Wetlands’ western coast. Its four tall stone towers rise above the settlement.",al={"where is menethil keep","menethil keep location","how to find menethil keep"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Menethil Keep?",a="Menethil Keep is the stone stronghold dominating Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Its four tall towers rise high above the harbor town, watching over the docks and surrounding marshes like stern guardians. It serves as the primary military bastion and refuge for the Alliance garrison in the region.",al={"what is menethil keep","menethil keep info","about menethil keep"},it="place",add="12a246c3"},{q="Is Menethil Keep dangerous?",a="Within its walls, Menethil Keep is completely safe for members of the Alliance, garrisoned by Captain Stoutfist and the local militia. The true dangers lie just outside in the foggy bogs of the Wetlands, where murlocs, Dark Iron dwarves, and ferocious beasts threaten travelers.",al={"is menethil keep safe","menethil keep danger","threats at menethil keep"},it="danger",add="6cd22f9e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler arriving by ship from Kalimdor or heading north toward Ironforge and Arathi, you can look to Menethil Keep for the military protection of this vital transport hub."},kw={"captain stoutfist","menethil harbor","menethil keep","militia","towers","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","npc:captain-stoutfist","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},src={"Menethil Keep"}}
E["subzone:mosshide-fen"] = {t="subzone",n="Mosshide Fen",z="wetlands",s="In eastern Wetlands, Mosshide Fen is held by the Mosshide gnolls. Its primitive camps lie far from the main trade roads, where travelers face danger.",h="In eastern Wetlands, Mosshide Fen is held by the Mosshide gnolls.",sec={{t="Territory of the Pack",b="Mosshide gnolls hold the tangled marsh of eastern Wetlands. Rough lean-tos and bone-strewn camps mark their territory. Gnawbone and other pack leaders command the tribe, which ambushes and devours travelers, scouts, and prospectors who enter its hunting grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mosshide Fen?",a="Mosshide Fen lies in eastern Wetlands, where sodden marshland is claimed and settled by the Mosshide gnolls.",al={"mosshide fen lore","what is this place","mosshide swamp"},it="place"},{q="Who rules Mosshide Fen?",a="The Mosshide gnolls occupy the fen under brutal leaders such as Gnawbone, who commands his pack to capture and devour outsiders trespassing on their land.",al={"who leads the gnolls here","gnawbone","mosshide leader"},it="residents"},{q="Why is this area dangerous to travelers?",a="Mosshide gnolls are aggressive and hungry. Travelers who leave established paths or search the wet brush for supplies risk sudden ambush by hunting packs.",al={"why is it dangerous","fen dangers"},it="danger"},{q="Why is it called Mosshide Fen?",a="The marshland takes its name from the Mosshide gnolls who have overrun the eastern Wetlands. These feral beasts have claimed the sodden bogs as their personal hunting territory, setting up clustered camps and aggressively preying upon anyone foolish enough to stray into their domain.",al={"mosshide fen name origin","why mosshide fen","how did mosshide fen get its name"},it="name",add="f76be1cd"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you must keep watch on Mosshide Fen. Its aggressive gnoll packs threaten prospectors searching the marshes and scouts securing the eastern paths."},kw={"gnawbone","gnolls","marshlands","mosshide","mosshide fen","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:gnoll","subzone:marshlands"},src={"Mosshide Fen"}}
E["subzone:raptor-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Raptor Ridge",z="wetlands",s="Raptor Ridge rises above the eastern Wetlands, northwest of the Dragonmaw Gates. Razormaw raptors hunt and nest among its crags, with a vicious matriarch deep in the caverns.",h="Raptor Ridge rises above the eastern Wetlands, northwest of the Dragonmaw Gates.",sec={{t="A Den of Predators",b="Razormaw raptors hunt in packs across Raptor Ridge, where rocky trails climb above the eastern Wetlands. Travelers near the foothills of Khaz Modan risk meeting these predators. In a cavern at the ridge's heart, the Razormaw Matriarch guards her brood and nests from intruders. The Dragonmaw Gates lie close by.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Raptor Ridge located?",a="Raptor Ridge rises in the far eastern Wetlands, directly northwest of the Dragonmaw Gates on the road toward Grim Batol.",al={"raptor ridge location","where is raptor ridge","how to get to raptor ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures live here?",a="Razormaw raptors roam the ridge. Deep in its cavern, the Razormaw Matriarch guards her nests and hatchlings.",al={"what mobs are at raptor ridge","raptors in wetlands","raptor ridge beasts"},it="residents"},{q="Who is the Razormaw Matriarch?",a="The Razormaw Matriarch leads the local raptor packs and broods over her clutch in the ridge's central cave.",al={"razormaw matriarch","raptor matriarch wetlands","raptor boss wetlands"},it="leader"},{q="Why is the area so dangerous to traverse?",a="Dense packs of aggressive, fast-moving raptors swarm trespassers. The ridge also lies in the shadow of hostile Dragonmaw orc territory near the mountain passes.",al={"is raptor ridge dangerous","raptor ridge threat"},it="danger"},{q="What is Raptor Ridge?",a="Raptor Ridge is a rugged highland area in the eastern Wetlands, situated just northwest of the Dragonmaw Gates. It serves as the primary nesting ground and lair for the region's vicious razormaw raptors, who hunt the surrounding marshes and fiercely defend their territory.",al={"what is raptor ridge","raptor ridge overview","tell me about raptor ridge"},it="place",add="26f8859b"},{q="Why is it called Raptor Ridge?",a="The ridge earns its straightforward name from the dense population of predatory raptors that have claimed the heights. Large packs of razormaw raptors prowl its slopes, nesting throughout the crags and inside its cavernous dens.",al={"why is it called raptor ridge","raptor ridge name origin","how did raptor ridge get its name"},it="name",add="fcab0786"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can seek a swift, tenacious marshland companion among the fierce Razormaw raptors of the ridge."},kw={"dragonmaw gates","raptor ridge","razormaw","razormaw matriarch","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:dragonmaw-gates","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:menethil-harbor"},src={"Raptor Ridge"}}
E["subzone:saltspray-glen"] = {t="subzone",n="Saltspray Glen",z="wetlands",s="Along Baradin Bay, salty spray sweeps across Saltspray Glen, where wild raptors roam the lowland. The glen lies between murloc waters and ancient dwarven ruins.",h="Along Baradin Bay, salty spray sweeps across Saltspray Glen, where wild raptors roam the lowland.",sec={{t="Brine and Claws",b="In the Wetlands' far northwest, salty spray blows inland across Saltspray Glen from Baradin Bay. Bluegill Marsh and its murloc-haunted waters lie to the south, while the quiet bluffs of Ironbeard's Tomb rise to the east. Cunning wild raptors nest through the marshy grass and hunt across the brackish flats. Their kin range nearby at Raptor Ridge and Black Channel Marsh, leaving little comfort for travelers passing through.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Saltspray Glen?",a="Saltspray Glen lies along the open coast of Baradin Bay. Fierce winds from the north and west drive seawater inland across the low ground as a dense, salty mist.",al={"saltspray glen name meaning","why saltspray","origin of name"},it="name"},{q="What creatures live in Saltspray Glen?",a="Aggressive wild raptors overrun the glen, nesting in its coastal brush and marshy hollows. They readily ambush anyone who wanders off the beaten path.",al={"monsters in saltspray glen","saltspray raptors","what is here"},it="danger"},{q="Where does Saltspray Glen lead?",a="Saltspray Glen lies in the Wetlands' northwestern reaches. Baradin Bay borders it to the north and west, Bluegill Marsh and its murlocs lie to the south, and the rocky rise of Ironbeard's Tomb stands to the east.",al={"saltspray glen location","where is saltspray glen","borders"},gp=true},{q="What is Saltspray Glen?",a="Saltspray Glen is a coastal valley nestled in the northwestern reaches of the Wetlands. Bordered by the waters of Baradin Bay to the north and west, it sits tucked between Bluegill Marsh to the south and the ancient resting place of Ironbeard's Tomb to the east. Constantly exposed to salty ocean breezes, the sodden glen serves primarily as a breeding and nesting ground for the region's fierce raptor population.",al={"what is saltspray glen","saltspray glen wetlands","where is saltspray glen"},it="place",add="4c44c0ba"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find vicious raptors prowling the glen's damp sea grass. They make hearty quarry and dependable, fierce beasts for trackers stalking the coast."},kw={"baradin bay","bluegill marsh","ironbeard's tomb","raptors","saltspray glen","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:baradin-bay","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","subzone:bluegill-marsh","subzone:raptor-ridge","subzone:black-channel-marsh","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site"},src={"Saltspray Glen"}}
E["subzone:sundown-marsh"] = {t="subzone",n="Sundown Marsh",z="wetlands",s="In the Wetlands' far west, Sundown Marsh holds deep water, stagnant pools, and dangerous wildlife. An eccentric pair keeps a solitary home along its muddy borders.",h="In the Wetlands' far west, Sundown Marsh holds deep water, stagnant pools, and dangerous wildlife.",sec={{t="A Wild and Murky Sinkhole",b="Sundown Marsh fills the Wetlands' deepest, westernmost reaches, where deep water and thick mud hide a dense population of predators. Giant crocolisks, shifting oozes, roaming raptors, and territorial Mosshide gnolls move through the mist. Most travelers keep to the main cobblestone road between Menethil Harbor and Ironforge, leaving this corner largely untamed.",sp=0},{t="Life at the Edge of the Mire",b="A lonely stone cottage with a churning windmill stands amid the marsh's hazards. The gnome Fradd Swiftgear and the dwarf Wenna Silkbeard make their living scavenging the bog. They sell curiosities and rare trade recipes recovered from the mire to travelers who brave its aggressive denizens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Sundown Marsh located?",a="Sundown Marsh lies in the Wetlands' deepest, westernmost reaches, in the northwest and away from the main royal roads.",al={"sundown marsh location","where is sundown marsh","wetlands marsh location"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in Sundown Marsh?",a="The gnome Fradd Swiftgear and the dwarf Wenna Silkbeard live in a small stone dwelling with a windmill. They make their living scavenging the bog and sell oddities and rare goods to passing travelers.",al={"who lives here","sundown marsh npcs","swiftgear cottage"},it="residents"},{q="What threats can be found in Sundown Marsh?",a="Giant crocolisks, foul oozes, bog beasts, raptors, and hostile Mosshide gnolls threaten travelers. These dangers discourage casual exploration.",al={"monsters in sundown marsh","sundown marsh dangers","enemies sundown marsh"},it="threat"},{q="Why would an adventurer travel into Sundown Marsh?",a="Travelers visit the windmill cottage to trade with Fradd Swiftgear and Wenna Silkbeard, who offer rare recipes and peculiar curiosities scavenged from the surrounding swamp.",al={"why visit sundown marsh","reasons to go to sundown marsh","sundown marsh vendors"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Sundown Marsh?",a="Sundown Marsh marks the deep, northwestern swamplands of the Wetlands. Dominated by murky waters and thick vegetation, this isolated stretch of bog surrounds a lonely stone windmill home where a couple of intrepid traders manage to carve out a living despite the surrounding hazards.",al={"what is sundown marsh","about sundown marsh","sundown marsh wetlands"},it="place",add="a91ad050"},{q="Is Sundown Marsh dangerous?",a="Sundown Marsh is treacherous for any traveler not prepared for the wild. Aggressive crocolisks lurk in the waters, raptors and roving gnolls prowl the mudbanks, and dangerous oozes and bog beasts wander the mire, making any journey off the beaten path perilous.",al={"how dangerous is sundown marsh","sundown marsh threats","is sundown marsh safe"},it="danger",add="d0103c3e"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Fradd Swiftgear and Wenna Silkbeard make a home with their windmill outpost in dangerous mud. Their ingenuity shows how gnomes can make a comfortable home anywhere."},kw={"crocolisks","fradd swiftgear","mosshide","oozes","sundown marsh","wenna silkbeard","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:gnoll"},src={"Sundown Marsh"}}
E["subzone:thelgen-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Thelgen Rock",z="wetlands",s="In the southern mountain wall of the Wetlands, Thelgen Rock’s caverns hold volatile Incendicite Ore. Venomous spiders infest the passages.",h="In the southern mountain wall of the Wetlands, Thelgen Rock’s caverns hold volatile Incendicite Ore.",sec={{t="A Web-Choked Cavern",b="Thelgen Rock cuts deep into the mountains between the Wetlands and Loch Modan. Aggressive spiders fill its web-choked passages, and their venom makes every step dangerous. Miners and adventurers still brave the tunnels for the valuable Incendicite Ore embedded in the rock.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes Thelgen Rock dangerous?",a="Large, poisonous spiders crowd Thelgen Rock’s caverns. Their webs fill the winding tunnels, where travelers can be cornered and overwhelmed by venomous bites.",al={"thelgen rock dangers","why is thelgen rock dangerous","spiders in thelgen rock"},it="threat"},{q="Why do prospectors and miners come here?",a="The caves hold rich seams of fiery, volatile Incendicite Ore, sought by dwarven prospectors and engineers. Despite the spiders, miners enter to gather samples from the cave walls.",al={"why visit thelgen rock","ore in thelgen rock","incendicite ore"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Thelgen Rock located?",a="Thelgen Rock lies along the Wetlands’ southern mountain ridge, south of the main road between Menethil Harbor and the Dun Algaz mountain pass.",al={"thelgen rock location","where is thelgen rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Thelgen Rock?",a="Thelgen Rock is an extensive cavern system carved deep into the southern mountains of the Wetlands. It is widely known among miners for its rich deposits of Incendicite Ore, though harvesting anything here requires braving the venomous swarms of spiders that have claimed every shadow and tunnel inside.",al={"thelgen rock what is it","what is this place thelgen rock","thelgen rock cave"},it="place",add="10e18c06"},{q="Is Thelgen Rock dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely hazardous. The caves are infested with aggressive, poisonous spiders that make any prospecting expedition a lethal undertaking. Explorers and miners seeking the rare mineral veins within must constantly watch the dark caverns to avoid being overwhelmed by venom and webbing.",al={"how dangerous is thelgen rock","thelgen rock danger","is thelgen rock safe"},it="danger",add="ba9bab1c"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Rare Incendicite Ore deposits lie deep within Thelgen Rock, drawing prospectors beneath the mountain despite the danger."},kw={"cave","incendicite ore","spider cave","spiders","thelgen rock","wetlands"},rel={"quest:466","zone:wetlands"},src={"Thelgen Rock"}}
E["subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Whelgar's Excavation Site",z="wetlands",s="Dwarven prospectors are trapped above Whelgar's Excavation Site, cut off from their findings. The dig sought ancient Titan relics, prehistoric secrets, and fossils, but mottled raptors overran the quarry.",h="Dwarven prospectors are trapped above Whelgar's Excavation Site, cut off from their findings.",sec={{t="A Ruined Expedition",b="Between Menethil Harbor and Dun Modr, dwarven prospectors dug for ancient fossils and earthen mysteries. Their search for prehistoric remnants stirred the native mottled raptors. Overwhelmed and under-equipped, the archaeologists fled to a ridge overlooking the site. Their tents, tools, and unearthed relics remain scattered among the prowling predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was the excavation site abandoned?",a="The dwarven excavators disturbed the territory of aggressive mottled raptors. Overwhelmed by the ferocious creatures, the surviving crew took refuge on a ridge overlooking the dig site.",al={"why is it abandoned","what happened to the digsite","why leave the dig"},it="ruin"},{q="What were the dwarves looking for here?",a="The dwarves sought prehistoric fossils and subterranean artifacts, hoping to uncover ancient clues about their Titan heritage and the world's distant past.",al={"what are they digging for","purpose of the excavation","whelgar digsite goal"},it="purpose"},{q="What threats roam the digsite now?",a="Mottled raptors swarm the quarry floor and surrounding ridges, including the feared Sarltooth.",al={"what is in the excavation site","digsite mobs","raptors in wetlands"},it="danger"},{q="Where did the surviving excavators go?",a="The surviving crew, including Prospector Whelgar, are trapped atop a ridge overlooking the dig site. They seek brave adventurers to recover their lost research.",al={"where is whelgar","where are the dwarves","digsite survivors location"},it="people"},{q="What is Whelgar's Excavation Site?",a="Whelgar's Excavation Site is a dwarven archaeological dig nestled in the foothills of the Wetlands, east of Menethil Harbor. Established by dwarven explorers seeking ancient relics and fossils, the site has unfortunately fallen on hard times after aggressive native predators drove the workers out of their own trenches.",al={"whelgars excavation site","whelgar digsite","what is whelgars dig site"},it="place",add="4eb1142c"},{q="What happened at Whelgar's Excavation Site?",a="What began as a promising dwarven archaeological endeavor took a disastrous turn when the digging stirred up the local wildlife. Vicious mottled raptors surged into the quarry and overwhelmed the camp, forcing the surviving excavators to abandon their tools, relics, and ongoing research to flee to safer ground.",al={"history of whelgars excavation site","whelgars excavation site history","what happened at the dig site"},it="history",add="65697e7b"},{q="Why is it called Whelgar's Excavation Site?",a="The digsite bears the name of Prospector Whelgar, the dwarf leading the expedition. He and the surviving crew have taken refuge on a ridge overlooking the raptor-infested quarry.",al={"who is whelgar","whelgar name origin","why whelgar digsite"},it="name",add="23dbaaa4"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing a dig abandoned to feral beasts is an insult to the Explorers' League. Reclaiming Whelgar's research means defending your heritage and recovering stolen Titan secrets.",["profession:Mining"]="The quarry's exposed walls and unearthed bedrock offer prime veins for miners daring enough to work beneath hungry raptors' snarls."},kw={"digsite","excavation","fossils","raptors","sarltooth","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Whelgar's Excavation Site"}}
E["zone:wetlands"] = {t="zone",n="Wetlands",z="wetlands",s="Fog and fighting shape life in the Wetlands, between Khaz Modan and Baradin Bay. Dwarven wars and orc invasions scarred the marsh, a rugged buffer between Ironforge and Lordaeron. Menethil Harbor keeps the Alliance connected to distant shores, amid Dragonmaw orcs, murlocs, and gnolls.",h="Fog and fighting shape life in the Wetlands, between Khaz Modan and Baradin Bay.",sec={{t="A Land of Water and Ruin",b="Below the Stonewrought Dam, cold marshland lies under gray skies and heavy fog. Once home to thriving dwarven settlements, the Wetlands now hold sunken stone ruins, sodden bogs, and treacherous mires. You can enter by the narrow pass at Dun Algaz, coming north from Loch Modan, or cross the arches of the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="The Scars of Grim Batol",b="Grim Batol looms over the eastern swamp, its halls once held by the Wildhammer dwarves. Defiled during the War of the Three Hammers, the stronghold became a redoubt for the Dragonmaw clan during the Second War. When the red dragonflight broke free of orcish captivity, its fiery vengeance shattered the orcish forces and laid waste to the slopes. Red wyrmkin guard the Dragonmaw Gates, while feral Dragonmaw survivors live in scattered hill camps and harass travelers across the swamp.",sp=0},{t="Port of the West Coast",b="Menethil Harbor occupies the rim of Baradin Bay, carrying Alliance trade and supplies through Khaz Modan. The port honors King Terenas Menethil II and links the Eastern Kingdoms with Kalimdor. Ships sail to Theramore Isle and, by way of Southshore, to Auberdine. Dwarven-built defenses protect the harbor, but coastal murlocs, swamp creatures, and raiders threaten vessels in the rocky channels.",sp=0},{t="Besieged Frontiers",b="War reaches the Wetlands from several directions. In the north, Dark Iron dwarves led by the warlock Balgaras the Foul sabotaged the Thandol Span and seized Dun Modr, cutting off overland supply trains. Mosshide gnolls roam the central fens and threaten even Rethiel the Greenwarden, an ancient protector. Rogue orc warbands, Dark Iron infiltrators, and cursed shipwrecks keep the swamp dangerous, and its defenders must stay alert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I travel to the Wetlands on foot?",a="From Loch Modan, take the mountain pass through Dun Algaz north into the Wetlands. Travelers coming from the north can cross the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands. Hostile Dragonmaw orcs and Dark Iron dwarves contest both routes.",al={"how to get to wetlands","path to wetlands","run to wetlands"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where do the boats at Menethil Harbor go?",a="One ship sails south to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh. The other calls at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, then crosses the Great Sea to Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore.",al={"menethil boats","menethil harbor ships","where does the boat go in wetlands"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Grim Batol and why is it guarded?",a="Grim Batol is an ancient dwarven fortress abandoned after the War of the Three Hammers and later occupied by the Dragonmaw clan. After the Second War, the freed red dragonflight drove out the orcs and sealed the mountain. Red dragonspawn and wyrmkin patrol the Dragonmaw Gates to keep intruders from the cursed halls.",al={"why are there dragons at grim batol","grim batol red dragons","dragonmaw gates"},it="place"},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr, a northern dwarven stronghold guarding the Thandol Span, was recently overrun by Dark Iron dwarves led by Balgaras the Foul. Survivors under Rhag Garmason hold an embattled camp nearby and fight to reclaim the town.",al={"who destroyed dun modr","dun modr ruins","dark irons in dun modr"},it="history"},{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is an ancient bog beast who lives in the Wetlands' Green Belt. He seeks travelers' help against aggressive Mosshide gnolls and diseased Fen Creepers so the marsh can recover.",al={"green belt","rethiel wetlands","who is the greenwarden"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q463.2"}},{q="Where did all the orcs in the swamp come from?",a="The swamp's orcs belong to the Dragonmaw clan, which fortified Grim Batol during the Second War. After the freed red dragonflight devastated them, survivors fled into the swamp and hills, where they still raid roads and travelers.",al={"why are there orcs in wetlands","wetlands dragonmaw","dragonmaw clan wetlands"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Wetlands?",a="The Wetlands is a cold, sprawling marshland nestled between the mountains of Khaz Modan and the western sea. Shrouded in perpetual gray mists, it lies immediately north of Loch Modan and south of the Arathi Highlands. Once home to numerous dwarven settlements, the region has been ravaged by past wars and now sits as a rugged, untamed wilderness dividing the dwarven kingdoms from the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"what is wetlands","wetlands lore","tell me about wetlands"},it="place",add="2cd88152",nx={8,9}},{q="Why is it all swamp here?",a="The Wetlands sits in a low basin bordered on three sides by towering mountain ranges, catching run-off and drainage from the heights above. It is fed by countless rivers, ponds, and streams running down toward Baradin Bay, keeping the earth perpetually saturated and cold.",al={"why is wetlands a swamp","wetlands geography","why so much water wetlands"},it="origin",add="4984d286"},{q="Who lives in the Wetlands?",a="The primary civilized presence is the Alliance at Menethil Harbor, alongside dwarven mountaineers struggling to hold key outposts. However, the wilderness is dominated by hostile forces: renegade Dragonmaw orcs hiding in the eastern foothills, Mosshide gnolls prowling the fens, murlocs crawling along the coasts, and violent Dark Iron dwarves pushing south from Dun Modr.",al={"who lives here","wetlands factions","inhabitants of wetlands"},it="residents",add="60c5b961"},{q="What is Menethil Harbor and who runs it?",a="Menethil Harbor is a heavily fortified port city built on an island in Baradin Bay, serving as the Alliance's primary coastal gateway in Khaz Modan. Named in honor of King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron, it is maintained by dwarves and allied humans, protected by the stout stone walls of Menethil Keep and guarded by Captain Stoutfist's garrison.",al={"menethil harbor","who runs menethil","menethil town"},it="place",add="8d21dccb",nx={11,12}},{q="Why did the dwarves build a port here?",a="During the Second War, Orgrim Doomhammer constructed a shipyard here to ferry the Horde across Baradin Bay to Lordaeron. After driving the orcs out, the Alliance reclaimed the location and rebuilt it into a thriving harbor, establishing essential maritime supply routes connecting Khaz Modan to both human allies and distant lands across the sea.",al={"why menethil harbor","why build a port in the swamp","reason for menethil harbor"},it="purpose",add="fd9bb568"},{q="Is Menethil Harbor Alliance territory?",a="Yes. Menethil Harbor stands as an official Alliance stronghold. Though it is a rough, bustling harbor town filled with sailors, merchants, travelers, and rough dockworkers, it flies the Alliance banner and is defended by Ironforge forces.",al={"is menethil alliance","menethil harbor faction","who owns menethil harbor"},it="side",add="4cff40a7"},{q="Who's in charge around here?",a="There is no single ruler over the untamed marshland. Alliance authority is concentrated at Menethil Harbor under Captain Stoutfist and the garrison within Menethil Keep. Outside the harbor walls, the swamp is a lawless frontier contested by military patrols, orcish warlords, and primal beasts.",al={"who leads wetlands","wetlands commander","who is the boss here"},it="in_charge",add="6dc9c02b",nx={14}},{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist?",a="Captain Stoutfist is the dwarven commander in charge of the garrison at Menethil Harbor. From the safety of the harbor, he coordinates defensive operations across the swamp, tasking capable adventurers with curbing the relentless raids of the nearby Dragonmaw orcs.",al={"captain stoutfist wetlands","stoutfist lore","who is stoutfist"},it="identity",add="b8a9f96f"},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs and why are they here?",a="The Dragonmaw are a brutal orc clan that used the Demon Soul to enslave Alexstrasza and the red dragonflight during the Second War, ruling from the heights of Grim Batol. When the Dragonqueen was freed, the vengeful dragons shattered the clan, scattering the survivors into the swamps and mountains of the Wetlands, where they remain a violent, lingering threat.",al={"dragonmaw wetlands","why are dragonmaw in wetlands","dragonmaw orcs"},it="threat",add="38351a9f"},{q="Who are the Dark Iron dwarves and why are they attacking Dun Modr?",a="The Dark Irons are a treacherous, shadow-wielding dwarven clan long exiled from Ironforge. Taking advantage of Alliance forces being deployed abroad, they struck north, seizing the town of Dun Modr and sabotaging the Thandol Span to sever vital communications and reclaim territory in Khaz Modan.",al={"dark iron dun modr","why dark irons in wetlands","dark iron attack wetlands"},it="threat",add="ecc875bb"},{q="What is the Thandol Span and why does it matter?",a="The Thandol Span is a magnificent pair of massive dwarven stone bridges spanning the chasm between northern Khaz Modan and the Arathi Highlands. Built after the War of the Three Hammers to facilitate trade and fellowship with the Wildhammers, it remains the sole overland link between the southern kingdoms and northern Lordaeron.",al={"thandol span","thandol bridge","why is thandol span important"},it="place",add="0f0d7fa8",nx={18}},{q="Why do the Dark Iron want to blow it up?",a="By destroying the Thandol Span, the Dark Irons aim to completely isolate Ironforge and Khaz Modan from Alliance allies in Lordaeron. Severing this overland lifeline prevents reinforcements from marching south to reclaim Dun Modr or aid against further Dark Iron incursions.",al={"why destroy thandol span","dark iron bridge plot","blow up thandol span"},it="motive",add="faff9f74"},{q="How did I end up in the Wetlands and where does this lead next?",a="Most travelers arrive by marching north through the mountain pass of Dun Algaz from Loch Modan, or by taking the long voyage into Menethil Harbor by boat. From here, the road continues north across the Thandol Span into the Arathi Highlands, while ships departing the docks carry adventurers west across the Great Sea.",al={"where to go from wetlands","wetlands next zone","wetlands path"},it="arrival",add="eabba297",nx={20}},{q="Is this the road to Ironforge?",a="Yes. Following the road south out of the swamp leads you straight into the narrow tunnels of Dun Algaz. Passing through the mountains brings you into Loch Modan, from which the main highway heads west through the North Gate Pass directly into the snows of Dun Morogh and Ironforge.",al={"road to ironforge wetlands","how to get to ironforge from wetlands","path to ironforge"},it="place",add="75fb0ece"},{q="How did I end up in the Wetlands?",a="Most Alliance travelers reach the Wetlands by heading north from Loch Modan, braving the narrow mountain tunnels of Dun Algaz to descend into the misty marshlands below. Others arrive by ship from across the Great Sea, sailing into Menethil Harbor from the shores of Kalimdor. Those venturing south from the Arathi Highlands must instead navigate the perilous crossings of the ruined Thandol Span.",al={"how did i get here","how did i arrive in wetlands","where did i come from"},it="arrival",add="78aee5e0"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in the Wetlands?",a="The marsh is a beleaguered frontier where the Alliance clings to a fragile foothold. From Menethil Harbor, you are called to safeguard essential trade routes and repel the lingering Dragonmaw orcs who raid the lowlands. Farther east and north, dwarven mountaineers require your steel to contain hostile gnoll packs, aid beleaguered excavation sites, and push back Dark Iron dwarves threatening to sever the Thandol Span entirely.",al={"what should i do here","why am i here","what is my mission in wetlands"},it="purpose",add="87ca94d2"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the Wetlands carries the loss of Dun Modr, the tragedy of Grim Batol, and the ongoing work of defending King Magni's northern trade route.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Menethil Harbor is the chief deep-water route across the Great Sea, linking the eastern kingdoms with outposts in Kalimdor.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find rich mineral veins in the hills and caverns of Thelgen Rock, including rare Incendicite ore sought by dwarven miners and engineers."},kw={"baradin bay","dragonmaw","dun algaz","dun modr","grim batol","menethil","menethil harbor","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-algaz","topic:dragonmaw-clan","npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:455"},m={levels="20-30"},src={"Wetlands (Classic)","Wetlands"}}
